helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3125864				0	he	Creating a New Library				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030400.xhp	0	help	par_id3152576				0	he	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Macros - Organize Macros - %PRODUCTNAME Basic\</emph\> and click \<emph\>Organizer\</emph\> or click the \<emph\>Select Module\</emph\> icon in the Basic IDE to open the \<emph\>Macro Organizer\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030400.xhp	0	help	par_id3153726				0	he	Click the \<emph\>Libraries\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030400.xhp	0	help	par_id3149664				0	he	Select to where you want to attach the library in the \<emph\>Location\</emph\> list. If you select %PRODUCTNAME Macros & Dialogs, the library will belong to the $[officename] application and will be available for all documents. If you select a document the library will be attached to this document and only available from there.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030400.xhp	0	help	par_id3153365				0	he	Click \<emph\>New\</emph\> and insert a name to create a new library.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147394				0	he	Appending a Library				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030400.xhp	0	help	par_id3153157				0	he	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Macros - Organize Macros - %PRODUCTNAME Basic\</emph\> and click \<emph\>Organizer\</emph\> or click the \<emph\>Select Module\</emph\> icon in the Basic IDE to open the \<emph\>Macro Organizer\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030400.xhp	0	help	par_id3146972				0	he	Click the \<emph\>Libraries\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030400.xhp	0	help	par_id3145640				0	he	Select to where you want to append the library in the \<emph\>Location\</emph\> list. If you select %PRODUCTNAME Macros & Dialogs, the library will belong to the $[officename] application and will be available for all documents. If you select a document the library will be appended to this document and only available from there.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030400.xhp	0	help	par_id3154253				0	he	Click \<emph\>Append\</emph\> and select an external library to append.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030400.xhp	0	help	par_id3154705				0	he	Select all libraries to be appended in the \<emph\>Append Libraries\</emph\> dialog. The dialog displays all libraries that are contained in the selected file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030400.xhp	0	help	par_id3163807				0	he	If you want to insert the library as a reference only check the \<emph\>Insert as reference (read-only)\</emph\> box. Read-only libraries are fully functional but cannot be modified in the Basic IDE.				20200411 15:09:53
