helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030102.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	DateValue Function [Runtime]				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030102.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156344				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>DateValue function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030102.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156344				0	he	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030102.xhp\" name=\"DateValue Function [Runtime]\"\>DateValue Function [Runtime]\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030102.xhp	0	help	par_id3150542				0	he	Returns a date value from a date string. The date string is a complete date in a single numeric value. You can also use this serial number to determine the difference between two dates.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030102.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148799				0	he	תחביר:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030102.xhp	0	help	par_id3154910				0	he	DateValue [(date)]				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030102.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150870				0	he	Return value:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030102.xhp	0	help	par_id3153194				0	he	Date				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030102.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153969				0	he	Parameters:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030102.xhp	0	help	par_id3153770				0	he	\<emph\>Date:\</emph\> String expression that contains the date that you want to calculate. The date can be specified in almost any format.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030102.xhp	0	help	par_id3153189				0	he	You can use this function to convert a date that occurs between December 1, 1582 and December 31, 9999 into a single integer value. You can then use this value to calculate the difference between two dates. If the date argument lies outside the acceptable range, $[officename] Basic returns an error message.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030102.xhp	0	help	par_id3146974				0	he	In contrast to the DateSerial function that passes years, months, and days as separate numeric values, the DateValue function passes the date using the format "month.[,]day.[,]year".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030102.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153142				0	he	Example:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030102.xhp	0	help	par_id3155412				0	he	Sub ExampleDateValue				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030102.xhp	0	help	par_id3153363				0	he	msgbox DateValue("12/02/1997")				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030102.xhp	0	help	par_id3149262				0	he	end sub				20200411 15:09:53
