helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120104.xhp	0	help	par_id3143228				0	he	Double				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156024				0	he	Parameters:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120104.xhp	0	help	par_id3154348				0	he	\<emph\>Text:\</emph\> String that represents a number.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120104.xhp	0	help	par_id3149670				0	he	Using the Val function, you can convert a string that represents numbers into numeric expressions. This is the inverse of the \<emph\>Str\</emph\> function. If only part of the string contains numbers, only the first appropriate characters of the string are converted. If the string does not contain any numbers, the \<emph\>Val\</emph\> function returns the value 0.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154365				0	he	Example:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120104.xhp	0	help	par_id3151177				0	he	Sub ExampleVal				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120104.xhp	0	help	par_id3159150				0	he	msgbox Val("123.123")				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120104.xhp	0	help	par_id3154126				0	he	msgbox Val("A123.123")				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120104.xhp	0	help	par_id3147229				0	he	end Sub				20200411 15:09:53
