helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020300.xhp	0	help	par_id631733				0	he	End Sub				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020300.xhp	0	help	par_id8234199				0	he	REM ***** Module2 *****				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020300.xhp	0	help	par_id6969512				0	he	'Option Explicit				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020300.xhp	0	help	par_id1196935				0	he	Sub demoBug				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020300.xhp	0	help	par_id1423993				0	he	CompatibilityMode( true )				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020300.xhp	0	help	par_id6308786				0	he	initMyText				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020300.xhp	0	help	par_id4104129				0	he	' Now returns empty string				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020300.xhp	0	help	par_id7906125				0	he	' (or rises error for Option Explicit)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020300.xhp	0	help	par_id8055970				0	he	print "Now in module2 : ", myText				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020300.xhp	0	help	par_id2806176				0	he	End Sub				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154368				0	he	Saving Variable Content after Exiting a SUB or FUNCTION				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3156288				0	he	DIM STATIC VarName As TYPENAME				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3154486				0	he	The variable retains its value until the next time the FUNCTION or SUB is entered. The declaration must exist inside a SUB or a FUNCTION.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155809				0	he	Specifying the Return Value Type of a FUNCTION				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3149404				0	he	As with variables, include a type-declaration character after the function name, or the type indicated by "As" and the corresponding key word at the end of the parameter list to define the type of the function's return value, for example:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3152899				0	he	Function WordCount(WordText as String) \<emph\>as Integer\</emph\>				20200411 15:09:53
