helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156344				0	he	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03020000.xhp\" name=\"File I/O Functions\"\>File I/O Functions\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153360				0	he	Use File I/O functions to create and manage user-defined (data) files.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150398				0	he	You can use these functions to support the creation of "relative" files, so that you can save and reload certain records by specifying their record number. File I/O functions can also help you manage your files by providing you with information such as file size, current path settings, or the creation date of a file or a directory.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Display Functions				20200411 15:09:53
