helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020302.xhp	0	help	par_id3154320				0	he	If the Loc function is used for an open random access file, it returns the number of the last record that was last read or written.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020302.xhp	0	help	par_id3151115				0	he	For a sequential file, the Loc function returns the position in a file divided by 128. For binary files, the position of the last read or written byte is returned.				20200411 15:09:53
