helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\02\11070000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Breakpoint				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\02\11070000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154863				0	he	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/02/11070000.xhp\" name=\"Breakpoint\"\>Breakpoint\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\02\11070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155364				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ToggleBreakPoint\"\>Inserts a breakpoint in the program line.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\02\11070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149346				0	he	The breakpoint is inserted at the cursor position. Use a breakpoint to interrupt a program just before an error occurs. You can then troubleshoot the program by running it in \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/02/11050000.xhp\" name=\"Single Step\"\>Single Step\</link\> mode until the error occurs. You can also use the \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/02/11080000.xhp\" name=\"Watch\"\>Watch\</link\> icon to check the content of the relevant variables.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\02\11070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156346				0	he	\<image id=\"img_id3152780\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_togglebreakpoint.png\" width=\"0.1665inch\" height=\"0.1665inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3152780\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
