helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\18010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148520				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:SelectObject\"\>Allows you to select objects in the current document.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\18010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149511				0	he	\<image id=\"img_id3159194\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_drawselect.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3159194\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\18010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147571				0	he	Selection				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\18010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155555				0	he	To select an object, click the object with the arrow. To select more than one object, drag a selection frame around the objects. To add an object to a selection, press Shift, and then click the object. \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>\</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"CALC\"\>\</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"CHART\"\>\</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"MATH\"\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>The objects selected together can then be defined as a \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05290000.xhp\" name=\"group\"\>group\</link\>, turning them into a single group object.\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\18010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3143267				0	he	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>\</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"CALC\"\>\</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"CHART\"\>\</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"MATH\"\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>You can edit individual elements of a group. You can also delete elements from a group with \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Shift\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+click.\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\18010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3166460				0	he	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>\</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"CALC\"\>\</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"CHART\"\>\</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"MATH\"\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>You can select single objects from a group by double-clicking, if you first disable the \<emph\>Double-click to edit Text\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Option\</emph\> Bar.\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Special Tips for Table Controls				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	bm_id3109850				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>table controls; properties\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>controls; properties of table controls\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>table controls;keyboard-only edit mode\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3109850				0	he	Special Tips for Table Controls				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3153539				0	he	You can define a table control to display the records as you like. In other words you can define data fields for displaying or editing data like in a database form.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3152372				0	he	The following fields are possible in a table control: text, date, time and currency field, numeric field, pattern field, check box and combo box. In the case of combined data/time fields, two columns are created automatically.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3159194				0	he	The number of selected lines, if any are selected, is in parentheses after the total number of records.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3155616				0	he	To insert columns into the table control, click in the column heads and bring up the context menu. The following commands are available:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150789				0	he	Insert Column				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3153750				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_INSERTCOL\"\>Calls a submenu to select a data field to adopt it in the table control.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3155552				0	he	Configure the table control using drag and drop: Open the data source browser and drag the desired fields out of the data source browser and on to the column heads of the table control. A pre-configured column is created.				20200411 15:09:53
