helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN10824				0	he	Moves the current form to the last record.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN1082A				0	he	Save record				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN1082F				0	he	Saves the current record, if necessary.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN10835				0	he	Undo data entry				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN1083A				0	he	Reverses the changes in the current record.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN10840				0	he	New record				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN10845				0	he	Moves the current form to the insert row.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN1084B				0	he	Delete record				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN10850				0	he	Deletes the current record.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN10856				0	he	Refresh form				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN1085B				0	he	Reloads the most recently saved version of the current form.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154638				0	he	Dropdown				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3152577	20			0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_DROPDOWN\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies whether the combo box should dropdown (Yes) or not (No).\</ahelp\>A control field with the dropdown property has an additional arrow button which opens the list of the existing form entries per mouse click. Under \<emph\>Line count\</emph\>, you can specify how many lines (or rows) should be displayed in the dropdown state. Combination fields can have the dropdown property.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3159198				0	he	Combo boxes that were inserted as columns in a table control are always dropdown as the default.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153140				0	he	Alignment / Graphics alignment				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3151281	12			0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_ALIGN\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies the alignment option for text or graphics that are used on a control.\</ahelp\>The alignment options are left-aligned, right-aligned, and centered. These options are available for the following elements:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN109DD				0	he	Title of Label fields				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN109E1				0	he	Content of text fields				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN109E5				0	he	Content of table fields in the columns of a table control				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN109E9				0	he	Graphics or text that are used in buttons				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN109EC				0	he	The \<emph\>Alignment\</emph\> option for buttons is called \<emph\>Graphics alignment\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153141				0	he	Vertical Alignment				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3151394				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_VERTICAL_ALIGN\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies the vertical alignment for text or graphics content which used on a control.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151073				0	he	AutoFill				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3152375	77			0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_AUTOCOMPLETE\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Assigns the AutoFill function to a combo box.\</ahelp\>The AutoFill function displays a list of previous entries after you start to type an entry.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154729				0	he	Label field				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3145801				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_CONTROLLABEL\"\>Specifies the source for the label of the control.\</ahelp\> The text of the label field will be used instead of the name of a database field. For example, in the \<emph\>Filter Navigator\</emph\>, \<emph\>Search\</emph\> dialog, and as a column name in the table view.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153223				0	he	To define one character of the label as a mnemonic, so that the user can access this control by pressing the character on the keyboard, insert a tilde (~) character in front of the character in the label.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154502				0	he	Only the text of a group frame can be used as the label field when using radio buttons. This text applies to all of the radio buttons of the same group.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148587				0	he	If you click on the \<emph\>...\</emph\> button next to the text field, you will see the \<emph\>Label Field Selection\</emph\> dialog. Select a label from the list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154512	220			0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"PCR_CHECKBOX_RID_DLG_SELECTLABELCONTROL_1\"\>Check the \<emph\>No assignment \</emph\>box to remove the link between a control and the assigned label field.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148834				0	he	Width				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148566	143			0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_WIDTH\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Sets the column width in the table control field.\</ahelp\>Sets the column width in the table control field in the units that are specified in the %PRODUCTNAME module options. If you want, you can enter a value followed by a valid measurement unit, for example, 2 cm.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id1877803				0	he	Repeat				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id9863277				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_REPEAT\"\>Specifies if the action of a control such as a spin button repeats when you click the control and hold the mouse button down.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id9827875				0	he	Delay				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id6092715				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_REPEAT_DELAY\"\>Specifies the delay in milliseconds between repeating events.\</ahelp\> A repeating event occurs when you click an arrow button or the background of a scrollbar, or one of the record navigation buttons of a Navigation Bar, and you keep the mouse button pressed for some time. You can enter a value followed by a valid time unit, for example, 2 s or 500 ms.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145164				0	he	Record marker				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3147257				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_RECORDMARKER\"\>Specifies whether the first column is displayed with row labels, in which the current record is marked by an arrow.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151019				0	he	Date format				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3152971	83			0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_DATEFORMAT\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Here, you can determine the format you want for the date readout.\</ahelp\>With date fields you can determine the format for the date readout.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3151356				0	he	\<variable id=\"hinweis\"\>All format fields (date, time, currency, numeric) are formatted automatically in the selected format as soon as you leave them regardless of how you entered the input.\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156054				0	he	Spin Button				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154360	88			0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_SPIN\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>The "Yes" option transforms the control field into a spin button, where corresponding arrow buttons are added.\</ahelp\>Numerical fields, currency fields, date and time fields can be introduced as spin buttons in the form.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159268				0	he	Tristate				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154254				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_TRISTATE\"\>Specifies whether a check box can also represent ZERO values of a linked database apart from the TRUE and FALSE values.\</ahelp\> This function is only available if the database accepts three states: TRUE, FALSE and ZERO.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3156712	183			0	he	The\<emph\> Tristate \</emph\>property is only defined for database forms, not for HTML forms.				20200411 15:09:53
