helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155081				0	he	For the literal mask "__.__.2000", for example, define the "NNLNNLLLLL" edit mask so that the user can only enter four digits when entering a date.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154818				0	he	Strict format				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148750				0	he	You can have a format check with control fields that accept formatted contents (date, time, and so on). \<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_STRICTFORMAT\"\>If the strict format function is activated (Yes), only the allowed characters are accepted.\</ahelp\> For example, in a date field, only numbers or date delimiters are accepted; all alphabet entries typed with your keyboard are ignored.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147167				0	he	Frame				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154991	61			0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_TARGET_FRAME\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies the target frame to display the document that is opened by the "Open document / web page" action.\</ahelp\>You can also specify the target frame to display a \<emph\>URL\</emph\> that you open when you click a button that has been assigned the Open document or web page action).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150521				0	he	If you click the field, you can select an option from the list that specifies into which frame the next document should be loaded. The following possibilities exist:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148814				0	he	Entry				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155500				0	he	Meaning				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149408				0	he	_blank				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3146770				0	he	The next document is created in a new empty frame.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149771				0	he	_parent				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3159143				0	he	The next document is created in a parent frame. If no parent exists, the document is created in the same frame.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3151374				0	he	_self				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148600				0	he	The next document is created in the same frame.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153067				0	he	_top				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149174				0	he	The next document is created in a top-level window, that is, in the highest frame of the hierarchy; if the current frame is already a top window, the document is created in the current frame.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3156172				0	he	The Frame property is relevant for HTML forms, but not for database forms.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146950				0	he	Graphics				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154344	115			0	he	An image button has a \<emph\>Graphics \</emph\>property. \<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_IMAGE_URL\"\>The\<emph\> Graphics\</emph\> property specifies the graphic's path and file name that you want to have displayed on the button.\</ahelp\> If you select the graphic file with the \<emph\>...\</emph\> button, the path and file name will be automatically included in the text box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150530				0	he	Help text				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3156310				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_HELPTEXT\"\>Provides the option of entering a help text that will be displayed as a tip on the control.\</ahelp\> The tip shows the text in user mode when the mouse is moved over the control.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153287				0	he	For URL type buttons, the help text appears as the extended tip instead of the URL address entered under URL.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145377				0	he	Help URL				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148649				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_HELPURL\"\>Specifies a batch label in URL spelling which refers to a help document and which can be called with the help of the control field.\</ahelp\> The help for the control field help can be opened if the focus is positioned on the control field and the user presses F1.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152541				0	he	Background color				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155073				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_BACKGROUNDCOLOR\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Sets the background color of the control field.\</ahelp\>A background color is available for most control fields. If you click on \<emph\>Background color\</emph\>, a list will open which enables you to select among various colors. The "Standard" option adopts the system setting. If the desired color is not listed, click the \<emph\>...\</emph\> button to define a color in the \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010501.xhp\" name=\"Color\"\>\<emph\>Color\</emph\>\</link\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148971				0	he	Scrollbar				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3144430				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_HSCROLL\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Adds the scrollbar type that you specify to a text box.\</ahelp\>Adds the scrollbar type that you specify to a text box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN1110B				0	he	Incr./decrement value				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN1110F				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Determines intervals to add or subtract with each activation of the spin button control.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146779				0	he	Value step				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155096	86			0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_VALUESTEP\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Determines spin button intervals.\</ahelp\>You can preset the value intervals for numerical and currency spin buttons. Use the up and down arrows of the spin button to increase or decrease the value.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145756				0	he	List entries				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3151300				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_STRINGITEMLIST\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Defines the list entries visible in the document. Open this list and type your text. Use Shift+Enter for a new line. With list and combo boxes, you can define the list entries that will be visible in the document. Open the \<emph\>List entries\</emph\> field and type your text.\</ahelp\> Please note the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170100.xhp\" name=\"tips\"\>tips\</link\> referring to the keyboard controls.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3152874				0	he	The predefined default list entry is entered into the \<emph\>Default selection combo\</emph\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154610				0	he	Note that the list entries entered here are only incorporated into the form if, on the \<emph\>Data\</emph\> tab under \<emph\>Type of list contents\</emph\>, the option "Valuelist" is selected.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154767				0	he	If you do not want the list entries to be written to the database or transmitted to the recipient of the Web form, but rather assigned values that are not visible in the form, you can assign the list entries to other values in a value list. The value list is determined on the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170102.xhp\" name=\"Data\"\>\<emph\>Data\</emph\>\</link\> tab. Under \<emph\>Type of List Contents\</emph\>, select the option "Value List". Then enter the values under \<emph\>List Contents\</emph\> that are to be assigned to the corresponding visible list entries of the form. For the correct assignment, the order in the value list is relevant.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150511				0	he	For HTML documents, a list entry entered on the \<emph\>General\</emph\> tab corresponds to the HTML tag <OPTION>; an entry of the value list entered on the \<emph\>Data\</emph\> tab under \<emph\>List content\</emph\> corresponds to the <OPTION VALUE=...> tag.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154290				0	he	Date max.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148637	122			0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_DATEMAX\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Determines a date which can not be exceeded by another value introduced by the user.\</ahelp\>Determines a date which can not be exceeded by another value introduced by the user.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149804				0	he	Max. text length				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150776	124			0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_MAXTEXTLEN\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Defines the maximum number of characters that the user can enter.\</ahelp\>For text and combo boxes, you can define the maximum number of characters that the user can enter. If this control field property is uncertain, the default setting will be zero.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153813				0	he	If the control is linked to a database and the text length is to be accepted from the field definition of the database, you must not enter the text length here. The settings are only accepted from the database if the control property was not defined ("Not Defined" state).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145599				0	he	Value max.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154733	126			0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_EFFECTIVEMAX\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Defines a value for the control field which can not be exceeded by another value introduced by the user.\</ahelp\>For numerical and currency fields, you can determine the maximum value that the user can enter.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154835				0	he	Time max.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155762	128			0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_TIMEMAX\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Determines a time which can not be exceeded by another value introduced by the user.\</ahelp\>Determines a time which can not be exceeded by another value introduced by the user.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150416				0	he	Multiselection				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3143275				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_MULTISELECTION\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Allows you to select more than one item in a list box.\</ahelp\>Allows you to select more than one item in a list box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	bm_id4040955				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>rich text control\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>controls;rich text control\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148527				0	he	Text type				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153724				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"37933\"\>Allows you to use line breaks and formatting in a control field, such as a text box or label. To manually enter a line break, press the Enter key. Select "Multi-line with formatting" to enter formatted text.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN113D2				0	he	If you select the text type "Multi-line with formatting", you cannot bind this control to a database field.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN11391				0	he	This control is named "Multiline input" for a text column inside a table control.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN114EF				0	he	Word break				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN11505				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Displays text on more than one line.\</ahelp\> Allows you to use line breaks in a text box, so that you can enter more than one line of text. To manually enter a line break, press the Enter key.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN11538				0	he	Toggle				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN1154E				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Specifies if a Push Button behaves as a Toggle Button. If you set Toggle to "Yes", you can switch between the "selected" and "not selected" control states when you click the button or press the spacebar while the the control has the focus. A button in the "selected" state appears "pressed in".\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN11558				0	he	Take Focus on Click				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN1156E				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>If you set this option to "Yes", the Push Button receives the focus when you click the button.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN11578				0	he	Hide selection				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN1158E				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"37965\"\>Specifies whether a text selection on a control remains selected when a the focus is no longer on a control.\</ahelp\> If you set \<emph\>Hide selection\</emph\> to "No", the selected text remains selected when the focus is no longer on the control that contains the text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN11598				0	he	Style				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN115AE				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"37966\"\>Specifies whether Check boxes and Option buttons are displayed in a 3D look (default) or a flat look.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN115B8				0	he	Border color				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN115CE				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"37967\"\>Specifies the border color for controls that have the Border property set to "flat".\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN115B7				0	he	Symbol color				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN115BB				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Specifies the color for symbols on controls, for example the arrows on a scrollbar.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149314				0	he	Date min.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155755	132			0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_DATEMIN\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Determines the earliest date that a user can enter.\</ahelp\>Determines the earliest date that a user can enter.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152866				0	he	Value min.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3147505	134			0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_EFFECTIVEMIN\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>You can determine here a value for the control field to prevent the user from entering a smaller value.\</ahelp\>For numerical and currency fields you can determine a minimum value to prevent the user from entering a smaller value.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153298				0	he	Time min.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148831	136			0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_TIMEMIN\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Determines the minimum time that a user can enter.\</ahelp\>Determines the minimum time that a user can enter.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155746				0	he	Decimal accuracy				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3146096	138			0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_DECIMAL_ACCURACY\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Determines the number of digits displayed to the right of the decimal point.\</ahelp\>With numerical and currency fields you can determine the number of digits displayed to the right of the decimal point.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151340				0	he	Name				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149819	10			0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_NAME\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>On the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> tab page, this option specifies the name for the control field. On the \<emph\>Form Properties \</emph\>tab page, this option specifies the name for the form.\</ahelp\>Each control field and each form has a \<emph\>Name \</emph\>property through which it can be identified. The name will appear in the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170600.xhp\" name=\"Form Navigator\"\>Form Navigator\</link\> and, using the name, the control field can be referred to from a macro. The default settings already specify a name which is constructed from using the field's label and number.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153025				0	he	If you work with macros, make sure that the names of the controls are unique.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146325				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>controls; grouping\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>grouping; controls\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>forms; grouping controls\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3146325				0	he	The name is also used to group different controls that belong together functionally, such as radio buttons. To do so, give the same name to all members of the group: controls with identical names form a group. Grouped controls can be represented visually by using a \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170000.xhp\" name=\"Group Box\"\>Group Box\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149720				0	he	Navigation bar				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149918	198			0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_NAVIGATIONBAR\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies whether to display the navigation bar on the lower border of the table control.\</ahelp\>Specifies whether to display the navigation bar on the lower border of table controls.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158426				0	he	Read-only				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153215	43			0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_READONLY\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Determines if the control is read-only (Yes) or if it can be edited (No).\</ahelp\>The\<emph\> Read-only \</emph\>property can be assigned to all controls in which the user can enter text. If you assign the read-only property to an image field which uses graphics from a database, the user will not be able to insert new graphics into the database.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148912				0	he	Border				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3145637	140			0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_BORDER\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Determines if the field's border should be displayed "Without frame", with a "3-D look" or "Flat".\</ahelp\>With control fields that have a frame, you can determine the border display on the form using the \<emph\>Border \</emph\>property. You can select among the "Without frame", "3-D look" or "Flat" options.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149266				0	he	Tab order				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3147483				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_TABINDEX\"\>The \<emph\>Tab order\</emph\> property determines the order in which the controls are focused in the form when you press the Tab key.\</ahelp\> In a form that contains more than one control, the focus moves to the next control when you press the Tab key. You can specify the order in which the focus changes with an index under \<emph\>Tab order\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3156207				0	he	The \<emph\>Tab order\</emph\> property is not available to \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170600.xhp\" name=\"Hidden Controls\"\>Hidden Controls\</link\>. If you want, you can also set this property for image buttons and image controls, so that you can select these controls with the Tab key.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150378				0	he	When creating a form, an index is automatically assigned to the control fields that are added to this form; every control field added is assigned an index increased by 1. If you change the index of a control, the indices of the other controls are updated automatically. Elements that cannot be focused (Tabstop = No) are also assigned a value. However, these controls are skipped when using the Tab key.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150640				0	he	You can also easily define the indices of the different controls in the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170300.xhp\" name=\"Tab Order\"\>\<emph\>Tab Order\</emph\>\</link\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id0509200912114423				0	he	Mouse wheel scroll				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id0509200912114566				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Sets whether the value changes when the user scrolls a mouse wheel. Never: No change of the value. When focused: (default) The value changes when the control has the focus and the wheel is pointing at the control and gets scrolled. Always: The value changes when the wheel is pointing at the control and gets scrolled, no matter which control has the focus.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154049				0	he	Default status				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150837				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_DEFAULT_CHECKED\"\>Specifies whether an option or a check box is selected by default.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149242				0	he	For a reset type button, you can define the status of the control if the reset button is activated by the user.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3156266				0	he	For grouped option fields, the status of the group corresponding to the default setting is defined by the \<emph\>Default Status\</emph\> property.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156150				0	he	Default selection				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148730	37			0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_DEFAULT_SELECT_SEQ\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies the list box entry to mark as the default entry.\</ahelp\>Specifies the list box entry to mark as the default entry.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150028	203			0	he	For a Reset type button, the\<emph\> Default selection\</emph\> entry defines the status of the list box if the reset button is activated by the user.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id919217				0	he	For a List box that contains a value list, you can click the \<emph\>...\</emph\> button to open the \<emph\>Default selection\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id50050				0	he	In the \<emph\>Default selection\</emph\> dialog, select the entries that you want to mark as selected when you open the form that contains the list box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150460				0	he	Default value				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154222				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_EFFECTIVEDEFAULT\"\>Sets the default value for the control field.\</ahelp\> For example, the default value will be entered when a form is opened.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150740	199			0	he	For a Reset type button, the\<emph\> Default value entry \</emph\>defines the status of the control if the reset button is activated by the user.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN11B70				0	he	Default scroll value				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN11B74				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_DEFAULT_SCROLLVALUE\"\>Sets the default value for the scrollbar.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155440				0	he	Scroll value max.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148877				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_SCROLLVALUE_MAX\"\>Specify the maximum value of a scrollbar control.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN111E4				0	he	Scroll value min.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN111E8				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_SCROLLVALUE_MIN\"\>Specify the minimum value of a scrollbar control.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN11B51				0	he	Small change				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN11B55				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Specify the value to add or subtract when the user clicks the arrow icon on the scrollbar.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN11B6F				0	he	Large change				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN11B73				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Specify the value to add or subtract when the user clicks next to the slider on the scrollbar.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id7215491				0	he	Default time				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id2299874				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Sets the default time.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150482				0	he	If you do not enter a value, the current time is inserted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id1727347				0	he	Default date				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id2545548				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Sets the default date.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id2360911				0	he	If you do not enter a value, the current date is inserted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id9207434				0	he	Default text				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id4563127				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Sets the default text for a text box or a combo box.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145206				0	he	Default button				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154681	145			0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_DEFAULT_BUTTON\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>The\<emph\> Default button\</emph\> property specifies that the corresponding button will be operated when you press the Return key.\</ahelp\>The\<emph\> Default button\</emph\> property specifies that the corresponding button will be operated when you press the Return key. If you open the dialog or form and do not carry out any further action, the button with this property is the default button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149750				0	he	This property should be assigned only to a single button within the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150931				0	he	When using Web page forms, you might come across this property in search masks. These are edit masks that contain a text field and a button to with the action "Submit form" is applied. The search term is entered in the text field and the search is started by activating the button. If the button is defined as the default button, however, simply hit Enter after entering the search term in order to start the search.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153389				0	he	Prefix symbol				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150271				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_CURRSYM_POSITION\"\>Determines if the currency symbol is displayed before or after the number when using currency fields.\</ahelp\> The default setting is currency symbols are not prefixed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154548				0	he	Tabstop				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155361	49			0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_TABSTOP\"\>The \<emph\>Tabstop \</emph\>property determines if a control field can be selected with the tab key.\</ahelp\> The following options are available:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148627				0	he	No				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3161673				0	he	When using the tab key, focusing skips the control.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3159323				0	he	Yes				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148584				0	he	The control can be selected with the Tab key.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146909				0	he	Thousands separator				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154936	148			0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_SHOWTHOUSANDSEP\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Inserts a thousands separator.\</ahelp\>With numerical and currency fields you can determine whether thousands separators are used.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156256				0	he	Label				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3156432	8			0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_LABEL\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>The Label property sets the label of the control field that is displayed in the form.\</ahelp\>The Label property sets the label of the control field that is displayed in the form. This property determines the visible label or the column header of the data field in table control forms.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154568				0	he	When you create a new control, the description predefined in the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> property is used as the default for labeling the control. The label consists of the control field name and an integer numbering the control (for example, CommandButton1). With the \<emph\>Title\</emph\> property, you can assign another description to the control so that the label reflects the function of the control. Change this entry in order to assign an expressive label to the control that is visible to the user.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	bm_id3163820				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>multi-line titles in forms\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>names; multi-line titles\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>controls; multi-line titles\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3163820				0	he	To create a multi-line title, open the combo box using the arrow button. You can enter a line break by pressing Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3159407				0	he	The \<emph\>Title\</emph\> property is only used for labeling a form element in the interface visible to the user. If you work with macros, note that at runtime, a control is always addressed through the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> property.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150293				0	he	URL				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154358	57			0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_TARGET_URL\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies the URL address that opens when you click an "Open document / web page" button.\</ahelp\>Enter the URL address for a Open document or web page button type in the \<emph\>URL\</emph\> box. The address opens when you click the button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3146074				0	he	If you move the mouse over the button in User mode, the URL appears as the extended tip, provided that no other Help text was entered.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147134				0	he	Currency symbol				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3145160	150			0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_CURRENCYSYMBOL\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>You can enter a character or a string for the currency symbol.\</ahelp\>In a currency field, you can pre-define the currency symbol by entering the character or string in the \<emph\>Currency symbol\</emph\> property.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144444				0	he	Value				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3152417	155			0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_HIDDEN_VALUE\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>You can enter the data that is inherited by the hidden control.\</ahelp\>In a \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170600.xhp\" name=\"hidden control\"\>hidden control\</link\>, under \<emph\>Value\</emph\>, you can enter the data which is inherited by the hidden control. This data will be transferred when sending the form.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157315				0	he	Password characters				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155323	157			0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_ECHO_CHAR\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>If the text box is used as a password input, enter the ASCII-code of the display character. This character is displayed instead of the characters typed by the user for the password.\</ahelp\>If the user enters a password, you can determine the characters that will be displayed instead of the characters typed by the user. Under \<emph\>Password character\</emph\>, enter the ASCII code of the desired character. You can use the values from 0 to 255.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3152493				0	he	The characters corresponding to certain ASCII codes can be seen in the \<emph\>Special Character\</emph\> dialog (Paste - Special Character).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157884				0	he	Literal mask				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3157557	160			0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_LITERALMASK\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Defines the literal mask. The literal mask contains the initial values and is always visible after downloading a form.\</ahelp\>With masked fields you can specify a literal mask. A literal mask contains the initial values of a form, and is always visible after downloading a form. Using a character code for the Edit mask, you can determine the entries that the user can type into the masked field.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148513				0	he	The length of the literal mask should always correspond to the length of the edit mask. If this is not the case, the edit mask is either cut off or filled with blanks up to the length of the edit mask.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146762				0	he	Font				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3151037	6			0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_FONT\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select the font for the text that is in the control field.\</ahelp\>For control fields which have visible text or titles, select the display font that you want to use. To open the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020100.xhp\" name=\"Font\"\>\<emph\>Font\</emph\>\</link\> dialog, click the \<emph\>...\</emph\> button. The selected font is used in control fields names and to display data in table control fields.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156734				0	he	Row height				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3160455	163			0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_ROWHEIGHT\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies the row height of a table control field.\</ahelp\>In table controls, enter a value for the row height. If you want, you can enter a value followed by valid measurement unit, for example, 2 cm.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN11FB6				0	he	Text lines end with				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN11FBA				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>For text fields, select the line end code to be used when writing text into a database column.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3160477				0	he	Time format				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3145187	169			0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_TIMEFORMAT\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>You can define the desired format for the time display.\</ahelp\>You can define the desired format for the time display.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158195				0	he	Help text				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3146823	171			0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_TAG\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies additional information or a descriptive text for the control field.\</ahelp\>In each control field you can specify additional information or a descriptive text for the control field. This property helps the programmer to save additional information that can be used in the program code. This field can be used, for example, for variables or other evaluation parameters.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157828				0	he	Formatting				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3146843				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_FORMATKEY\"\>Specifies the format code for the control. Click the \<emph\>...\</emph\> button to select the format code.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN122C4				0	he	Scale				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN122C8				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_SCALEIMAGE\"\>Resizes the image to fit the size of the control.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN1209F				0	he	Acting on a record				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN120B1				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"37930\"\>Specifies to show or hide the action items in a selected Navigation Bar control.\</ahelp\> Action items are the following: Save record, Undo, New record, Delete record, Refresh.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN120BE				0	he	Positioning				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN120D9				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"37928\"\>Specifies to show or hide the positioning items in a selected Navigation Bar control.\</ahelp\> Positioning items are the following: Record label, Record position, Record count label, Record count.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN120D7				0	he	Navigation				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN120DB				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"37929\"\>Specifies to show or hide the navigation items in a selected Navigation Bar control.\</ahelp\> Navigation items are the following: First record, Previous record, Next record, Last record.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN12156				0	he	Filtering / Sorting				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN1215A				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"37931\"\>Specifies to show or hide the filtering and sorting items in a selected Navigation Bar control.\</ahelp\> Filtering and sorting items are the following: Sort ascending, Sort descending, Sort, Automatic filter, Default filter, Apply filter, Remove filter/sort.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN12175				0	he	Icon Size				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN12179				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"37927\"\>Specifies whether the icons in a selected Navigation Bar should be small or large.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id0409200920593864				0	he	Visible				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id0409200920593851				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Defines whether the control will be visible in live mode. In design mode, the control is always visible.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id0409200921154683				0	he	Note that if this property is set to "Yes" (the default), this does not necessarily mean the control will really appear on the screen. Additional constraints are applied when calculating a control's effective visibility. For instance, a control placed in a hidden section in Writer will never be visible at all, until at least the section itself becomes visible.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id0409200921154691				0	he	If the property is set to "No", then the control will always be hidden in live mode.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id0409200921154614				0	he	Older OpenOffice.org versions up to 3.1 will silently ignore this property when reading documents which make use of it.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN12314				0	he	Visible size				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN12318				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Specifies the size of scrollbar thumb in "value units". A value of ("Scroll value max." minus "Scroll value min." ) / 2 would result in a thumb which occupies half of the background area.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN12375				0	he	If set to 0, then the thumb's width will equal its height.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN12332				0	he	Orientation				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN12336				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Specifies the horizontal or vertical orientation for a scrollbar or spin button.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170300.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Tab Order				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146959				0	he	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170300.xhp\" name=\"Tab Order\"\>Tab Order\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170300.xhp	0	help	par_id3150347	2			0	he	\<variable id=\"text\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:TabDialog\"\>In the\<emph\> Tab Order \</emph\>dialog you can modify the order in which control fields get the focus when the user presses the tab key.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170300.xhp	0	help	par_id3109850				0	he	If form elements are inserted into a document, \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> automatically determines in which order to move from one control to the next when using the Tab key. Every new control added is automatically placed at the end of this series. In the \<emph\>Tab Order\</emph\> dialog, you can adapt the order of this series to your individual needs.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170300.xhp	0	help	par_id3155934				0	he	You can also define the index of a control through its specific properties by entering the desired value under \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170101.xhp\" name=\"Order\"\>\<emph\>Order\</emph\>\</link\> in the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> dialog of the control.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170300.xhp	0	help	par_id3149760				0	he	A radio button can only be accessed by the Tab key when the radio button is selected. If you have designed a group of radio buttons where none are selected, then the user will not be able to access the group or any of the radio buttons by keyboard.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149140				0	he	Controls				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170300.xhp	0	help	par_id3150789	5			0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_TABORDER_CONTROLS\"\>Lists all controls in the form. These controls can be selected with the tab key in the given order from top to bottom.\</ahelp\> Select a control from the \<emph\>Controls \</emph\>list to assign the desired position in the tab order.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153750				0	he	Move Up				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170300.xhp	0	help	par_id3154751	7			0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_PUSHBUTTON_RID_SVXDLG_TAB_ORDER_PB_MOVE_UP\"\>Click the\<emph\> Move Up\</emph\> button to shift the selected control one position higher in the tab order.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155339				0	he	Move Down				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170300.xhp	0	help	par_id3154823	9			0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_PUSHBUTTON_RID_SVXDLG_TAB_ORDER_PB_MOVE_DOWN\"\>Click the\<emph\> Move Down\</emph\> button to shift the selected control one position lower in the tab order.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154288				0	he	Automatic Sort				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170300.xhp	0	help	par_id3153748	11			0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_PUSHBUTTON_RID_SVXDLG_TAB_ORDER_PB_AUTO_ORDER\"\>Click the\<emph\> Automatic Sort\</emph\> button to automatically sort the controls according to their position in the document.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24020000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Graphics Mode				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149762				0	he	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/24020000.xhp\" name=\"Graphics Mode\"\>Graphics Mode\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150255				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:GrafMode\"\>Lists view attributes for the selected graphic object. The embedded or linked graphic object in the current file will not be changed, only the view of the object.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150275				0	he	\<image id=\"img_id3154515\" src=\"res/helpimg/zellvor.png\" width=\"1.528in\" height=\"0.292in\" localize=\"true\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3154515\"\>Cell Styles\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150771				0	he	Graphics mode				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155262				0	he	Default				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155434				0	he	The view of the graphic object is not changed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147574				0	he	Grayscale				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153760				0	he	The graphic object is shown in grayscale. A color graphic object can become monochrome in grayscale. You can also achieve tinted grayscale colors by raising one of the color parameters.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151246				0	he	Black and White				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153062				0	he	The graphic object is shown in black and white. All brightness values below 50% will appear black, all over 50% will appear white.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146795				0	he	Watermark				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149670				0	he	The graphic object is raised in brightness and reduced in contrast so that it can be used in the background as a watermark. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\14060000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Alias				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\14060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150758				0	he	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/14060000.xhp\" name=\"Alias\"\>Alias\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\14060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148731				0	he	\<ahelp visibility=\"visible\" hid=\".uno:DBViewAliases\"\>Displays the "Alias" row in the lower part of the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/02010100.xhp\" name=\"Query Design\"\>Query Design\</link\>.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\14060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150808				0	he	\<image src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_dbviewaliases.png\" id=\"img_id3151315\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3151315\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\14060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151234				0	he	Alias				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Data				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145641				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>controls; reference by SQL\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>bound fields; controls\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>controls; bound fields/list contents/linked cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>list contents;controls\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells linked to controls\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>linked cells;controls\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>controls;assigning data sources\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155413				0	he	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170102.xhp\" name=\"Data\"\>Data\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3155306	2			0	he	The\<emph\> Data \</emph\>tab page allows you to assign a data source to the selected control.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3148773				0	he	For forms with database links, the associated database is defined in the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170200.xhp\" name=\"Form Properties\"\>Form Properties\</link\>. You will find the functions for this on the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170203.xhp\" name=\"Data\"\>\<emph\>Data\</emph\>\</link\> tab page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3149377				0	he	The possible settings of the \<emph\>Data\</emph\> tab page of a control depend on the respective control. You will only see the options that are available for the current control and context. The following fields are available:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_idN108B4				0	he	Reference value (off)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_idN108B8				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Check boxes and radio buttons in spreadsheets can be bound to cells in the current document. If the control is enabled, the value you enter in Reference value (on) is copied to the cell. If the control is disabled, the value from Reference value (off) is copied to the cell.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159121				0	he	Reference value (on)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3163812	141			0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_REFVALUE\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>You can enter a reference value for the web form, which will be remitted to a server when sending the form. With database forms, the value entered is written in the database field, assigned to the control field.\</ahelp\>You can assign a reference value to option buttons and check boxes. The reference value will be remitted to a server when sending the web form. With database forms the value entered here will be written in the database assigned to the control field.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3150225				0	he	\<emph\>Reference values for Web forms\</emph\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3147611				0	he	Reference values are useful if you design a Web form and the information on the status of the control is to be transmitted to a server. If the control is clicked by the user, the corresponding reference value is sent to the server.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3149570				0	he	For example, if you have two control fields for the options "feminine" and "masculine", and assign a reference value of 1 to the field "feminine" and the value 2 to the "masculine" field, the value 1 is transmitted to the server if a user clicks the "feminine" field and value 2 is sent if the "masculine" field is clicked.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3150260				0	he	\<emph\>Reference values for database forms\</emph\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3150654				0	he	For database forms, you can also characterize the status of an option or a check box by a reference value, storing it in the database. If you have a set of three options, for example "in progress", "completed", and "resubmission", with the respective reference values, "ToDo", "OK", and "RS", these reference values appear in the database if the respective option is clicked.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148455				0	he	Data field				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3155852	6			0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_CONTROLSOURCE\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies the field of the data source table to which the control refers.\</ahelp\>With database forms, you can link controls with the data fields.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3153224				0	he	You have several possibilities:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3159110				0	he	First case: There is only one table in the form.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3156356				0	he	Under \<emph\>Data field\</emph\>, specify the field of the data source table whose contents you want to be displayed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3146898				0	he	Second case: The control belongs to a subform that is created by an SQL query.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3154273				0	he	Under \<emph\>Data field\</emph\>, specify the field of the SQL statement whose contents you want to be displayed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3153949				0	he	Third case: \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170900.xhp\" name=\"Combo Boxes\"\>Combo Boxes\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3147494				0	he	For combo boxes, the field of the data source table in which the values entered or selected by the user should be stored is specified under \<emph\>Data field\</emph\>. The values displayed in the list of the combo box are based on an SQL statement, which is entered under \<emph\>List content\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3145167				0	he	Fourth case: \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170900.xhp\" name=\"List Boxes\"\>List Boxes\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3153764				0	he	The data source table does not contain the data to be displayed, but rather a table linked to the data source table through a common data field.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3149021				0	he	If you want a list box to display data from a table that is linked to the current data source table, under \<emph\>Data field\</emph\> specify the field of the data source table to which the content of the list box refers. Or you can specify the database field that controls the display of the data in the form. This data field provides the link to the other table if both tables can be linked through a common data field. It is usually a data field in which unique identification numbers are stored. The data field whose contents are displayed in the form is specified by an SQL statement under \<emph\>List content\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3153924				0	he	List boxes work with references. They can either be implemented with linked tables by SQL statements (fourth case) or through value lists:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3145641				0	he	\<emph\>References through linked tables (SQL statements)\</emph\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3147341				0	he	If you want a list box to display data from a database table that is linked by a common data field to the table on which the form is based, the link field of the form table is specified under \<emph\>Data field\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3155174				0	he	The link is created with an SQL Select, which, if you selected "SQL" or "Native SQL", is specified under \<emph\>Type of list contents\</emph\> in the field \<emph\>List content\</emph\>. As an example, a table "Orders" is linked to the current form control, and in the database a table "Customers" is linked to the "Orders" table. You can use an SQL statement as follows:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3148537				0	he	SELECT CustomerName, CustomerNo FROM Customers,				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3154967				0	he	where "CustomerName" is the data field from the linked table "Customers", and "CustomerNo" is the field of the table "Customers" that is linked to a field of the form table "Orders" specified under \<emph\>Data field\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3163808				0	he	\<emph\>References Using Value Lists\</emph\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3145295				0	he	For list boxes, you can use value lists. Value lists are lists that define reference values. In this way, the control in the form does not directly display the content of a database field, but rather values assigned in the value list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3151186				0	he	If you work with reference values of a value list, the contents of the data field that you specified under \<emph\>Data Field\</emph\> in the form are not visible, but rather the assigned values. If you chose "Valuelist" on the \<emph\>Data\</emph\> tab under \<emph\>Type of list contents\</emph\> and assigned a reference value to the visible list entries in the form under \<emph\>List entries\</emph\> (entered in the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170101.xhp\" name=\"General\"\>\<emph\>General\</emph\>\</link\> tab), then the reference values are compared with the data content of the given data field. If a reference value corresponds to the content of a data field, the associated list entries are displayed in the form.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154664				0	he	Bound field				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3148475				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_BOUNDCOLUMN\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Use an index to specify the table field or table SQL query to link to the field that is provided under \<emph\>Data field\</emph\>. Valid values for this property are 1, 2, 3, and so on.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_idN10AD2				0	he	If you delete the contents of the \<emph\>Bound field\</emph\> cell in the property browser, the first field of the result set is used to display and to exchange data.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3154588				0	he	This property for list boxes defines which data field of a linked table is displayed in the form.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3151213	38			0	he	If a list box in the form is to display contents of a table linked to the form table, then define in the \<emph\>Type of list contents\</emph\> field if the display is determined by an SQL command or the (linked) table is accessed. With the \<emph\>Bound field\</emph\> property, you use an index to specify to which data field of the query or of the table the list field is linked. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3148427				0	he	The property \<emph\>Bound field\</emph\> is only for forms that are used to access more than one table. If the form is based on only one table, the field to be displayed in the form is specified directly under \<emph\>Data field\</emph\>. However, if you want the list box to display data from a table that is linked to the current table over a common data field, the linked data field is defined by the property \<emph\>Bound field\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3150365				0	he	If you selected "SQL" under \<emph\>Type of list contents\</emph\>, the SQL command determines the index to be specified. Example: If you specify an SQL command such as "SELECT Field1, Field2 FROM tablename" under \<emph\>List content\</emph\>, refer to the following table:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3154716				0	he	Bound field				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3150666				0	he	Link				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3154206				0	he	{empty}				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3145257				0	he	The database field "Field1" is linked to the field specified under \<emph\>Data field\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3150887				0	he	1				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3156064				0	he	The database field "Field2" is linked to the field specified under \<emph\>Data field\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3154134				0	he	If you selected "Table" under \<emph\>Type of list contents\</emph\>, the table structure defines the index to be specified. Example: If a database table is selected under \<emph\>List content\</emph\>, refer to the following table:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3155379				0	he	Bound field				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3155529				0	he	Link				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3155373				0	he	{empty}				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3154260				0	he	The 1st column of the table is linked to the field specified under \<emph\>Data field\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3156448				0	he	1				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3154486				0	he	The 2nd column of the table is linked to the field specified under \<emph\>Data field\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3149949				0	he	2				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3146767				0	he	The 3rd column of the table is linked to the field specified under \<emph\>Data field\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149772				0	he	Type of list contents				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3154419				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_LISTSOURCETYPE\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Determines the data to fill the lists in list and combo boxes.\</ahelp\>Determines the data to fill the lists in list and combo boxes.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3153326				0	he	With the "Valuelist" option, all entries entered in the \<emph\>List entries\</emph\> field of the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170101.xhp\" name=\"General\"\>\<emph\>General\</emph\>\</link\> tab appear in the control. For database forms, you can use reference values (see the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170102.xhp\" name=\" References Using Value Lists\"\>\<emph\>References Using Value Lists\</emph\>\</link\> section).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3153067				0	he	If the content of the control is read from a database, you can determine the type of the data source with the other options. For example, you can choose between tables and queries.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153820				0	he	List content				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3159171				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_LISTSOURCE\"\>With database forms, specifies the data source for the list content of the form-element. This field can be used to define a value list for documents without a database connection.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3168456				0	he	In the case of database forms, the data source determines the entries of the list or combo box. Depending on the selected type, you have a choice between different data sources under \<emph\>List content\</emph\>, provided that these objects exist in your database. All available database objects of the type selected under \<emph\>Type of list contents\</emph\> are offered here. If you have selected the "Value List" option as the type, you can use references for database forms. If the display of the control is controlled by an SQL command, the SQL statement is entered here.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3155870				0	he	Examples of SQL statements:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3144504				0	he	For list boxes, an SQL statement may have the following form				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3156188				0	he	SELECT field1, field2 FROM table,				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3155266				0	he	Here "table" is the table whose data is displayed in the list of the control (list table). "field1" is the data field that defines the visible entries in the form; its content is displayed in the list box. "field2" is the field of the list table that is linked to the form table (value table) through the field specified under \<emph\>Data field\</emph\> if \<emph\>Bound field\</emph\> = 1 was selected.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3145074				0	he	For combo boxes, an SQL statement may take the following form				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3150991				0	he	SELECT DISTINCT field FROM table,				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3154344				0	he	Here "field" is a data field from the list table "table" whose content is displayed in the list of the combo box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3149328				0	he	\<emph\>Value lists for HTML documents\</emph\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3156034				0	he	For HTML forms, you can enter a value list under \<emph\>List content\</emph\>. Select the option "Valuelist" under \<emph\>Type of list contents\</emph\>. The values entered here will not be visible in the form, and are used to assign values to the visible entries. The entries made under \<emph\>List content\</emph\> correspond to the HTML tag <OPTION VALUE=...>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3154855				0	he	In the data transfer of a selected entry from a list box or a combo box, both the list of the values displayed in the form, which was entered on the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170101.xhp\" name=\"General\"\>\<emph\>General\</emph\>\</link\> tab under \<emph\>List entries\</emph\>, and the value list entered on the \<emph\>Data\</emph\> tab under \<emph\>List content\</emph\>, are taken into consideration: If a (non-empty) text is at the selected position in the value list (<OPTION VALUE=...>), it will be transmitted. Otherwise, the text displayed in the (<OPTION>) control is sent.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3163377				0	he	If the value list is to contain an empty string, enter the value "$$$empty$$$" under \<emph\>List content\</emph\> at the corresponding position (note uppercase/lowercase). $[officename] interprets this input as an empty string and assigns it to the respective list entry.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3156309				0	he	The following table shows the connections between HTML, JavaScript, and the $[officename] field \<emph\>List content\</emph\> using an example list box named "ListBox1". In this case, "Item" designates a list entry visible in the form:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3159204				0	he	\<emph\>HTML Tag\</emph\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3152539				0	he	\<emph\>JavaScript\</emph\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3158404				0	he	\<emph\>Entry in value list of the control (List content)\</emph\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3151198				0	he	\<emph\>Transmitted data\</emph\>				20200411 15:09:53
