helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170904.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Combo Box Wizard: Database Field				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170904.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144740				0	he	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170904.xhp\" name=\"Combo Box Wizard: Database Field\"\>Combo Box Wizard: Database Field\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170904.xhp	0	help	par_id3153323				0	he	With the combination fields, you can either save the value of a field in a database or display this value in a form.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170904.xhp	0	help	par_id3155150				0	he	The user values entered in the combination field or selected in the list can be saved in the database table that is accessed in the form. Note that the saving of values in another table is not possible. If the values are not to be saved in a database, they will be saved only in the form. This is especially helpful in HTML forms, where the user's entered or selected values are to be assigned to a server.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170904.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149760				0	he	Do you want to save the value in a database field?				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170904.xhp	0	help	par_id3150178				0	he	Two options are available for this question:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170904.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153394				0	he	Yes, I want to save it in the following database field				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170904.xhp	0	help	par_id3147043				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"DBP_RADIOBUTTON_RID_PAGE_OPTION_DBFIELD_RB_STOREINFIELD_YES\"\>Specifies whether the user's entered or selected combination field value should be saved in a database field.\</ahelp\> Several database table fields are offered which can be accessed in the current form.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170904.xhp	0	help	par_id3145212				0	he	In \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170102.xhp\" name=\"Control - Properties\"\>Control - Properties\</link\> the selected field appears as an entry in the \<emph\>Data\</emph\> tab page under \<emph\>Data field\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170904.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149177				0	he	List field				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170904.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"DBP_LISTBOX_RID_PAGE_OPTION_DBFIELD_LB_STOREINFIELD\"\>Specifies the data field where the combination field value should be saved.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170904.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148538				0	he	No, I only want to save the value in the form				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170904.xhp	0	help	par_id3149398				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"DBP_RADIOBUTTON_RID_PAGE_OPTION_DBFIELD_RB_STOREINFIELD_NO\"\>Specifies that the value of this combination field will not be written in the database and will only be saved in the form.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\19090000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	HTML Source				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\19090000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154788				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>HTML documents;source text\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\19090000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154788				0	he	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/19090000.xhp\" name=\"HTML Source\"\>HTML Source\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\19090000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156183				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:SourceView\"\>Displays the source text of the current HTML document. To view the HTML source of a new document, you must first save the new document as an HTML document.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\19090000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149760				0	he	In HTML Source mode, you can view and edit the \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#tags\" name=\"tags\"\>tags\</link\> of \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#html\" name=\"HTML\"\>HTML\</link\>. Save the document as a plain text document. Assign an .html or .htm extension to designate the document as HTML.				20200411 15:09:53
