helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153032				0	he	Show Draw Functions				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1089D				0	he	You can show and hide the \<emph\>Visible Buttons\</emph\>. Click the arrow at the end of the toolbar to access the \<emph\>Visible Buttons\</emph\> command.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149398				0	he	Selection				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147573				0	he	\<image id=\"img_id3153824\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_drawselect.png\" width=\"0.222in\" height=\"0.222in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3153824\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150771				0	he	Lets you select objects in the current document. To select an object, click the object with the arrow. To select more than one object, drag a selection frame around the objects. To add an object to a selection, press Shift, and then click the object.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143270				0	he	Line				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154897				0	he	\<image id=\"img_id3147618\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_line.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3147618\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155922				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Line\"\>Draws a straight line where you drag in the current document. To constrain the line to 45 degrees, hold down Shift while you drag.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153360				0	he	To enter text on a line, double-click the line and type or paste your text. The text direction corresponds to the direction you dragged to draw the line. To hide the line, select \<emph\>Invisible\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Line Style\</emph\> box on the \<emph\>Drawing Object Properties\</emph\> bar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152922				0	he	Rectangle				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154125				0	he	\<image id=\"img_id3158407\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_rect.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3158407\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147230				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Rect\"\>Draws a rectangle where you drag in the current document. To draw a square, hold down Shift while you drag. Click where you want to place a corner of the rectangle, and drag to the size you want.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153367				0	he	Ellipse				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156443				0	he	\<image id=\"img_id3153951\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_ellipse.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3153951\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3159197				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Ellipse\"\>Draws an oval where you drag in the current document. Click where you want to draw the oval, and drag to the size you want. To draw a circle, hold down Shift while you drag.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155308				0	he	Polygon				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154129				0	he	\<image id=\"img_id3152576\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_polygon_unfilled.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3152576\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147214				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Polygon_Unfilled\"\>Draws a line composed of a series of straight line segments. Drag to draw a line segment, click to define the endpoint of the line segment, and then drag to draw a new line segment. Double-click to finish drawing the line. To create a closed shape, double-click the starting point of the line.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154638				0	he	Hold the Shift key while drawing a polygon to position new points at 45 degree angles.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154319				0	he	The \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05270000.xhp\" name=\"Edit Points\"\>Edit Points\</link\> mode enables you to interactively modify the individual points of the polygon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153279				0	he	Curve				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153876				0	he	\<image id=\"img_id3149379\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_bezier_unfilled.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149379\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148878	57			0	he	\<variable id=\"kurvetext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Bezier_Unfilled\"\>Draws a smooth Bezier curve. Click where you want the curve to start, drag, release, and then move the pointer to where you want the curve to end and click. Move the pointer and click again to add a straight line segment to the curve. Double-click to finish drawing the curve. To create a closed shape, double click the starting point of the curve.\</ahelp\> The arc of the curve is determined by the distance you drag. \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148587				0	he	Freeform Line				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155602				0	he	\<image id=\"img_id3154510\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_linetoolbox.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3154510\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154163				0	he	\<variable id=\"freihandtext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Freeline_Unfilled\"\>Draws a freeform line where you drag in the current document. To end the line, release the mouse button. To draw a closed shape, release the mouse button near the starting point of the line.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147259				0	he	Arc				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156359				0	he	\<image id=\"img_id3153710\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_arc.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3153710\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148482				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Arc\"\>Draws an arc in the current document. To draw an arc, drag an oval to the size you want, and then click to define the starting point of the arc. Move your pointer to where you want to place the endpoint and click. You do not need to click on the oval. To draw an arc that is based on a circle, hold down Shift while you drag.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153924				0	he	Ellipse Pie				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154363				0	he	\<image id=\"img_id3159186\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_pie.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3159186\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156383				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Pie\"\>Draws a filled shape that is defined by the arc of an oval and two radius lines in the current document. To draw an ellipse pie, drag an oval to the size you want, and then click to define the first radius line. Move your pointer to where you want to place the second radius line and click. You do not need to click on the oval. To draw a circle pie, hold down Shift while you drag.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154964				0	he	Circle Segment				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151017				0	he	\<image id=\"img_id3147315\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_circlecut.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3147315\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149106				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:CircleCut\"\>Draws a filled shape that is defined by the arc of a circle and a diameter line in the current document. To draw a circle segment, drag a circle to the size you want, and then click to define the starting point of the diameter line. Move your pointer to where you want to place the endpoint of the diameter line and click. You do not need to click on the circle. To draw an ellipse segment, hold down Shift while you drag.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145150				0	he	Text				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145790				0	he	\<image id=\"img_id3155608\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_texttoolbox.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3155608\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154657				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:DrawText\"\>Draws a text box with horizontal text direction where you drag in the current document. Drag a text box to the size you want anywhere in the document, and then type or paste your text. Rotate the text box to get rotated text.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158214				0	he	Text Animation				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150380				0	he	\<image id=\"img_id3152580\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_text_marquee.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3152580\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150826	63			0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Text_Marquee\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Inserts animated text with horizontal text direction into the current document. Drag a text box, and then type or paste your text. To assign an animation effect, choose \<emph\>Format - Text - Text Animation\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>\<variable id=\"lauftext\"\>Inserts animated text with horizontal text direction into the current document. \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149966				0	he	Callouts				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153781				0	he	\<image id=\"img_id3145256\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_drawcaption.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3145256\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151274				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:DrawCaption\"\>Draws a line that ends in a rectangular callout with horizontal text direction from where you drag in the current document. Drag a handle of the callout to resize the callout. To add text, click the edge of the callout, and then type or paste your text. To change a rectangular callout to a rounded callout, drag the largest corner handle when the pointer changes to a hand.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10E50				0	he	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05270000.xhp\" name=\"Points\"\>Points\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10E60				0	he	Enables you to edit points on your drawing.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10E75				0	he	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/04140000.xhp\" name=\"From File\"\>From File\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10E95				0	he	\<link href=\"text/shared/3dsettings_toolbar.xhp\"\>Extrusion On/Off\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10EA5				0	he	Switches the 3D effects on and off for the selected objects.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149735				0	he	Vertical Callouts				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156068				0	he	\<image id=\"img_id3154818\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_verticalcaption.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3154818\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150492				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:VerticalCaption\"\>Draws a line that ends in a rectangular callout with vertical text direction from where you drag in the current document. Drag a handle of the callout to resize the callout. To add text, click the edge of the callout, and then type or paste your text. To change a rectangular callout to a rounded callout, drag the largest corner handle when the pointer changes to a hand. Only available when Asian language support is enabled.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166437				0	he	Vertical Text				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146929				0	he	\<image id=\"img_id3154372\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_verticaltext.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3154372\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152989				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:VerticalText\"\>Draws a text box with vertical text direction where you click or drag in the current document. Click anywhere in the document, and then type or paste your text. You can also move the cursor to where you want to add the text, drag a text box, and then type or paste your text. Only available when Asian language support is enabled.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155555				0	he	\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/insert_graphic_drawit.xhp\" name=\"Tips\"\>Tips for working with the \<emph\>Drawing \</emph\>bar.\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170901.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Combo Box / List Box Wizard: Table Selection				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170901.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154228				0	he	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170901.xhp\" name=\"Combo Box / List Box Wizard: Table Selection\"\>Combo Box / List Box Wizard: Table Selection\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170901.xhp	0	help	par_id3149716				0	he	Specifies a table from the available database tables that contains the data field whose content should be displayed as a list entry.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170901.xhp	0	help	par_id3153114				0	he	For list boxes, a table that can be linked with the current form table is indicated. The link table must have at least one field in common with the table of the current form. This makes it possible to establish an unambiguous reference.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170901.xhp	0	help	par_id3155555				0	he	For combo boxes, there must be a relationship between the form table and the table containing the data to be displayed in the combo box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170901.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147226				0	he	Table				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170901.xhp	0	help	par_id3155338	7			0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"DBP_LISTBOX_RID_PAGE_LCW_CONTENTSELECTION_TABLE_LB_SELECTTABLE\"\>In the\<emph\> Table \</emph\>field, select the table containing the data field whose content should be displayed in the control field.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170901.xhp	0	help	par_id3159233				0	he	The table given here appears in the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170102.xhp\" name=\"Control properties\"\>Control properties\</link\> as an element of an SQL statement in the \<emph\>List Contents\</emph\> field.				20200411 15:09:53
