helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000020.xhp	0	help	par_id3145364				0	he	1				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000020.xhp	0	help	par_id3149262				0	he	The $[officename] Web page filter supports certain capabilities of CSS2. However, to use it, print layout export must be activated in \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Load/Save - HTML Compatibility\</emph\>. Then, in HTML documents, besides the HTML Page Style, you can also use the styles "First page", "Left page" and "Right page". These styles should enable you to set different page sizes and margins for the first page and for right and left pages when printing.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000020.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145750				0	he	Importing and Exporting Numbering				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000020.xhp	0	help	par_id3145591				0	he	If, in \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Load/Save - HTML Compatibility\</emph\>, the export option "$[officename] Writer" or "Internet Explorer" is selected, the indents of numberings are exported as "margin-left" CSS1 property in the STYLE attribute of the <OL> and <UL> tags. The property indicates the difference relative to the indent of the next higher level.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000020.xhp	0	help	par_id3153573				0	he	A left paragraph indent in numbering is indicated as "margin-left" CSS1 property. First-line indents are ignored in numbering and not exported.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000020.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148556				0	he	Importing and Exporting Spreadsheet Files				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000020.xhp	0	help	par_id3153365				0	he	$[officename] imports and exports references to deleted sections such as, for example, a referenced column. The whole formula can be viewed during the export process and the deleted reference contains an indication (#REF!) to the reference. A #REF! will be correspondingly created for the reference during the import.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000020.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150228				0	he	Importing and Exporting Graphics Files				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000020.xhp	0	help	par_id3152578				0	he	As with HTML documents, you can choose to use a filter with or without the element ($[officename] Impress) in the name to open a $[officename] graphics file. If without, the file will be opened as a $[officename] Draw document. Otherwise, the file saved by an old program version is now opened in $[officename] Impress.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000020.xhp	0	help	par_id3144441				0	he	When you import an EPS file, a preview of the graphic is displayed in the document. If a preview is not available, a placeholder corresponding to the size of the graphic is displayed in the document. Under Unix and Microsoft Windows you can print the imported file by using a PostScript printer. \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>If a different printer is used the preview will be printed.\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> When exporting EPS graphics, a preview is created and has the TIFF or EPSI format. If an EPS graphic together with other graphics is exported in the EPS format then this file will be embedded unchanged in the new file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000020.xhp	0	help	par_id3146120				0	he	Multipage-TIFFs are allowed when graphics are imported or exported in TIFF format. The graphics are retrieved as a set of individual pictures in a single file, for example, the individual pages of a fax.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000020.xhp	0	help	par_id3159153				0	he	Some $[officename] Draw and $[officename] Impress options can be accessed through \<emph\>File - Export\</emph\>. See \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000200.xhp\" name=\"Graphics Export Options\"\>Graphics Export Options\</link\> for more information.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000020.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153213				0	he	PostScript				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000020.xhp	0	help	par_id3156444				0	he	To export a document or graphic in PostScript format:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000020.xhp	0	help	par_id3163714				0	he	If you have not yet done so, install a PostScript printer driver, such as the Apple LaserWriter driver.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000020.xhp	0	help	par_id3153142				0	he	Print the document with the \<emph\>File - Print\</emph\> menu command.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000020.xhp	0	help	par_id3154149				0	he	Select the PostScript printer in the dialog and mark the \<emph\>Print to file\</emph\> check box. A PostScript file will be created.				20200411 15:09:53
