helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154136				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>graphics, see also pictures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>images, see also pictures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>images; inserting and editing bitmaps\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>illustrations, see pictures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>bitmaps; inserting and editing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pixel graphics; inserting and editing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exporting; bitmaps\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>importing; bitmaps\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pictures; editing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing; pictures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>invert filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>smoothing filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sharpening filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>remove noise filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>solarization filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>aging filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>posterizing filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pop-art filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>charcoal sketches filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>mosaic filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pictures;filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>filters;pictures\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154136				0	he	\<variable id=\"insert_bitmap\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/insert_bitmap.xhp\" name=\"Inserting, Editing, Saving Bitmaps\"\>Inserting, Editing, Saving Bitmaps\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149811				0	he	Inserting Bitmaps				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3153031				0	he	A bitmap image can be inserted in $[officename] Writer, $[officename] Calc, $[officename] Draw and $[officename] Impress documents.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3147209				0	he	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Picture - From File\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3149236				0	he	Select the file. In the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> box you can restrict the selection to certain file types.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3153126				0	he	Click the \<emph\>Link\</emph\> box if you want a link to the original file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3154306				0	he	If the \<emph\>Link\</emph\> box is marked, whenever the document is updated and loaded the bitmap image is reloaded. The editing steps that you have carried out in the local copy of the image in the document are re-applied and the image is displayed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3147336				0	he	If the \<emph\>Link\</emph\> box is not marked, you are always working with the copy created when the graphic was first inserted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3153824				0	he	To embed graphics that were first inserted as links, go to \<emph\>Edit - Links\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Break Link\</emph\> button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3151384				0	he	Click \<emph\>Open\</emph\> to insert the image.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147303				0	he	Editing Bitmaps				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	hd_id187078				0	he	Icons on the Picture bar				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3148552				0	he	When you select the bitmap image, the \<emph\>Picture\</emph\> Bar offers you the tools for editing the image. Only a local copy is edited in the document, even if you have inserted an image as a link.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3159413				0	he	The \<emph\>Picture\</emph\> Bar may look slightly different depending to the module you are using.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3154124	13			0	he	A number of filters are located on the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/24010000.xhp\" name=\"Graphic Filter\"\>Graphic \<emph\>Filter\</emph\>\</link\> toolbar, which you can open with the icon on the \<emph\>Picture\</emph\> Bar. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id7055574				0	he	The original picture file will not be changed by the filters. Filters are applied to a picture only inside the document. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3145273				0	he	Some of the filters open a dialog, which you can use to select, for example, the intensity of the filter. Most filters can be applied multiple times to increase the filter effect.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3150105				0	he	In $[officename] Draw and $[officename] Image, you can add text and graphics, select these objects together with the bitmap, and export the selection as a new bitmap image.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	hd_id2572405				0	he	The Picture dialog				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id6457411				0	he	Right-click the picture and choose \<emph\>Picture\</emph\> from the submenu to open a properties dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id7991882				0	he	Change the properties of the selected picture, then click OK.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153574				0	he	Saving Bitmaps				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3152576				0	he	If you want to save in a format such as GIF, JPEG or TIFF, you must select and export the bitmap image.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id0801200803544667				0	he	To export a bitmap in Draw or Impress:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3155414				0	he	Select the bitmap image. You can also select additional objects, such as text, to be exported with the image by pressing the shift key while selecting or by opening a selection frame around all objects.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3148618				0	he	Choose \<emph\>File - Export\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Export\</emph\> dialog opens.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3157139				0	he	The \<emph\>Export\</emph\> command writes the picture with all applied filter effects to a file. The \<emph\>Save as Picture\</emph\> command in the context menu saves the picture without any filter effects, if the picture was inserted as a linked picture. An embedded picture will always be saved or exported with filters applied.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3083443				0	he	In the \<emph\>File format\</emph\> field, select the file format you want, for example GIF or JPEG.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3152462				0	he	If you only want to export the selected objects, mark the \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3150874				0	he	If \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> is not marked, the entire page of the document is exported.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3149417				0	he	Enter a name for the file and click \<emph\>Export\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id0801200803525078				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>To export a bitmap in Writer: Right-click the bitmap, choose Save Graphics. You see the Graphics Export dialog. Enter a file name and select a file type.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
