helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\export_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id3150084				0	he	Choose \<emph\>File - Save as\</emph\>. You will see the \<emph\>Save as\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\export_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id3153348				0	he	In the \<emph\>Save as type\</emph\> list box, select the desired format.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\export_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id3150985				0	he	Enter a name in the \<emph\>File name\</emph\> box and click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\export_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id3153252	7			0	he	If you want the file dialogs to offer another file format as default, select that format in \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Load/Save - General\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Default file format \</emph\>area.				20200411 15:09:53
