helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Copying Spreadsheet Areas to Text Documents				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154927				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; copying areas to text documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying; sheet areas, to text documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;sheet areas in text documents\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154927				0	he	\<variable id=\"dragdrop_table\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/dragdrop_table.xhp\" name=\"Copying Spreadsheet Areas to Text Documents\"\>Copying Spreadsheet Areas to Text Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3155892				0	he	Open both the text document and the spreadsheet.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088				0	he	Select the sheet area you want to copy.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3149827				0	he	Point to the selected area and press the mouse button. Keep the mouse button pressed for a moment, then drag the area into the text document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3152780	32			0	he	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WIN\"\>If the documents are not visible next to each other, first drag the mouse pointer to the destination document button. Continue to hold down the mouse button. The document is displayed, and you can move the mouse pointer within the document. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3156346				0	he	Once the cursor is located in the place where you want to insert the sheet area, release the mouse button. The sheet area is inserted as an OLE object.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3154047				0	he	You can select and edit the OLE object at any time.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3149164				0	he	To edit the OLE object, double-click on it.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3155389				0	he	Alternatively, select the object and choose \<emph\>Edit - Object - Edit\</emph\> or choose \<emph\>Edit\</emph\> from the context menu. You edit the object in its own frame within the text document, but you see the icons and menu commands needed for spreadsheets.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3154860				0	he	Choose \<emph\>Open\</emph\> to open the source document of the OLE object.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Changing Default Templates				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154285				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>default templates; changing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;default templates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defaults;documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>custom templates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>updating; templates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing;templates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>templates;editing and saving\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>saving;templates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>resetting;templates\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154285				0	he	\<variable id=\"standard_template\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/standard_template.xhp\" name=\"Changing Default Templates\"\>Changing Default Templates\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3152811				0	he	When you open a new document with \<emph\>File - New\</emph\>, a blank document appears based on a $[officename] template. You can edit, modify, or replace this template so that the new document contains your customized Styles or other contents.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150792				0	he	Modifying Default Templates				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3154365				0	he	First, open either an existing $[officename] template and modify it, or open a new document and edit it as necessary to create the desired template.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3159152				0	he	You can define a document template for each $[officename] module. The following describes how to proceed for text documents.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3145748	8			0	he	Save the document by choosing\<emph\> File\</emph\> -\<emph\> Templates - Save \</emph\>and saving the document in the \<emph\>My Templates\</emph\> category.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3154011				0	he	Choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Organize\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3145799				0	he	Double-click \<emph\>My Templates\</emph\> in the list on the left. You will see the user-defined templates in the user directory specified under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME - Paths\</emph\>. Select the template you have just saved and open the context menu or open the submenu of the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3146901				0	he	Choose \<emph\>Set As Default Template\</emph\>. The next time you open a new text document, the new document will be based on the new default template.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153947				0	he	Resetting Default Templates				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3156276				0	he	To reset the modified text template to the original default template:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3146792				0	he	Choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Organize\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3153714				0	he	Open the context menu and choose \<emph\>Reset default template\</emph\>. In the submenu, select the document type whose default setting you want to restore. Thereafter, when you open an empty text document, it will again correspond to the $[officename] default template for text documents.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153764				0	he	Using Custom Templates				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3150386	14			0	he	There are several ways to make your work easier by using your own custom templates. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149109				0	he	Templates in the Template Folder				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3146918				0	he	You can save a new template with \<emph\>File - Templates - Save\</emph\> or by selecting "Template" file type in any Save dialog. Save the template in the user directory specified under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME - Paths\</emph\> to be able to access the template from within the \<emph\>File - New - From Templates and Documents\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3155960				0	he	You may need to update the view of the templates in the dialog before you can see a newly created template. In this case, choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Organize\</emph\> and in the submenu of the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> button, choose \<emph\>Update\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3147343				0	he	To open the template for editing, choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Edit\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3147315				0	he	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01110000.xhp\" name=\"Templates\"\>Templates\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
