helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\change_title.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156324				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>titles; changing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;document titles\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>documents; changing titles\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\change_title.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156324				0	he	\<variable id=\"change_title\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/change_title.xhp\" name=\"Changing the Title of a Document\"\>Changing the Title of a Document\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\change_title.xhp	0	help	par_id3152801				0	he	You can specify a title for your document. Some file manager utilities can display the titles next to the filenames of your documents.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\change_title.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156136				0	he	How to change the title of the current document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\change_title.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345				0	he	Choose \<emph\>File - Properties\</emph\>. This opens the \<emph\>Properties of\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\change_title.xhp	0	help	par_id3156410				0	he	Select the \<emph\>Description\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\change_title.xhp	0	help	par_id3147242				0	he	Type the new title in the \<emph\>Title\</emph\> box and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\change_title.xhp	0	help	par_id3163802				0	he	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01100000.xhp\" name=\"Properties of\"\>Properties of\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
