helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Inserting Hyperlinks				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150789				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>hyperlinks; inserting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>links; inserting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; hyperlinks\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150789				0	he	\<variable id=\"hyperlink_insert\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/hyperlink_insert.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Hyperlinks\"\>Inserting Hyperlinks\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149095				0	he	You can insert hyperlinks in two ways: as text or as a button. In both cases, the visible text can be different from the URL.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153527	7			0	he	Display the \<emph\>Hyperlink\</emph\>\<emph\>Bar\</emph\> by choosing \<emph\>View - Toolbars - Hyperlink Bar\</emph\>. Type the visible text in the left field and the full URL in the right field, including http:// or file://.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149811	8			0	he	Place the text cursor in the document at the point where you want to insert the hyperlink. Click the\<emph\> Hyperlink\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Hyperlink\</emph\>\<emph\>Bar\</emph\>. The hyperlink is inserted as text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3155421				0	he	If you want to insert the hyperlink as a button, click and hold the \<emph\>Hyperlink\</emph\> icon and select \<emph\>As Button\</emph\> from the sub-menu.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150275				0	he	\<image id=\"img_id3149763\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_hyperlinkdialog.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149763\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3151385	30			0	he	To use the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/09070000.xhp\" name=\"Hyperlink dialog\"\>Hyperlink dialog\</link\> instead of the \<emph\>Hyperlink\</emph\>\<emph\>Bar\</emph\> to define the hyperlink, click the icon on the \<emph\>Standard\</emph\> bar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3154685	23			0	he	To jump to a specific line in a text document, first enter a bookmark at that position (\<emph\>Insert - Bookmark\</emph\>). 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_idN1076D				0	he	To jump to a cell in a spreadsheet, first enter a name for the cell (\<emph\>Insert - Names - Define\</emph\>).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3144432				0	he	In the \<emph\>URL\</emph\> combo box, enter only the short form of the URL when jumping within the same document: If the bookmark is called \<emph\>Target\</emph\>, enter \<emph\>Target\</emph\>. To jump to another document, enter the complete URL.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3152887				0	he	Hyperlinks can also be inserted by drag-and-drop from the Navigator. Hyperlinks can refer to references, headings, graphics, tables, objects, directories or bookmarks.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975				0	he	If you wish to insert in a text a hyperlink that refers to Table 1, drag the entry Table 1 from the Navigator and drop it in the text. To do this, the \<emph\>Insert as Hyperlink\</emph\> drag mode must be selected in the Navigator.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Copying Drawing Objects Into Other Documents				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153394				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>draw objects; copying between documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying; draw objects between documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;draw objects from other documents\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153394				0	he	\<variable id=\"copy_drawfunctions\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/copy_drawfunctions.xhp\" name=\"Copying Drawing Objects Into Other Documents\"\>Copying Drawing Objects Into Other Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345	28			0	he	In $[officename] it is possible to copy drawing objects between text, spreadsheets and presentation documents. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345				0	he	Select the drawing object or objects.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3156426				0	he	Copy the drawing object to the clipboard, for example, by using \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+C.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3152996				0	he	Switch to the other document and place the cursor where the drawing object is to be inserted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3149234				0	he	Insert the drawing object, for example, by using \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+V.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147573				0	he	Inserting into a text document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3150276				0	he	An inserted drawing object is anchored to the current paragraph. You can change the anchor by selecting the object and clicking the \<emph\>Change Anchor\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>OLE-Object\</emph\> toolbar or the \<emph\>Frame\</emph\> toolbar. This opens a popup menu where you can select the anchor type.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145609				0	he	Inserting into a spreadsheet				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3151210	30			0	he	An inserted drawing object is anchored to the current cell. You can change the anchor between cell and page by selecting the object and clicking the \<emph\>Change Anchor\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3149456\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_toggleanchortype.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149456\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				20200411 15:09:53
