helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Turning off Automatic URL Recognition				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149346				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>AutoCorrect function; URL recognition\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>recognizing URLs automatically\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Internet; turning off recognition of addresses\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>automatic hyperlink formatting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>URL;turning off URL recognition\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hyperlinks;turning off automatic recognition\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>links;turning off automatic recognition\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149346				0	he	\<variable id=\"autocorr_url\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/autocorr_url.xhp\" name=\"Turning off Automatic URL Recognition\"\>כיבוי הזיהוי האוטומטי של כתובות אינטרנט\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3166410				0	he	עם כתיבת טקסט, ‎$[officename]‎ מזהה באופן אוטומטי מילה שנראית כמו \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#url\" name=\"URL\"\>כתובת אינטרנט\</link\> ומחליף את המילה בקישור. ‎$[officename]‎ מעצבת את הקישור עם תכונות גופן (כמו צבע וקו תחתון) שמתבססות על סגנונות תו מסויימים.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3153561				0	he	אם אינך רוצה ש-‎$[officename]‎ תזהה כתובות אינטרנט בצורה אוטומטית בזמן הכתיבה, קיימות מספר דרכים לביטול יכולת זו.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154306				0	he	ביטול זיהוי כתובת אינטרנט				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3149233				0	he	בזמן הכתיבה ולאחר המרת מילה לקישור, אפשר ללחוץ על \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Z כדי לבטל את העיצוב הזה.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3149235				0	he	אם רק מאוחר יותר שמת לב להמרה זו, אפשר לבחור את הקישור ולבחור מתפריט הפקודות \<emph\>עיצוב - עיצוב ברירת-מחדל\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152350				0	he	כיבוי זיהוי כתובות אינטרנט				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3149514				0	he	יש לטעון מסמך שלגביו ברצונך לשנות את דרך זיהוי כתובות האינטרנט.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3151246				0	he	אם ברצונך לשנות את הדרך לזיהוי כתובות אינטרנט במסמכי טקסט, יש לפתוח מסמך טקסט.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3159413				0	he	יש לבחור \<emph\>כלים - אפשרויות תיקון אוטומטי\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3148550				0	he	בתיבת-השיח \<emph\>תיקון אוטומטי\</emph\>, יש לבחור בלשונית \<emph\>אפשרויות\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3153360				0	he	אם הסרת הסימון \<emph\>זיהוי כתובות אינטרנט\</emph\>, מילים לא יהפכו יותר לקישור באופן אוטומטי.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3156423				0	he	In $[officename] Writer there are two check boxes in front of \<emph\>URL Recognition\</emph\>. The box in the first column is for later post-editing and the box in the second column is for AutoCorrect as you type.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\measurement_units.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Selecting Measurement Units				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\measurement_units.xhp	0	help	bm_id3159201				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>documents;measurement units in\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>measurement units;selecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>units;measurement units\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>centimeters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inches\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>distances\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>selecting;measurement units\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\measurement_units.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159201				0	he	\<variable id=\"measurement_units\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/measurement_units.xhp\" name=\"Selecting Measurement Units\"\>Selecting Measurement Units\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\measurement_units.xhp	0	help	par_id3146957				0	he	You can select separate measurement units for $[officename] Writer, $[officename] Writer/Web, $[officename] Calc, $[officename] Impress and $[officename] Draw documents.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\measurement_units.xhp	0	help	par_idN10674				0	he	Open a document of the type for which you want to change the measurement units.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\measurement_units.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345				0	he	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\measurement_units.xhp	0	help	par_id3154749				0	he	In the left pane of the dialog, double-click the application for which you want to select the measurement unit.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\measurement_units.xhp	0	help	par_id3147653				0	he	Double-click \<emph\>%PRODUCTNAME Writer\</emph\> if you want to select the measurement units for text documents.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\measurement_units.xhp	0	help	par_id3150443				0	he	Click on \<emph\>General\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\measurement_units.xhp	0	help	par_id3147335				0	he	On the \<emph\>General\</emph\> tab page, select the measurement unit. Close the dialog with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\measurement_units.xhp	0	help	par_id3153126				0	he	\<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000003.xhp\" name=\"Entering measurement units directly\"\>Entering measurement units directly\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\measurement_units.xhp	0	help	par_id3148473				0	he	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040200.xhp\" name=\"Writer - General\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Writer - General\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\integratinguno.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Integrating new UNO components				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\integratinguno.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149760				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>add-ons, see UNO components\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>UNO components;integrating new\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>installing;UNO components\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\integratinguno.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149760				0	he	\<variable id=\"integratinguno\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/integratinguno.xhp\" name=\"Integrating new UNO components\"\>Integrating new UNO components\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\integratinguno.xhp	0	help	par_id3147571				0	he	Programmers can write and integrate their own UNO (Universal Network Objects) components to $[officename]. Those new components can be added to the $[officename] menus and toolbars; we call them "Add-Ons".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\integratinguno.xhp	0	help	par_id3154751				0	he	The integration of new components is supported by some tools and services. Details can be found in the $[officename] Developer's Guide. The three main steps are as follows:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\integratinguno.xhp	0	help	par_id3153748	3			0	he	Register the new components within $[officename]. This can be accomplished using the tool \<item type=\"literal\"\>unopkg\</item\>, which can be found in {installpath}\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>/ \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>\\\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>program.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\integratinguno.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345				0	he	Integrate the new components as services. The ProtocolHandler and JobDispatch services assist you; more information can be found in the $[officename] Developer's Guide.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\integratinguno.xhp	0	help	par_id3166460				0	he	Change the user interface (menus or toolbars). This can be done almost automatically by writing an XML text file that describes the changes. More information can be found in the $[officename] Developer's Guide.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\integratinguno.xhp	0	help	par_id3151110				0	he	The Add-Ons can extend the functionality of $[officename]. They are not related to the \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"CALC\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060112.xhp\" name=\"Add-Ins\"\>Add-Ins\</link\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Add-Ins\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> that provide new functions for $[officename] Calc.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Protecting Content in %PRODUCTNAME				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150620				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>protecting; contents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>protected contents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>contents protection\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>encryption of contents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>passwords for protecting contents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>indexes;unprotecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>security;protecting contents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>master passwords\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>form controls; protecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables of contents;unprotecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables in text;protecting cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>draw objects;protecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>OLE objects;protecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>graphics;protecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>frames;protecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sections;protecting\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155364				0	he	\<variable id=\"protection\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/protection.xhp\" name=\"Protecting Content in %PRODUCTNAME\"\>Protecting Content in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\>\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153394				0	he	The following is an overview of the different ways of protecting contents in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> from being modified, deleted or viewed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146957				0	he	Protecting All Documents When Saving				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3150775				0	he	All documents that are saved in \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000021.xhp\" name=\"OpenDocument format\"\>OpenDocument format\</link\> can be saved with a password. Documents that are saved with a password cannot be opened without the password. The content is secured so that it cannot be read with an external editor. This applies to content, graphics and OLE objects.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3166410				0	he	Turning on protection				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3145121				0	he	Choose \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\> and mark the \<emph\>Save with password\</emph\> check box. Save the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3154286				0	he	Turning off protection				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3148492				0	he	Open the document, entering the correct password. Choose \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\> and clear the \<emph\>Save with password\</emph\> check box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3145068				0	he	Information entered in \<emph\>File - Properties\</emph\> is not encrypted. This includes the name of the author, creation date, word and character counts.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149294				0	he	Protecting Revision Marking				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3161646				0	he	With every change made in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc and \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer, the review function records who made the change. This function can be turned on with protection, so that it can only be turned off when the correct password is entered. Until then, all changes will continue to be recorded. Acceptance or rejection of changes is not possible.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3154684				0	he	Turning on protection				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153104				0	he	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Changes - Protect Records\</emph\>. Enter and confirm a password of at least 5 characters.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3144760				0	he	Turning off protection				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3152920				0	he	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Changes - Protect Records\</emph\>. Enter the correct password.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155113				0	he	Protecting Frames, Graphics, and OLE Objects				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153703				0	he	You can protect the content, position and size of inserted graphics. The same applies to frames (in Writer) and OLE objects.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3147131				0	he	Turning on protection				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3150088				0	he	For example, for graphics inserted in Writer: Choose \<emph\>Format - Graphics - Options\</emph\> tab. Under \<emph\>Protect\</emph\>, mark \<emph\>Contents\</emph\>, \<emph\>Position\</emph\> and/or \<emph\>Size\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3147510				0	he	Turning off protection				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153657				0	he	For example, for graphics inserted in Writer: Choose \<emph\>Format - Graphics - Options\</emph\> tab. Under \<emph\>Protect\</emph\>, unmark as appropriate.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152992				0	he	Protecting Drawing Objects and Form Objects				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3166429	59			0	he	The draw objects that you insert into your documents with the \<emph\>Drawing \</emph\>toolbar can be protected from being accidentally moved or changed in size. You can do the same with form objects inserted with the \<emph\>Form Controls\</emph\> toolbar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153226				0	he	Turning on protection				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3148815	61			0	he	Choose \<emph\>Format - Object - Position and Size \</emph\>- \<emph\>Position and Size\</emph\> tab. Mark the \<emph\>Position\</emph\> or \<emph\>Size\</emph\> check box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3156289				0	he	Turning off protection				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3154991	63			0	he	Choose \<emph\>Format - Object - Position and Size \</emph\>- \<emph\>Position and Size\</emph\> tab. Unmark the \<emph\>Position\</emph\> or \<emph\>Size\</emph\> check box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B8C				0	he	\<embedvar href=\"text/shared/guide/digital_signatures.xhp#digital_signatures\"/\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id4680928				0	he	\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/protection.xhp\"\>Protecting Content in %PRODUCTNAME Writer\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id9014252				0	he	\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cell_protect.xhp\"\>Protecting Cells in %PRODUCTNAME Calc\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Inserting Charts				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153910				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>charts; inserting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>plotting data as charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; inserting charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>charts; editing data\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing; chart data\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exchanging chart axes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data; putting in columns/rows (charts)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>ordering; data series\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data series order in charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>values; changing in charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>numbers; changing in a chart\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>charts; selecting and changing types\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>2D charts selection\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>types of charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>line charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>combination charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>bar charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>charts; variants\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>3D charts;inserting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>selecting;XY charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>error indicators in charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>error bars in charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>logarithmic axes in charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>averages in charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>showing; statistics in a 2D chart\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>variances in charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>standard deviation in charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>regression curves in charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>trend lines in charts\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153910				0	he	\<variable id=\"chart_insert\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/chart_insert.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Charts\"\>Inserting Charts\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3139133				0	he	Different methods exist to start a chart:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id6772972				0	he	Insert a chart based on data from cells in Calc or Writer.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id6049684				0	he	These charts update automatically when the source data changes.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id2356944				0	he	Insert a chart with a default data set, and then use the Data Table dialog to enter your own data for that chart.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id866115				0	he	These charts can be created in Writer, Impress and Draw. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3146763				0	he	Copy a chart from Calc or Writer into another document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id701315				0	he	These charts are snapshots of the data at the time of copying. They do not change when the source data changes.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id4439832				0	he	In Calc, a chart is an object on a sheet, it cannot be a sheet of its own.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id719931				0	he	Chart in a Calc spreadsheet				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150275				0	he	Select the cells that contain the data that you want to present in your chart.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id7211218				0	he	Click the \<emph\>Insert Chart\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Standard\</emph\> toolbar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id7549363				0	he	You see a chart preview and the Chart Wizard.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id9091769				0	he	Follow the instructions in the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> to create the chart. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3761406				0	he	Chart in a Writer text document				20200411 15:09:53
