helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_legend.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008				0	he	To edit a chart legend:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_legend.xhp	0	help	par_id3146957				0	he	Double-click on the chart.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_legend.xhp	0	help	par_id3154824				0	he	A gray border appears around the chart and the menu bar now contains commands for editing the objects in the chart.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_legend.xhp	0	help	par_id3153031				0	he	Choose \<emph\>Format - Legend\</emph\> or double-click on the legend. This opens the \<emph\>Legend\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_legend.xhp	0	help	par_id3147210				0	he	Choose from the available tabs to make modifications, then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_legend.xhp	0	help	par_id3145674				0	he	To select the legend, first double-click on the chart (see step 1), then click on the legend. You can now move the legend within the chart using the mouse.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_legend.xhp	0	help	par_id3154347				0	he	\<link href=\"text/schart/01/05010000.xhp\" name=\"Format - Object Properties\"\>Format - Object Properties\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Setting up Printer and Fax Under UNIX Based Platforms				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154422				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>spadmin\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>printers; adding, UNIX\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>default printer; UNIX\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>standard printer under UNIX\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>faxes; fax programs/fax printers under UNIX\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>printers; faxes under UNIX\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>PostScript; PDF converter, UNIX\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>converters; PostScript, UNIX\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>PDF; PostScript to PDF converter, UNIX\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147834				0	he	\<variable id=\"spadmin\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/spadmin.xhp\" name=\"Setting up Printer and Fax Under UNIX Based Platforms\"\>Setting up Printer and Fax Under UNIX Based Platforms\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3159876				0	he	%PRODUCTNAME uses the installed fonts of your system. In a text document you can select from all printable fonts. In an HTML document or in Web layout, only fonts that are visible on screen are offered. In spreadsheets and drawings you can select from all installed fonts.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3159233				0	he	Under UNIX based platforms, the printer administration program \<emph\>spadmin\</emph\> is provided to help you set up printers and faxes for use with the $[officename] software.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3156410				0	he	Call the printer administration program \<emph\>spadmin\</emph\> as follows:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3147242				0	he	Change to the {install_path}/program directory.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3147209				0	he	Enter: ./spadmin				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3152349				0	he	After it starts, the window of the printer administration program \<emph\>spadmin\</emph\> appears.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3149580				0	he	Following a server installation, the system administrator first logs on as with root privileges, and starts the printer administration program \<emph\>spadmin\</emph\>. The administrator then creates a general printer configuration file called {install_path}/share/psprint/psprint.conf for all users. All changes are immediately available to all users.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159177				0	he	Setting up Printers				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3159157				0	he	Under UNIX based platforms, the $[officename] software only offers direct support for printers using the PostScript technology. Other printers must be set up as described in the section \<emph\>Printer Drivers in the $[officename] Software\</emph\>. The $[officename] software automatically provides a printer with the default driver for each system queue. You can add additional printers as needed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148564				0	he	Adding a Printer				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3147559				0	he	Change to the {install_path}/program directory.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3152360				0	he	Enter: ./spadmin				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3153360				0	he	Click the \<emph\>New Printer\</emph\> button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3151210				0	he	Select the \<emph\>Create Printer\</emph\> option and click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3153192				0	he	Select the appropriate driver for your printer. If you are not using a PostScript printer or your model is not listed, use the \<emph\>Generic Printer\</emph\> driver or follow the steps below. You can also add new drivers using the \<emph\>Import\</emph\> button or delete unnecessary drivers using the \<emph\>Delete\</emph\> button. Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3125863				0	he	Choose a command line that you can use to print on your printer (for example, lp -d my_queue). Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3150767				0	he	Give the printer a name and determine whether it should become the default printer. Click \<emph\>Finish\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3155429				0	he	To print a test page, click on \<emph\>Test Page\</emph\>. If the test page fails to print or is incorrectly printed, check all settings as described in \<emph\>Changing Printer Settings\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146147				0	he	Printer Drivers in the $[officename] Software				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3147428				0	he	When installing a non-PostScript printer, you must set your system so that PostScript can be converted into the language of the printer. We recommend using current PostScript conversion software such as Ghostscript (http://www.cs.wisc.edu/~ghost/).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3154639				0	he	You should set up the \<emph\>Generic Printer\</emph\> in that case. Also make sure that the page margins are set correctly.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3159153				0	he	If you are using a printer using the PostScript technology, you should install a description file for the printer (PostScript Printer Definition - PPD) so that you can utilize the specific printer features like paper tray selection, duplex print function and all built-in fonts. You can also use the generic printer driver since it contains the most important data and is suitable for most printers. In that case, you will have to do without the paper tray selection and must correctly set the page margins.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3146976	128			0	he	Some PPD files are installed as default files. If there is no matching PPD file for your printer, you will find various PPD files at http://www.adobe.com/products/printerdrivers/. You can also ask the manufacturer of your printer for PPD files. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147435				0	he	Importing Drivers When Creating a New Printer				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3149484				0	he	Click \<emph\>Import\</emph\> in the driver selection dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3149260	347			0	he	Click \<emph\>Browse\</emph\> to select the directory where you unpacked the PPD files. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3147443				0	he	In the \<emph\>Selection of drivers\</emph\> list box, select the printer driver you want to install.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3145364				0	he	Click OK.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152885				0	he	Deleting Drivers When Creating a New Printer				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3154729				0	he	Select the printer driver.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3155417				0	he	Click \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3149909				0	he	Be sure that you do not delete the generic printer driver, and remember that drivers deleted from server installations are no longer available to other users who are using the same server installation.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3148456				0	he	If the printer has more fonts built in than the usual PostScript fonts, you must also load the AFM files for these additional fonts. Copy the AFM files into the {install_path}/share/psprint/fontmetric directory or into the {install_path}/user/psprint/fontmetric directory. You can find AFM files, for example, at ftp://ftp.adobe.com/pub/adobe/type/win/all/afmfiles/.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148388				0	he	Changing Printer Settings				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3156284				0	he	In the printer administration program \<emph\>spadmin\</emph\>, select the printer from the \<emph\>Installed printers\</emph\> list box and click \<emph\>Properties\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> dialog appears containing several tab pages. This is where you can make settings that are used according to the PPD file of the selected printer.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3148833				0	he	Select the command on the \<emph\>Command\</emph\> tab page. You can remove superfluous commands using the \<emph\>Remove\</emph\> button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3154270				0	he	On the \<emph\>Paper\</emph\> tab page, you can define the paper format and paper tray to be used as the default settings for this printer.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3145649				0	he	On the \<emph\>Device\</emph\> tab page, you can activate the special options for your printer. If your printer can only print in black and white, choose "grayscale" under \<emph\>Color\</emph\>, otherwise choose "color". If switching to grayscale leads to unfavorable results, you can also select "color" under \<emph\>Color\</emph\> and see how the printer or PostScript emulator applies it. Furthermore, on this tab page you can set the precision with which colors are described as well as the PostScript level.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3150752				0	he	The \<emph\>Font Replacement\</emph\> tab page allows you to select a printer font type available in the printer for each font type installed on your computer. This way you can reduce the data volume sent to the printer. Font replacement can be turned on or off for each printer individually.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3153924				0	he	You should also set the page margins correctly on the \<emph\>Additional settings\</emph\> tab when using the generic printer driver so that your printout is not cropped. You can also enter a description in the Comments field, which will also be displayed on the \<emph\>Print\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3155443				0	he	Some of these settings can also be set for the current printout in the \<emph\>Print\</emph\> dialog or the \<emph\>Printer Settings\</emph\> dialog in the $[officename] software with the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150042				0	he	Renaming or Deleting Printers				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3147338				0	he	Select a printer from the \<emph\>Installed printers\</emph\> list box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3149258				0	he	To rename the selected printer, click \<emph\>Rename\</emph\>. Enter an appropriate name in the dialog that appears and click OK. The name must be unique and should be chosen so that you can recognize the printer and the application. Printer names must be assigned the same for all users because, when documents are exchanged, the selected printer remains unchanged if the recipient has it under the same name.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3153963				0	he	To delete the selected printer, click \<emph\>Remove\</emph\>. The default printer or a printer that has been created by the system administrator in a server installation cannot be removed using this dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147346				0	he	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>Selecting a Default Printer \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3145769				0	he	To make the printer selected from the \<emph\>Installed printers\</emph\> list box the default printer, double-click its name or click the \<emph\>Default\</emph\> button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154204				0	he	Using Fax Functionality				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3148463				0	he	If you have installed a fax package such as Efax or HylaFax on your computer, you can send faxes with the $[officename] software.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3154575				0	he	Change to the {install_path}/program directory.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3151277				0	he	Enter: ./spadmin				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3146808				0	he	Click \<emph\>New Printer\</emph\>. This opens the \<emph\>Add Printer\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3151070				0	he	Select \<emph\>Connect a fax device\</emph\>. Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3150787				0	he	Choose whether to use the default driver or another printer driver. If you are not using the default driver, select the appropriate driver. Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3155111				0	he	Enter a command line with which to communicate with the fax in the following dialog. In the command line of each fax sent "(TMP)" is replaced by a temporary file and "(PHONE)" by the telephone number of the recipient fax machine. If "(TMP)" occurs in the command line, the PostScript code is transmitted in a file, otherwise as standard input through a pipe. Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3146135				0	he	Assign a name to your new fax printer and determine whether the telephone numbers (see below) marked in the text should be removed from the printout, or not. Click \<emph\>Finish\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3147506				0	he	You can now send faxes by printing to the printer that has just been created.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3148419				0	he	Enter the fax number as text in the document. You can also enter a field that takes the fax number from your active database. In any case, the fax number must start with the characters @@# and end with @@. A valid entry would have the form @@#1234567@@.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3150826				0	he	If these characters including the telephone number are not printed, activate the \<emph\>Fax number is removed from the printout\</emph\> option under \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> on the \<emph\>Command\</emph\> tab page. If no telephone number is entered in the document, a dialog prompting you for it will appear after the printout.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3154196				0	he	In $[officename] you can also activate an icon for sending faxes to a default fax. To do this, choose \<emph\>Tools - Customize - Toolbars\</emph\>, click \<emph\>Add Commands\</emph\> and add from "Documents" the \<emph\>Send Default Fax\</emph\> icon. You can set which fax is used when this button is pressed under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Print\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3150517				0	he	Remember to create one separate print job for each fax, otherwise, the first recipient will receive all the faxes. In the \<emph\>Tools - Mail Merge\</emph\> dialog select the \<emph\>Printer\</emph\> option and then select the \<emph\>Single print jobs\</emph\> check box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146929				0	he	Connecting a PostScript to PDF Converter				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3154989				0	he	If a PostScript to PDF converter such as Ghostscript or Adobe Acrobat Distiller is installed on your computer, you can quickly create PDF documents in the $[officename] software.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3150524				0	he	In spadmin, click \<emph\>New Printer\</emph\>. This opens the \<emph\>Add Printer\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3145268				0	he	Select \<emph\>Connect a PDF converter\</emph\>. Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3156445				0	he	Choose whether to use the default driver, the Acrobat Distiller driver or another driver. The driver "Generic Printer (T42 enabled)" prefers the type 42 fonts over type 3 fonts; this driver is a good choice for output to a software PostScript interpreter. Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3155128				0	he	In the next dialog, enter a command line for the PostScript->PDF Converter. Enter the directory where the PDF files should be saved. If you do not provide a directory, the user's home directory will be used. In the command line "(TMP)" is replaced by a temporary file and "(OUTFILE)" by the target file, the name of which is created from the document name. If "(TMP)" occurs in the command line, the Postscript code is forwarded in a file, otherwise as standard input through a pipe. If Ghostscript or Adobe Acrobat Distiller is in the search path, you can use one of the predefined command lines. Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3152889				0	he	Assign a name to your new PDF converter. Click \<emph\>Finish\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3153064				0	he	You can now create PDF documents by printing to the converter that has just been created.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Scripting %PRODUCTNAME				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	bm_id5277565				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>assigning scripts\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>programming;scripting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>form controls;assigning macros\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pictures;assigning macros\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>hyperlinks;assigning macros\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>shortcut keys;assigning macros\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>controls;assigning macros (Basic)\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>menus;assigning macros\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>events;assigning scripts\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1070A				0	he	\<variable id=\"scripting\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/scripting.xhp\"\>Assigning Scripts in %PRODUCTNAME\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10728				0	he	You can assign custom scripts (macros) to menu items, icons, dialog controls, and events in %PRODUCTNAME.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1072B				0	he	%PRODUCTNAME internally supports the following scripting languages:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10731				0	he	%PRODUCTNAME Basic				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10739				0	he	JavaScript				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1073D				0	he	BeanShell				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_id6797082				0	he	Python				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1091F				0	he	In addition, developers can use high-level languages, for example Java programming language, to control %PRODUCTNAME externally. See the API project at Apache OpenOffice.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10751				0	he	To assign a script to a new menu entry				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10758				0	he	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Customize\</emph\>, and click the \<emph\>Menus\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1093D				0	he	Click \<emph\>Add\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10760				0	he	In the \<emph\>Category\</emph\> list box, scroll down and open the "%PRODUCTNAME Macros" entry.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10768				0	he	You see entries for "%PRODUCTNAME Macros" (scripts in the share directory of your %PRODUCTNAME installation), "My Macros" (scripts in the user directory), and the current document. Open any one of them to see the supported scripting languages.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1076C				0	he	Open any scripting language entry to see the available scripts. Select a script.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10770				0	he	A list of the script functions appears in the \<emph\>Functions\</emph\> list box. Select a function.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10778				0	he	Click \<emph\>New\</emph\> to create a new menu assignment. The new menu entry appears in the \<emph\>Menu entries\</emph\> list box. Click the menu entry and enter text to rename the entry.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10783				0	he	To assign a script to a key combination				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10787				0	he	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Customize - Keyboard\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A59				0	he	In the \<emph\>Category\</emph\> list box, scroll down and open the "%PRODUCTNAME Macros" entry.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A61				0	he	You see entries for "%PRODUCTNAME Macros" (scripts in the share directory of your %PRODUCTNAME installation), "My Macros" (scripts in the user directory), and the current document. Open any one of them to see the supported scripting languages.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A65				0	he	Open any scripting language entry to see the available scripts. Select any script.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A69				0	he	A list of the script functions will appear in the \<emph\>Functions\</emph\> list box. Select any function.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A71				0	he	Click the option button for %PRODUCTNAME or Writer (or whichever application is currently open). 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A74				0	he	Selecting the option button sets the scope of the new key combination to be applicable in all of %PRODUCTNAME or only in documents of the current module.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A78				0	he	Select a key combination from the \<emph\>Shortcut keys\</emph\> list box and click \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1078A				0	he	To assign a script to an event				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1078E				0	he	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Customize - Events\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A16				0	he	Click \<emph\>Assign Macro\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A9E				0	he	In the \<emph\>Library\</emph\> list box, scroll down and open the "%PRODUCTNAME Macros" entry.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10AA6				0	he	You see entries for "%PRODUCTNAME Macros" (scripts in the share directory of your %PRODUCTNAME installation), "My Macros" (scripts in the user directory), and the current document. Open any one of them to see the supported scripting languages.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10AAA				0	he	Open any scripting language entry to see the available scripts. Select any script.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10AAE				0	he	A list of the script functions will appear in the \<emph\>Assigned Macros\</emph\> list box. Select any function.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10AB6				0	he	Select to save in %PRODUCTNAME or current document.				20200411 15:09:53
