helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_barformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3156136				0	he	You can add texture to the bars in a graph or chart (instead of the default colors) via bitmap graphics:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_barformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3153748				0	he	Enter edit mode by double-clicking on the chart.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_barformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3149182				0	he	Click on any bar of the bar series you want to edit. All bars of this series are now selected.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_barformat.xhp	0	help	par_id720847				0	he	If you want to edit only one bar, click again on that bar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_barformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3147275				0	he	In the context menu choose \<emph\>Object Properties\</emph\>. Then choose the \<emph\>Area\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_barformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3146797				0	he	Click on \<emph\>Bitmap\</emph\>. In the list box select a bitmap as a texture for the currently selected bars. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to accept the setting.				20200411 15:09:53
