helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3149807	18			0	he	From now on, if you save a document, the \<emph\>File type \</emph\>will be set according to your choice. Of course, you still can select another file type in the file save dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156423				0	he	Opening Microsoft Office Files by Default				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153092				0	he	Converting Many Microsoft Office Files into OpenDocument Format				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3146986				0	he	The \<emph\>Document Converter Wizard\</emph\> will copy and convert all Microsoft Office files in a folder into $[officename] documents in the OpenDocument file format. You can specify the folder to be read, and the folder where the converted files are to be saved.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3150486				0	he	Choose \<link href=\"text/shared/autopi/01130000.xhp\" name=\"File - AutoPilot - Document Converter\"\>\<emph\>File - Wizards - Document Converter\</emph\>\</link\> to start the wizard.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154319				0	he	Macros in Microsoft Office and $[officename]				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3154921				0	he	Microsoft Office and $[officename] cannot run the same macro code. Microsoft Office uses VBA (Visual Basic for Applications) code, and $[officename] uses Basic code based on the $[officename] API (Application Program Interface) environment. Although the programming language is the same, the objects and methods are different.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id0804200804173539				0	he	The most recent versions of %PRODUCTNAME can run some Excel Visual Basic scripts if you enable this feature at \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Load/Save - VBA Properties\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3152577				0	he	If you use macros in one of the applications and want to use the same functionality in the other application, you must edit the macros. $[officename] can load the macros that are contained within Microsoft Office files and you can then view and edit the macro code in the $[officename] \<link href=\"text/shared/main0600.xhp\" name=\"Basic IDE\"\>Basic IDE\</link\> editor.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152596				0	he	You can choose to preserve or delete VBA macros				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3153144				0	he	Open a Microsoft Office document that contains VBA macro code. Change only the normal contents (text, cells, graphics), and do not edit the macros. Save the document as a Microsoft Office file type. Open the file in Microsoft Office, and the VBA macros will run as before.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3150011				0	he	You may delete the VBA macros from the Microsoft Office file on loading or on saving.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3155366				0	he	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01130100.xhp\" name=\"Load/Save - VBA Properties\"\>Load/Save - VBA Properties\</link\>\</emph\> to set the VBA macro handling of $[officename].				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\filternavigator.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Using the Filter Navigator				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\filternavigator.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150322				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>filters; Navigator\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>filter conditions;connecting\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\filternavigator.xhp	0	help	par_idN105A3				0	he	\<variable id=\"filternavigator\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/filternavigator.xhp\"\>Using the Filter Navigator\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\filternavigator.xhp	0	help	par_id3150322				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:FormFilterNavigator\"\>To connect several filter conditions with Boolean OR, click the \<emph\>Filter navigation\</emph\> icon on the filter bar.\</ahelp\> The \<emph\>Filter navigator\</emph\> window appears.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\filternavigator.xhp	0	help	par_id3153711				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FILTER_NAVIGATOR\"\>The filter conditions that have been set appear in the \<emph\>Filter navigator\</emph\>. As soon as a filter is set, you see a blank filter entry at the bottom of the \<emph\>Filter navigator\</emph\> . You can select this entry by clicking the word "Or". Once you have selected the blank filter entry, you can enter additional filter conditions in the form. These conditions are linked by Boolean OR to the previously defined conditions.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\filternavigator.xhp	0	help	par_id3145620				0	he	The context menu can be called for each entry in the \<emph\>Filter navigator\</emph\>. \<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_FILTER_IS_NOT_NULL\"\>You can edit the filter conditions in this area directly as text. If you wish to check if a field has content or no content, you can select the filter conditions "empty" (SQL:"Is Null") or "not empty" (SQL: "Is not Null").\</ahelp\> It is also possible to delete the entry by using the context menu.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\filternavigator.xhp	0	help	par_id3156374				0	he	You can move filter conditions in the \<emph\>Filter navigator\</emph\> by dragging and dropping, or use the keys \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Alt+Up Arrow or \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Alt+Down Arrow. To copy filter conditions, drag them while holding down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\breaking_lines.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Inserting Line Breaks in Cells				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\breaking_lines.xhp	0	help	bm_id6305734				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>line breaks; in cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; line breaks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text flow; in cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text breaks in cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>wrapping text; in cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>words; wrapping in cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>automatic line breaks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>new lines in cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;line breaks in cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables;inserting line breaks\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\breaking_lines.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D5				0	he	\<variable id=\"breaking_lines\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/breaking_lines.xhp\"\>Inserting Line Breaks in Cells\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\breaking_lines.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D9				0	he	Inserting line breaks in $[officename] Calc spreadsheet cells				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\breaking_lines.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E0				0	he	To insert a line break in a spreadsheet cell, press the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter keys. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\breaking_lines.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E3				0	he	This will work only with the text edit cursor inside the cell, not at the input line. So first double-click the cell, then single-click at the text position where you want the line break.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\breaking_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id0509200914160968				0	he	You can search for a newline character in the Find & Replace dialog by searching for \\n as a regular expression. You can use the text function CHAR(10) to insert a newline character into a text formula.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\breaking_lines.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E6				0	he	Formatting $[officename] Calc cells for automatic line wrapping				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\breaking_lines.xhp	0	help	par_idN106ED				0	he	Select the cells for which you want an automatic line break.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\breaking_lines.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F1				0	he	Choose \<emph\>Format - Cells - Alignment\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\breaking_lines.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F9				0	he	Select \<emph\>Wrap text automatically\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\breaking_lines.xhp	0	help	par_idN10700				0	he	Inserting line breaks in $[officename] Writer text document tables				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\breaking_lines.xhp	0	help	par_idN10707				0	he	To insert a line break in a text document table cell, press the Enter key.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\breaking_lines.xhp	0	help	par_idN1070A				0	he	An automatic line break will be performed while you type across the end of each cell.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\breaking_lines.xhp	0	help	par_idN10718				0	he	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05340300.xhp\"\>Alignment\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Drag-and-Drop With the Data Source View				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145071				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>drag and drop; data source view\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data source view; drag and drop\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying;from data source view\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;from data source view\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145071				0	he	\<variable id=\"dragdrop_beamer\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/dragdrop_beamer.xhp\" name=\"Drag-and-Drop With the Data Source View\"\>Drag-and-Drop With the Data Source View\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3151111				0	he	A fast way of copying from a data source into a text or spreadsheet document, or of creating forms based on a data source, is by drag-and-drop.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3147335				0	he	\<image id=\"img_id3155390\" src=\"res/helpimg/copydata.png\" width=\"8.47mm\" height=\"8.47mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3155390\"\>Mouse pointer copying data\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3145315				0	he	Copying with Drag-and-Drop				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3149233				0	he	If you want to reverse a drag-and-drop, position the cursor in your document and choose \<emph\>Edit - Undo\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3149656				0	he	It is also possible to copy by drag-and-drop from a document into a data source:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3153379				0	he	A text table or the selected range of a spreadsheet can be dragged using drag-and-drop to a table container in the data source explorer.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3151211				0	he	Plain text can be copied using drag-and-drop from one document to a data field in the data source view.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145421				0	he	Using data in a text document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3154685				0	he	You can insert a database field in a text document by dragging a field name from the column header of the data source view into the document. This is especially useful when designing form letters. Simply drag the desired fields - home address, form of address, and so on - into your document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3153105				0	he	To insert a complete record, select the corresponding header and drag it into the document. When you release the mouse button, the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12070000.xhp\" name=\"Insert database columns\"\>\<emph\>Insert database columns\</emph\>\</link\> dialog appears, in which you can decide whether to use all database fields, and whether to copy the data into the document as text, a table or fields. All currently selected records will be inserted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147230				0	he	Applying data to a table document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3125864				0	he	You can insert one or more records into the current sheet of a spreadsheet by selecting the rows in the data source view and dragging and dropping them into the spreadsheet. The data is inserted at the place where you release the mouse button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149766				0	he	Inserting controls in a text form				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3155132				0	he	When you create a text form linked to a database, you can generate controls by drag-and-drop from the data source view.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3149562				0	he	When you drag a database column into the text document, you insert a field. If you hold down Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> while dragging, a text field is inserted, grouped with an appropriate label field. The text field already contains all the database information that you need for the form.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Registering an Address Book				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152823				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>data sources; registering address books\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>address books; registering\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>system address book registration\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>registering; address books\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154228				0	he	\<variable id=\"data_addressbook\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_addressbook.xhp\" name=\"Registering an Address Book\"\>Registering an Address Book\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3154927				0	he	In \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> you can register different data sources. The contents of the data fields are then available to you for use in various fields and controls. Your system address book is such a data source.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3149346				0	he	\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> templates and wizards use fields for the contents of the address book. When activated, the general fields in the templates are automatically replaced with the fields from the data source of your address book.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3147399				0	he	In order for the replacement to take place, you must tell \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> which address book you use. The wizard asking for this information appears automatically the first time you activate, for example, a business letter template. You can also call the wizard by following the steps listed below.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id5941648				0	he	The address book data is read-only in %PRODUCTNAME Base. It is not possible to add, edit, or delete address data from within Base.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149096				0	he	Address Data Source Wizard				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008				0	he	To call the \<link href=\"text/shared/autopi/01170000.xhp\" name=\"Address Data Source\"\>Address Data Source\</link\> wizard, choose \<emph\>File - Wizards - Address Data Source\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149811				0	he	Registering An Existing Address Book Manually				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3150771				0	he	Choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Address Book Source\</emph\>. The \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01110101.xhp\" name=\"Templates: Address Book Assignment\"\>\<emph\>Templates: Address Book Assignment\</emph\>\</link\> dialog appears.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3148491				0	he	In the \<emph\>Data source\</emph\> combo box, select the system address book or the data source you want to use as an address book.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3149669	11			0	he	If you have not yet registered the system address book in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> as the data source, click the \<emph\>Administrate\</emph\> button. This takes you to the \<emph\>Address Book Data Source Wizard\</emph\>, in which you can register your address book as a new data source in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3154365				0	he	In the \<emph\>Table\</emph\> combo box, select the database table you want to use as the address book.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3147084				0	he	Under \<emph\>Field assignment\</emph\>, match the fields for first name, company, department, and so on to the actual field names used in your address book.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_idN10784				0	he	When finished, close the dialog with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3149983				0	he	Now your data source is registered in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> as the address book. If you now open a template from the \<emph\>Business Correspondence\</emph\> category, \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> can automatically insert the correct fields for a form letter.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_protect.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Protecting Records				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_protect.xhp	0	help	bm_id3159201				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>changes; protecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>protecting; recorded changes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>records; protecting\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_protect.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159201	1			0	he	\<variable id=\"redlining_protect\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/redlining_protect.xhp\" name=\"Protecting Records\"\>Protecting Records\</link\> \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id1631824				0	he	The review function is available in %PRODUCTNAME for text documents and spreadsheet documents.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3154751				0	he	To protect the changes made in a document during editing, choose \<emph\>Edit - Changes - Protect Records\</emph\>. To turn off the function or to accept or reject changes it is necessary to enter the correct password first.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088				0	he	Choose \<emph\>Protect Records\</emph\>. This opens the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/password_dlg.xhp\" name=\"Password\"\>\<emph\>Password\</emph\>\</link\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345				0	he	Enter a password consisting of at least 5 characters and confirm it. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytable2application.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Inserting Data From Spreadsheets				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytable2application.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154186				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>tables; inserting spreadsheet cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; cell ranges from spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;cell ranges from spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>presentations;inserting spreadsheet cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text documents;inserting spreadsheet cells\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytable2application.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154186				0	he	\<variable id=\"copytable2application\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/copytable2application.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Data From Spreadsheets\"\>Inserting Data From Spreadsheets\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytable2application.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088				0	he	Use the clipboard to copy the contents of a single cell. You can also copy a formula from a cell into the clipboard (for example, from the input line of the formula bar) so that the formula can be inserted into a text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytable2application.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345				0	he	To copy a cell range into a text document, select the cell range in the sheet and then use either the clipboard or drag-and-drop to insert the cells into the text document. You will then find an OLE object in the text document, which you can edit further.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytable2application.xhp	0	help	par_id3146957				0	he	If you drag cells to the normal view of a presentation document, the cells will be inserted there as an OLE object. If you drag cells into the outline view, each cell will form a line of the outline view.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytable2application.xhp	0	help	par_id3148538				0	he	When you copy a cell range from $[officename] Calc to the clipboard, the drawing objects, OLE objects and charts within this range are also copied.				20200411 15:09:53
