helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_title.xhp	0	help	par_id3153527				0	he	To edit a chart title that you have inserted into a $[officename] document:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_title.xhp	0	help	par_id3153681				0	he	Double-click on the chart.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_title.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345				0	he	A gray border appears around the chart and the menu bar now contains commands for editing the objects in the chart.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_title.xhp	0	help	par_id3149811				0	he	Double-click on the default title text. A gray border appears around the text and you can now make changes. Press Enter to create a new line.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_title.xhp	0	help	par_id2706991				0	he	If no title text exists, choose \<emph\>Insert - Title\</emph\> to enter the text in a dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_title.xhp	0	help	par_id3145382				0	he	A single-click on the title allows you to move it with the mouse.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_title.xhp	0	help	par_id3155341				0	he	If you want to change the formatting of the main title, choose \<emph\>Format - Title - Main Title\</emph\>. This opens the \<emph\>Title\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_title.xhp	0	help	par_id3147336				0	he	Select one of the available tabs in the dialog to make modifications.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_title.xhp	0	help	par_id3155135				0	he	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. In your document, click outside the chart to exit chart editing mode.				20200411 15:09:53
