helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Searching for Attributes				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	bm_id5681020				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>fonts;finding\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>font attributes;finding\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text attributes;finding\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>attributes; finding\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>finding; attributes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>resetting;Find & Replace mode\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN10663				0	he	\<variable id=\"find_attributes\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/find_attributes.xhp\"\>Searching for Attributes\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN10681				0	he	You can search for text with attributes that are applied either by direct formatting or by styles. For example, if you search for the \<emph\>Font\</emph\> attribute, all instances of text that do not use the default font are found. All text that has a directly coded font attribute, and all text where a style switches the font attribute, are found.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN10688				0	he	If you want to find text with any font by name, click the \<emph\>Format\</emph\> button in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02100000.xhp\"\>Find & Replace\</link\> dialog of %PRODUCTNAME Writer.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN1069D				0	he	After you select the attributes that you want to search for, the \<emph\>Search for Styles\</emph\> box in the \<emph\>Options \</emph\>area of the %PRODUCTNAME Writer \<emph\>Find & Replace \</emph\>dialog changes to \<emph\>Including Styles\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B0				0	he	If you want to search for text in which attributes were set by using direct formatting and styles, select the \<emph\>Including Styles\</emph\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B7				0	he	The search criteria for attributes are listed below the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN106BE				0	he	To search for all font changes				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN106C5				0	he	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Find & Replace\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN106CD				0	he	Clear the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> text box if necessary.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D5				0	he	Click \<emph\>Attributes\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN106DD				0	he	In the \<emph\>Attributes\</emph\> dialog, select the \<emph\>Font\</emph\> check box, and click OK.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E8				0	he	In the \<emph\>Find & Replace\</emph\> dialog, you now can read "Font" below the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> text box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F4				0	he	Click \<emph\>Find\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN106FB				0	he	All places where a font change was applied, either directly or by assigning an appropriate style, are found.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN106FE				0	he	To reset the Find & Replace mode				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN10702				0	he	To stop searching for the current attributes, reset the \<emph\>Find & Replace\</emph\> dialog to normal mode.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN1070C				0	he	Click \<emph\>No Format\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN1071E				0	he	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/02100000.xhp\"\>Find & Replace\</link\> dialog				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_id6837672				0	he	Searching for attributes is available in the Find & Replace dialog for text documents.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Error Report Tool				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150616				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>Error Report Tool\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>reporting errors\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>crash reports\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>activating;Error Report Tool\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150616				0	he	\<variable id=\"error_report\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/error_report.xhp\" name=\"Error Report Tool\"\>Error Report Tool\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345				0	he	The Error Report Tool starts automatically when a program crash occurs. If the program enters into an endless loop, so that it does not respond to mouse-clicks or keypresses, you can also start the Error Report Tool manually.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088				0	he	The Error Report Tool gathers all necessary information that can help the program developers to improve the code, so that in later versions this error can possibly be avoided. Please help us to improve the software and send the generated error report.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148538				0	he	Starting the Error Report Tool				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3149811				0	he	With most program crashes the Error Report Tool will start automatically. However, if the program seems to be stuck and the tool does not start automatically, you can start the tool manually:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154046				0	he	Completing the Report				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3147335				0	he	On the main Error Report Tool dialog, you can enter some additional information that may help the developers to localize the error. For example, if the error only appears after a change in your hardware or software environment, or if you clicked on a button, please include that information.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159399				0	he	Sending the Error Report				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3150504				0	he	The Error Report Tool uses the HTTP PUT / SOAP protocol to send the report data. You may optionally enter some descriptive text that will help us to identify the context of the program crash. Then click the \<emph\>Send\</emph\> button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3149670				0	he	You will not get an answer to your error report. If you need support, please visit the \<link href=\"text/shared/main0108.xhp\"\>support forum\</link\> on the Internet.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3153526				0	he	You may choose to respond to questions that the developers may have about the reported error. Mark the check box if you allow to be contacted by e-mail, should additional information be required. By default this box is not marked, so you will not get any e-mail.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150792				0	he	What Data is Sent?				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3154366				0	he	The error report consists of several files. The main file contains information about the error type, operating system name and version, memory usage, and the description that you entered. You can click the \<emph\>Show Report\</emph\> button on the main dialog of the Error Report Tool to view what will get sent in the main file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3151177				0	he	In addition, relevant memory contents and stack traces are gathered by some system standard tools ("dbhhelp.dll" on Windows systems, "pstack" on UNIX systems). This information will be sent also.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Copying Graphics From the Gallery				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145345				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>Gallery;dragging pictures to draw objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>draw objects;dropping Gallery pictures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>drag and drop;from Gallery to draw objects\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145345				0	he	\<variable id=\"dragdrop_fromgallery\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp\" name=\"Copying Graphics From the Gallery\"\>Copying Graphics From the Gallery\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3155535				0	he	If you drag a graphic from the Gallery into a text, spreadsheet or presentation document, the graphic will be inserted there.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3149762				0	he	If you release the graphic \<emph\>directly on a draw object\</emph\>, please note the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3153825				0	he	If you move the graphic (drag it without pressing any key, in which case no additional symbol appears next to the mouse pointer), only the attributes are copied from the graphic and applied to the draw object on which you release the mouse button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3153665				0	he	If you copy the graphic (drag it while holding down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key, in which case a plus sign appears next to the mouse pointer), the graphic will be inserted as an object.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3154514				0	he	If you create a hyperlink (drag while holding down Shift and \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>, in which case a linking arrow appears next to the mouse pointer), the drawing object is replaced by the graphic from the Gallery, but the position and size of the replaced draw object are retained.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Working with Queries				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	bm_id840784				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>databases;creating queries\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>filtering;data in databases\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>queries;defining\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defining;queries\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>wizards;database queries\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Query Wizard\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN105F9				0	he	\<variable id=\"data_queries\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_queries.xhp\"\>Working with Queries\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN10617				0	he	If you often want to access only a subset of your data that can be well defined by a filter condition, you can define a query. This is basically a name for the new view at the filtered data. You open the query and see the current data in the table layout that you defined.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN1061A				0	he	Creating a New Query With the Query Wizard				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN1061E				0	he	In %PRODUCTNAME you can create a new query using the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/querywizard00.xhp\"\>Query Wizard\</link\>:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN10632				0	he	Open the database file where you want to create the new query.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN10636				0	he	In the left pane of the database window, click the \<emph\>Queries\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN1063E				0	he	Click \<emph\>Use Wizard to Create Query\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN10645				0	he	Creating a New Query With the Design View				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN1064C				0	he	Open the database file where you want to create the new query.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN10650				0	he	In the left pane of the database window, click the \<emph\>Queries\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN10658				0	he	Click \<emph\>Create Query in Design View\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN1065F				0	he	You see the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/02010100.xhp\"\>Query Design window\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
