helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153345				0	he	Designing Business Cards Through a Dialog				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3146798	70			0	he	Choose \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01010300.xhp\" name=\"File - New - Business Cards\"\>\<emph\>File - New - Business Cards\</emph\>\</link\> to open the\<emph\> Business Cards \</emph\>dialog, which allows you to choose how your business cards will look.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147654				0	he	Designing Labels and Business Cards				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3152349				0	he	You can design both labels and business cards through the \<emph\>Labels\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3153880				0	he	Choose \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01010200.xhp\" name=\"File - New - Labels\"\>\<emph\>File - New - Labels\</emph\>\</link\> to open the \<emph\>Labels\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3149233				0	he	On the \<emph\>Labels\</emph\> tab, under \<emph\>Format\</emph\>, define the label format.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3145674				0	he	$[officename] Writer contains many formats of commercially available sheets for labels, badges, and business cards. You can also add other, user-defined formats.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3143271				0	he	On the \<emph\>Labels\</emph\> tab, under \<emph\>Inscription\</emph\>, you can choose what you want written on the labels.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3145610				0	he	This often involves database fields, so that the labels can be printed with varying content, when sending "Form Letters" for example. It is also possible to have the same text printed on every label.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3151385	85			0	he	Use the \<emph\>Database \</emph\>and \<emph\>Table \</emph\>list boxes to select the database and table from which the data fields are obtained. Click on the arrow button to transfer the selected data field into the inscription area. Press Enter to insert a line break. You can also enter spaces and any other fixed text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3147560				0	he	On the \<emph\>Format\</emph\> tab you can define your own label formats, not covered by the predefined formats. To do this, select "User" from the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> list box. On the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab, you can specify whether all labels or only certain ones are to be created.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3150358				0	he	On the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab page, make sure that the \<emph\>Synchronize contents\</emph\> box is selected. If this is selected, a label only has to be entered (on the top left label) and edited once.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3156424				0	he	As soon as you click on \<emph\>New Document\</emph\>, you will see a small window with the \<emph\>Synchronize Labels\</emph\> button. Enter the first label. When you click on the \<emph\>Synchronize Labels\</emph\> button, the current individual label is copied to all the other labels on the sheet.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3149767				0	he	Click on \<emph\>New Document\</emph\> to create a new document with the settings you have entered.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3150449				0	he	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01010300.xhp\" name=\"Business Cards\"\>Business Cards\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Working With %PRODUCTNAME XML Filters 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	bm_id7007583				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>file filters (XML)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>saving;to XML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>loading;XML files\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>importing;from XML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exporting;to XML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>XSLT filters, see also XML filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>distributing XML filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>deleting;XML filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>testing XML filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>XML filters;creating/testing/distributing/deleting\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10923				0	he	\<variable id=\"xsltfilter\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/xsltfilter.xhp\"\>About XML Filters\</link\> \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10927				0	he	%PRODUCTNAME \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000021.xhp\"\>stores documents in XML format\</link\>. You can create customized filters that convert the native OpenDocument XML file format used by %PRODUCTNAME into another format. These filters can be integrated into %PRODUCTNAME seamlessly so that you can save or load these formats transparently.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1093A				0	he	To create an XML filter, you must have a good understanding of XML and XSLT concepts. These concepts are beyond the scope of this help.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1093D				0	he	An XML filter contains \<emph\>stylesheets\</emph\> that are written in the XSLT language. The stylesheets define the transformation from the OpenDocument file format to another XML format through export and import filters. There are three types of XML filters:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10947				0	he	 \<emph\>Import Filters\</emph\> load external XML files and transform the format of the files into the OpenDocument XML file format. After you install an import filter, the name of the filter is added to the list of file types in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01020000.xhp\"\>File Open dialog\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10960				0	he	 \<emph\>Export Filters\</emph\> transform OpenDocument XML files and \<emph\>save\</emph\> the files to a different XML format. After you install an export filter, the name of the filter is added to the list of file types in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01070001.xhp\"\>Export dialog\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10979				0	he	 \<emph\>Import/Export Filters\</emph\> load and save OpenDocument XML files into a different XML \<emph\>format\</emph\>. After you install these filters, the names of the filters are added to the list of file types in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01020000.xhp\"\>File Open dialog\</link\> and the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01070000.xhp\"\>File Save As dialog\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B39				0	he	\<link href=\"http://www.w3.org/Style/XSL/\"\>World Wide Web Consortium Pages on Extensible \<emph\>Stylesheet\</emph\> Language (XSL)\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B4E				0	he	\<link href=\"http://www.w3.org/XML/\"\>World Wide Web Consortium Pages on Extensible Markup Language (XML)\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10D97				0	he	 \<embedvar href=\"text/shared/00/00000021.xhp#xmlformat\"/\> 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_id5569017				0	he	\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/xsltfilter_distribute.xhp\"\>Distributing XML filters\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_id6426892				0	he	\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/xsltfilter_create.xhp\"\>Creating and Testing XML filters\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_paragraph.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	הגדרת מסגרות לפיסקאות				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_paragraph.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147571				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>borders, see also frames\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>paragraphs; defining borders\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>borders; for paragraphs\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>frames; around paragraphs\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;paragraph borders\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defining;paragraph borders\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_paragraph.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147571	15			0	he	\<variable id=\"border_paragraph\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/border_paragraph.xhp\" name=\"Defining Borders for Paragraphs\"\>הגדרת מסגרות לפיסקאות\</link\> \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_paragraph.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159233				0	he	הגדרת סגנון מסגרת מוכן				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_paragraph.xhp	0	help	par_id3156113				0	he	יש למקם את הסמן בפיסקה שברצונך להגדיר מסגרת עבורה.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_paragraph.xhp	0	help	par_id3149398				0	he	יש לבחור \<emph\>עיצוב - פיסקה - מסגרות\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_paragraph.xhp	0	help	par_id3156326				0	he	Select one of the default border styles in the \<emph\>Default\</emph\> area.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_paragraph.xhp	0	help	par_id3154285				0	he	Select a line style and color for the selected border style in the \<emph\>Line\</emph\> area. These settings apply to all border lines that are included in the selected border style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_paragraph.xhp	0	help	par_id3153665				0	he	Select the distance between the border lines and the page contents in the \<emph\>Spacing to contents\</emph\> area. You can only change distances to edges that have a border line defined.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_paragraph.xhp	0	help	par_id3153543				0	he	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to apply the changes.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_paragraph.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149237				0	he	Setting a Customized Border Style				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_paragraph.xhp	0	help	par_id3155388				0	he	Choose \<emph\>Format - Paragraph - Borders\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_paragraph.xhp	0	help	par_id3148943				0	he	In the \<emph\>User-defined\</emph\> area select the edge(s) that you want to appear in a common layout. Click on an edge in the preview to toggle the selection of an edge.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_paragraph.xhp	0	help	par_id3148948				0	he	Select a line style and color for the selected border style in the \<emph\>Line\</emph\> area. These settings apply to all border lines that are included in the selected border style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_paragraph.xhp	0	help	par_id3152811				0	he	Repeat the last two steps for every border edge.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_paragraph.xhp	0	help	par_id3150793				0	he	Select the distance between the border lines and the page contents in the \<emph\>Spacing to contents\</emph\> area. You can only change distances to edges that have a border line defined.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_paragraph.xhp	0	help	par_id3151178				0	he	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to apply the changes.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Copying Graphics Between Documents				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	bm_id3159201				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>drag and drop; pictures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pictures; drag and drop between documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying;pictures, between documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;pictures from other documents\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159201				0	he	\<variable id=\"dragdrop_graphic\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/dragdrop_graphic.xhp\" name=\"Copying Graphics Between Documents\"\>Copying Graphics Between Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3155805				0	he	You can copy a graphic from one document to another by drag-and-drop. If you plan to publish your document, please observe copyright laws and obtain the consent of the authors.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3147576				0	he	Open the document in which you want to insert the graphic object.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3155338				0	he	Open the document from which you want to copy the graphic.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3149182				0	he	Click the graphic while pressing the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key, to select it without executing any hyperlinks it may refer to.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3151110				0	he	Keep the mouse button pressed and wait a moment while the object is copied to an internal memory.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3149763	21			0	he	Drag the graphic into the other document. \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WIN\"\>If the documents are not visible side by side, first move the mouse pointer to the button of the target document while keeping the mouse button pressed. The document in question is then displayed and you can move the mouse pointer into the document. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3155628				0	he	Release the mouse button as soon as the gray text cursor indicates the position where you want to insert a copy of the picture.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3150276				0	he	If the graphic is connected with a hyperlink, the hyperlink and not the graphic is inserted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Comparing Versions of a Document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154788				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>documents; comparing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>comparing documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>versions; comparing documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changes;comparing to original\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>review function; comparing documents\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154788				0	he	\<variable id=\"redlining_doccompare\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/redlining_doccompare.xhp\" name=\"Comparing Versions of a Document\"\>Comparing Versions of a Document\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id4186223				0	he	The review function is available in %PRODUCTNAME for text documents and spreadsheet documents.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id3995178				0	he	Imagine you have some co-authors or reviewers who collaborate with you writing your original document. One day you send out copies of your document to all reviewers. You ask them to edit the copy and send it back.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id9948423				0	he	Normally, the reviewers enable change tracking by \<emph\>Edit - Changes - Record\</emph\> and you can easily see the changes.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id3155421				0	he	If one of the authors has made changes to a document without recording them, you can compare the changed document to your original document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id3153087				0	he	Open your original document and then choose \<emph\>Edit - Compare Document\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id4208807				0	he	You should always start with opening the newer document and compare it with the older document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id3145315				0	he	A file selection dialog appears. Select the copy of the document and confirm the dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id3149762				0	he	\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> combines both documents into your original document. All text passages that occur in your document but not in the copy are identified as having been inserted, and all text passages that are missing in your original document are identified as deletions.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id3145674				0	he	You can now accept the "insertions", in which case the relevant texts stay in their original form, or you can accept the "deletions", in which case the marked text contained in the copy is not inserted in your document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Pasting Contents in Special Formats				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	bm_id3620715				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>clipboard;pasting formatted/unformatted text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;clipboard options\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;formatted/unformatted text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text formats;pasting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formats;pasting in special formats\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10725				0	he	\<variable id=\"pasting\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/pasting.xhp\"\>Pasting Contents in Special Formats\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10743				0	he	Contents that are stored on the clipboard can be pasted into your document using different formats. In %PRODUCTNAME you can choose how to paste the contents using a dialog or a drop-down icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10746				0	he	The available options depend on the contents of the clipboard.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144547360				0	he	In Writer text documents, you can press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command+Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl+Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+V to paste the contents of the clipboard as unformatted text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10749				0	he	Pasting clipboard contents using an icon menu				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10750				0	he	Click the arrow next to the \<emph\>Paste\</emph\> icon on the Standard Bar to open the menu.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10758				0	he	Select one of the options.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1075B				0	he	If you do not like the result, click the \<emph\>Undo\</emph\> icon and then paste again with another option.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10762				0	he	Pasting clipboard contents using a dialog				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10769				0	he	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Paste special\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10771				0	he	Select one of the options and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10774				0	he	If you are in a spreadsheet and the contents of the clipboard are spreadsheet cells, then a different \<emph\>Paste Special\</emph\> dialog appears. Use the \<emph\>Paste Special\</emph\> dialog to copy cells using basic or advanced options.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077E				0	he	\<emph\>Transpose\</emph\>: swaps the rows and the columns of the cell range to be pasted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10785				0	he	\<emph\>Link\</emph\>: pastes the cell range as a link. If the source file changes, the pasted cells change also.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1078C				0	he	The other options are explained in the help, when you call the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02070000.xhp\"\>Paste Special\</link\> dialog from within %PRODUCTNAME Calc.				20200411 15:09:53
