helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_view.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Viewing a Database				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_view.xhp	0	help	bm_id2339854				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>opening;database files\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>viewing; databases\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data sources;viewing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>databases;viewing\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_view.xhp	0	help	par_idN105A6				0	he	\<variable id=\"data_view\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_view.xhp\"\>Viewing a Database\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_view.xhp	0	help	par_idN105C4				0	he	There are two different methods of viewing a database in %PRODUCTNAME.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_view.xhp	0	help	par_idN105CA				0	he	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\> to open the database file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_view.xhp	0	help	par_idN105D1				0	he	The \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/dabadoc.xhp\"\>database file\</link\> gives you full access to tables, queries, reports, and forms. You can edit the structure of your tables and change the contents of the data records.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_view.xhp	0	help	par_idN105E3				0	he	Choose \<emph\>View - Data source\</emph\> to view the registered databases.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_view.xhp	0	help	par_idN105EA				0	he	The \<link href=\"text/shared/guide/database_main.xhp\"\>data source view\</link\> can be used to drag-and-drop table fields from registered databases into your documents and to produce mail merges.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_view.xhp	0	help	par_idN10606				0	he	\<embedvar href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/main.xhp#base\"/\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_view.xhp	0	help	par_idN1060E				0	he	\<embedvar href=\"text/shared/guide/database_main.xhp#database_main\"/\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Copying Attributes With the Format Paintbrush				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	bm_id380260				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>Format Paintbrush\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>formatting;copying\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>copying;formatting\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>Paintbrush\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN1053A				0	he	\<variable id=\"formatpaintbrush\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/paintbrush.xhp\"\>Copying Formatting With the Format Paintbrush\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10655				0	he	You can use the Format Paintbrush tool to copy formatting from a text selection or from an object and apply the formatting to another text selection or object.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_id101920091122570				0	he	In Calc, the Format Paintbrush only applies to cell formatting.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106DD				0	he	Select the text or object whose formatting you want to copy.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10667				0	he	On the \<emph\>Standard Bar\</emph\>, click the \<emph\>Format Paintbrush\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10660				0	he	The cursor changes to a paint bucket.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10663				0	he	If you want to apply the formatting to more than one selection, double-click the \<emph\>Format Paintbrush\</emph\> icon\<image id=\"img_id209967\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_formatpaintbrush.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id209967\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>. After you apply all the formatting, click the icon again.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066E				0	he	Select or click the text or object that you want to apply the formatting to.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10716				0	he	To exclude paragraph formatting, hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> when you click. To exclude character formatting, hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift when you click.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10671				0	he	The following table describes the formatting attributes that the \<emph\>Format Paintbrush\</emph\> can copy:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10691				0	he	Type of Selection				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10697				0	he	Comment				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN1069E				0	he	Nothing selected, but cursor is inside a text passage				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A4				0	he	Copies the formatting of the current paragraph and the character formatting of the next character in the text flow direction.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AB				0	he	Text is selected				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B1				0	he	Copies the formatting of the last selected character and of the paragraph that contains the character.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B8				0	he	Frame is selected				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106BE				0	he	Copies the frame attributes that are defined in \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Frame\</item\> dialog. The contents, size, position, linking, hyperlinks, and macros in the frame are not copied.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106C5				0	he	Object is selected				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106CB				0	he	Copies the object formatting that is defined in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Graphics\</item\> or \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Drawing Object\</item\> dialogs. The contents, size, position, hyperlinks, and macros in the object are not copied.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D2				0	he	Form control is selected				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D8				0	he	Not supported				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106DF				0	he	Drawing object is selected				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E5				0	he	Copies all formatting attributes. In Impress and Draw, the text contents of the object is also copied.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106EC				0	he	Text within Calc cells is selected				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F2				0	he	Not supported				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F9				0	he	Writer table or cells are selected				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106FF				0	he	Copies the formatting that is specified in Table, Text Flow, Borders, and Background tab pages in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Table\</item\> dialog. The paragraph and character formatting are also copied.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10706				0	he	Calc table or cells are selected				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN1070C				0	he	Copies the formatting that is specified in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Cells\</item\> dialog as well as the formatting of the cell contents				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\workfolder.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Changing Your Work Directory				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\workfolder.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150789				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>work directory change\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>My Documents folder;changing work directory\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>paths; changing work directory\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pictures; changing paths\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;work directory\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\workfolder.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149346				0	he	\<variable id=\"workfolder\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/workfolder.xhp\" name=\"Changing Your Working Directory\"\>Changing Your Working Directory\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\workfolder.xhp	0	help	par_id3150774				0	he	When you start a dialog to open or save a document, $[officename] initially displays your work directory. To change this directory:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\workfolder.xhp	0	help	par_id3153681				0	he	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - $[officename] - Paths\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\workfolder.xhp	0	help	par_id3163802	5			0	he	Click \<emph\>My Documents \</emph\>and click the\<emph\> Edit button, or \</emph\>double-click on \<emph\>My Documents\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\workfolder.xhp	0	help	par_id3153880				0	he	In the \<emph\>Select Path\</emph\> dialog, choose the work directory you want and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\workfolder.xhp	0	help	par_id3158430				0	he	You also use this procedure to change the directory displayed by $[officename] when you want to insert a graphic. Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - $[officename] - Paths - Graphics\</emph\>, then follow step 3.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\workfolder.xhp	0	help	par_id3154286				0	he	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010300.xhp\" name=\"Paths\"\>Paths\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Working with Groups 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	bm_id6888027				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>groups;entering/exiting/ungrouping\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>frames; selection frames\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>selecting;objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exiting;groups\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>entering groups\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>ungrouping groups\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>selection frames\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>multiple selection\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>marking, see selecting\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	hd_id2454298				0	he	\<variable id=\"groups\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/groups.xhp\"\>Working with Groups\</link\> \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id2307199				0	he	You can combine several graphic objects into a group so that you can use them like a single object. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id9983825				0	he	You can move, transform, resize, distort, or convert all objects in a group together, and you can enter the group any time to change the individual objects. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id5734733				0	he	You can change the properties (line size, fill color, and more) of all objects in a group together, and you can enter the group and change the individual objects. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id561540				0	he	Groups can also be nested to form groups within other groups. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	hd_id7705618				0	he	To group objects				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id607013				0	he	Select the objects together that you want to group. Hold down Shift while you click the individual objects.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id1399578				0	he	Right-click any of the selected objects to open the context menu. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id598162				0	he	In Impress or Draw, choose Group. In Calc or Writer, choose Group – Group.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id6738792				0	he	To select the objects, you can also drag a selection frame around the objects.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id7309793				0	he	For example, you can group all of the objects in a company logo to move and resize the logo as a single object.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id1227759				0	he	After you have grouped objects, selecting any part of the group selects the entire group.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	hd_id7424237				0	he	To enter a group				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id1388592				0	he	Right-click any object of the group.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id343943				0	he	In Impress or Draw, choose Enter Group. In Calc or Writer, choose Group - Edit Group.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id8726767				0	he	Now you can select and edit a single object in the group.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id691549				0	he	You can add or delete objects to and from a group in this mode. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id9909665				0	he	The objects that are not part of the group are shown with dimmed colors.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	hd_id9141819				0	he	To exit a group				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id6354869				0	he	Right-click any object of the group.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id2685323				0	he	In Impress or Draw, choose Exit Group. In Calc or Writer, choose Group - Exit Group.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id6042664				0	he	To exit a group in Draw or Impress, you can also double-click anywhere outside the group.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	hd_id7889950				0	he	To ungroup a group				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3236182				0	he	Right-click any object of the group.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id1251258				0	he	In Impress or Draw, choose Ungroup. In Calc or Writer, choose Group - Ungroup.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id8111819				0	he	Now you can select and edit all objects as individual objects.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Applying Digital Signatures				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	bm_id7430951				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>signing documents with digital signatures\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>digital signatures;getting/managing/applying\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	hd_id344248				0	he	\<variable id=\"digitalsign_send\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/digitalsign_send.xhp\"\>Applying Digital Signatures\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN1063C				0	he	Getting a Certificate				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN10640				0	he	You can get a certificate from a certification authority, which may be a private company or a governmental institution. Some certification authorities want money for their service, for example when they certify your identity. Other certificates are free of costs, for example those offered by some e-mail providers, which certify your e-mail address. A few of the companies that offer certificates to private persons are listed in the following, in alphabetical order: \<link href=\"http://www.globalsign.net\"\>GlobalSign\</link\>, \<link href=\"http://www.verisign.com\"\>Verisign\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F6				0	he	Managing your Certificates				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN1070A				0	he	If you are using Microsoft Windows, you can manage your certificates from the Control Panel applet "Internet Options" on the "Contents" tab page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_id8311410				0	he	Import your new root certificate into the Trusted Root Certification Authorities list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN1071D				0	he	If you are using Solaris or Linux, you must install a recent version of Thunderbird, Mozilla Suite, or Firefox software to install some system files that are needed for encryption.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN10720				0	he	If you have created different profiles in Thunderbird, Mozilla, or Firefox, and you want %PRODUCTNAME to use one specified profile for certificates, then you can set the environment variable MOZILLA_CERTIFICATE_FOLDER to point to the folder of that specified profile.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_id944242				0	he	Open your Web browser's preferences dialog, select the Privacy & Security tab page, click on Certificates - Manage Certificates. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_id6452223				0	he	Import your new root certificate, then select and edit the certificate. Enable the root certificate to be trusted at least for web and email access. This ensures that the certificate can sign your documents. You may edit any intermediate certificate in the same way, but it is not mandatory for signing documents.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_id6486098				0	he	When you have edited the new certificates, restart %PRODUCTNAME.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN10681				0	he	Signing a document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN10688				0	he	Choose \<emph\>File - Digital Signatures\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN10690				0	he	A message box advises you to save the document. Click \<emph\>Yes\</emph\> to save the file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN10698				0	he	After saving, you see the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/digitalsignatures.xhp\"\>Digital Signatures\</link\> dialog. Click \<emph\>Add\</emph\> to add a public key to the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AE				0	he	In the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/selectcertificate.xhp\"\>Select Certificate\</link\> dialog, select your certificate and click OK. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN106C0				0	he	You see again the Digital Signatures dialog, where you can add more certificates if you want. Click OK to add the public key to the saved file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN106C3				0	he	A signed document shows an icon \<image id=\"img_id262764\" src=\"xmlsecurity/res/certificate_16.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id262764\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> in the status bar. You can double-click the icon in the status bar to view the certificate.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_id2008200911381426				0	he	The result of the signature validation is displayed in the status bar and within the Digital Signature dialog. Several documents and macro signatures can exist inside an ODF document. If there is a problem with one signature, then the validation result of that one signature is assumed for all signatures. That is, if there are ten valid signatures and one invalid signature, then the status bar and the status field in the dialog will flag the signature as invalid.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E0				0	he	Signing the macros inside a document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E4				0	he	Normally, macros are part of a document. If you sign a document, the macros inside the document are signed automatically. If you want to sign only the macros, but not the document, proceed as follows:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN106EA				0	he	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Macros - Digital Signature\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F2				0	he	Apply the signature as described above for documents.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F5				0	he	When you open the Basic IDE that contains signed macros, you see an icon \<image id=\"img_id9252296\" src=\"xmlsecurity/res/certificate_16.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id9252296\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> in the status bar. You can double-click the icon in the status bar to view the certificate.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_id5734733				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click to open the View Certificate dialog.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_id561540				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Choose this setting to accept the certificate until you exit %PRODUCTNAME.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
