helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_idN108FE				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_HELP_TOOLBOXITEM_SEARCHDIALOG\"\>Opens the \<emph\>Find on this page\</emph\> dialog\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_id3154366				0	he	These commands can also be found in the context menu of the Help document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_idN10922				0	he	Help Page				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_idN10926				0	he	You can copy from the Help Viewer to the clipboard on your operating system with standard copy commands. For example:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_idN1092C				0	he	On a Help page, select the text that you want to copy.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_idN10930				0	he	Press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+C.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_idN10933				0	he	To search the current Help page:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_idN10939				0	he	Click the \<emph\>Find on this Page\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_idN10940				0	he	The \<emph\>Find on this Page\</emph\> dialog opens.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A36				0	he	You can also click in the Help page and press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+F.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A22				0	he	In the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> box, enter the text that you want to find.				20200411 15:09:53
