helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151054				0	he	New Dictionary				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3153360				0	he	In the \<emph\>Dictionary\</emph\> section you can name a new user-defined dictionary or dictionary of exceptions and specify the language.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150398				0	he	Name				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3153192				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:EDIT:RID_SFXDLG_NEWDICT:ED_DICTNAME\"\>Specifies the name of the new custom dictionary.\</ahelp\> The file extension "*.DIC" is automatically appended.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150767				0	he	Language				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3148920				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:LISTBOX:RID_SFXDLG_NEWDICT:LB_DICTLANG\"\>By selecting a certain language you can limit the use of the custom dictionary.\</ahelp\> By selecting \<emph\>All\</emph\> the custom dictionary is used independently of the current language.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153106				0	he	Exceptions (-)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3149561				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:CHECKBOX:RID_SFXDLG_NEWDICT:BTN_EXCEPT\"\>Specifies whether you wish to avoid certain words in your documents.\</ahelp\> In this way, you can create a custom dictionary of all the words to be avoided. If this exception dictionary is activated, during spellchecking you receive a corresponding note about any words which should be avoided.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145785				0	he	Edit				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3152576				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_PUSHBUTTON_RID_SFXPAGE_LINGU_PB_LINGU_DICS_EDIT_DIC\"\>Opens the \<emph\>Edit custom dictionary\</emph\> dialog, in which you can add to your custom dictionary or edit existing entries.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3147436	75			0	he	In the \<emph\>Edit custom dictionary \</emph\>dialog you have the option to enter new terms or edit existing entries. If you edit an exception dictionary, the dialog has the added facility of defining an exception for a word. During the spellcheck this exception is then listed as a suggestion.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3145750	76			0	he	When a dictionary is edited, a check is made on the status of the file. If the file is write-protected, it cannot be changed. The buttons \<emph\>New\</emph\> and \<emph\>Delete\</emph\> are then deactivated. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150116				0	he	Book				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3147394				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:LISTBOX:RID_SFXDLG_EDITDICT:LB_ALLDICTS\"\>Specifies the book to be edited.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3154730	79			0	he	\<variable id=\"ignore\"\>The \<emph\>IgnoreAllList (All) \</emph\>includes all words that have been marked with \<emph\>Ignore\</emph\> during spellcheck. This list is valid only for the current spellcheck. \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3154757				0	he	The \<emph\>IgnoreAllList\</emph\> entry cannot be selected and cannot be deleted. Only the words included as content can be deleted. This happens automatically each time that $[officename] is closed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149018				0	he	Language				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3154255				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:LISTBOX:RID_SFXDLG_EDITDICT:LB_DICTLANG\"\>Assigns a new language to the current custom dictionary.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151189				0	he	Word				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3151252				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:EDIT:RID_SFXDLG_EDITDICT:ED_WORD\"\>You can type a new word for inclusion in the dictionary. In the list below you will see the contents of the current custom dictionary.\</ahelp\> If you select a word from this list it is displayed in the text field. If you type a word with a trailing = character, such as "AutoComplete=", the word is never automatically hyphenated and no hyphenation is suggested. Typing "Auto=Complete" results in the word being hyphenated, or a hyphenation suggested, where you insert the = sign.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155175				0	he	Suggestion				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3147323				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:EDIT:RID_SFXDLG_EDITDICT:ED_REPLACE\"\>This input field is only available if you are editing an exception dictionary. The field shows the alternative suggestion for the current word in the "Word" text box.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147361				0	he	New				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3163808	89			0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:PUSHBUTTON:RID_SFXDLG_EDITDICT:PB_NEW_REPLACE\"\>Adds the word in the \<emph\>Word \</emph\>text field to your current custom dictionary. The word in the \<emph\>Suggestion \</emph\>field is also added when working with exception dictionaries.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3145790				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Removes the marked word from the current custom dictionary.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3151277				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Deletes the selected dictionary after a confirmation, provided it is not write-protected.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149032				0	he	Options				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3145259				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_CLB_LINGU_OPTIONS\"\>Defines the options for the spellcheck and hyphenation.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149965				0	he	Edit				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3153231				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_PUSHBUTTON_RID_SFXPAGE_LINGU_PB_LINGU_OPTIONS_EDIT\"\>If you want to change a value, select the entry and then click \<emph\>Edit\</emph\>.\</ahelp\> You will see a dialog for entering a new value.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150983				0	he	Check uppercase words				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3152582				0	he	Specifies that capitalization is checked during spellcheck.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150826				0	he	Check words with numbers.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3150208				0	he	Specifies that words that contain numbers as well as letters are to be checked.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147509				0	he	Check capitalization				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3154200				0	he	Checks for the correct use of capitals at the start of words during spellcheck.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166424				0	he	Check special regions				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3150345				0	he	Specifies that special regions, such as text in headers and footers, document tables, and text frames, are checked during spellcheck.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166429				0	he	Check spelling as you type				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3155531				0	he	\<variable id=\"automatisch\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:SpellOnline\"\>Automatically checks spelling as you type, and underlines errors.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3156291				0	he	Typing errors are highlighted in the document with a red underline. If you place the cursor over a word marked in this way, you can open the context menu to obtain a list of corrections. Select a correction to replace the word. If you make the same mistake again while editing the document, it will be marked as an error again.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3153815				0	he	To place the word pair in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040200.xhp\" name=\"AutoCorrect replacement table\"\>AutoCorrect replacement table\</link\>, open the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040500.xhp\" name=\"AutoCorrect context menu\"\>AutoCorrect context menu\</link\> and choose \<emph\>AutoCorrect\</emph\>. Make your selection from the submenu. The word is replaced and at the same time the word pair is placed in the replacement table.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150111	53			0	he	Minimal number of characters for hyphenation 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3150316				0	he	Specifies the minimum number of characters required for automatic hyphenation to be applied. \<ahelp hid=\"HID_LNGDLG_NUM_PREBREAK\" visibility=\"hidden\"\> Type the minimum number of characters that must come before or after the hyphen.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148823				0	he	Characters before line break				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3156029				0	he	Sets the minimum number of characters of the word to be hyphenated that must remain at the end of the line.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154956				0	he	Characters after line break				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3149439				0	he	Specifies the minimum number of characters of a hyphenated word required at the next line.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156337				0	he	Hyphenate without inquiry				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3151130				0	he	Specifies that you will never be asked for a manual hyphenation. If the field is not marked, when a word is not recognized you will be presented with a dialog for entering hyphens.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155900				0	he	Hyphenate special regions				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3155098				0	he	Specifies that hyphenation will also be carried out in footnotes, headers and footers.				20200411 15:09:53
