helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3153707	28			0	he	         \<emph\>Example:\</emph\> Type the text 'Test' in cell A1; and the text 'test' in B1. Then type the formula "=A1=B1" in cell C1. If the \<emph\>Case sensitive\</emph\> box is marked, FALSE will appear in the cell; otherwise, TRUE will appear in the cell.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3153965				0	he	The EXACT text function is always case-sensitive, independent of the settings in this dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145231				0	he	Decimal places				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3149568				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:NUMERICFIELD:RID_SCPAGE_CALC:ED_PREC\"\>Defines the number of decimals to be displayed for numbers with the \<emph\>Standard\</emph\> number format. The numbers are displayed as rounded numbers, but are not saved as rounded numbers.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145150				0	he	Precision as shown				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3150644				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCPAGE_CALC:BTN_CALC\"\>Specifies whether to make calculations using the rounded values displayed in the sheet. Charts will be shown with the displayed values. If the \<emph\>Precision as shown\</emph\> option is not marked, the displayed numbers are rounded, but they are calculated internally using the non-rounded number.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152581				0	he	Search criteria = and <> must apply to whole cells				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3149211				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCPAGE_CALC:BTN_MATCH\"\>Specifies that the search criteria you set for the Calc database functions must match the whole cell exactly. When the \<emph\>Search criteria = and <> must apply to whole cells\</emph\> box is marked, $[officename] Calc behaves exactly as MS Excel when searching cells in the database functions.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
