helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01130100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145582				0	he	Microsoft Word 97/2000				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149762				0	he	Select the settings for Microsoft Word 97/2000 documents.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01130100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155420				0	he	Load Basic code to edit				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3159399	6			0	he	\<variable id=\"codetext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\"OFFMGR:CHECKBOX:RID_OFAPAGE_MSFILTEROPT:CB_WBAS_CODE\"\>Loads and saves the Basic code from a Microsoft document as a special $[officename] Basic module with the document. The disabled Microsoft Basic code is visible in the $[officename] Basic IDE between \<emph\>Sub\</emph\> and \<emph\>End Sub\</emph\>.\</ahelp\> You can edit the code. When saving the document in $[officename] format, the Basic code is saved as well. When saving in another format, the Basic code from the $[officename] Basic IDE is not saved. \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01130100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153824				0	he	Save original Basic code again				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150084				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"OFFMGR:CHECKBOX:RID_OFAPAGE_MSFILTEROPT:CB_WBAS_STG\"\>Specifies that the original Microsoft Basic code contained in the document is held in a special internal memory for as long as the document remains loaded in $[officename]. When saving the document in Microsoft format the Microsoft Basic is saved again with the code in an unchanged form.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153088				0	he	When saving in another format than Microsoft Format, the Microsoft Basic Code is not saved. For example, if the document contains Microsoft Basic Code and you save it in $[officename] format, you will be warned that the Microsoft Basic Code will not be saved.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3151246				0	he	The \<emph\>Save original Basic code again\</emph\> checkbox takes precedence over the \<emph\>Load Basic code to edit\</emph\> check box. If both boxes are marked and you edit the disabled Basic Code in the $[officename] Basic IDE, the original Microsoft Basic code will be saved when saving in the Microsoft format. A message appears to inform you of this.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148946	19			0	he	To remove any possible Microsoft Basic macro viruses from the Microsoft document, unmark the \<emph\>Save Original Basic Code again\</emph\> check box and save the document in Microsoft format. The document will be saved without the Microsoft Basic code.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01130100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154924				0	he	Microsoft Excel 97/2000				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149457				0	he	Specifies the settings for documents in Microsoft Excel 97/2000.				20200411 15:09:53
