helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040700.xhp	0	help	par_id3149416				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_REDLINE_OPT\"\>Defines the appearance of changes in the document.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040700.xhp	0	help	par_id3156153				0	he	To record or show changes in your text or spreadsheet document, choose \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02230000.xhp\" name=\"Edit - Changes\"\>\<emph\>Edit - Changes - Record\</emph\>\</link\> or \<emph\>Edit - Changes - Show\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040700.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155419				0	he	Text display				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040700.xhp	0	help	par_id3144510				0	he	Defines the settings for displaying recorded changes. Select the type of change with the radio buttons, and the corresponding display attribute and color. The preview field shows the effect of the selected display options.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040700.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148550				0	he	Insertions / Attributes				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040700.xhp	0	help	par_id3154758				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_LISTBOX_TP_REDLINE_OPT_LB_INS_ATTR\"\>Specifies how changes in the document are displayed when text is inserted.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040700.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152812				0	he	Deletions / Attributes				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040700.xhp	0	help	par_id3154365				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_LISTBOX_TP_REDLINE_OPT_LB_DEL_ATTR\"\>Specifies how changes in the document are displayed when text is deleted. If you record text deletions, the text is displayed with the selected attribute (for example, strikethrough) and is not deleted.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040700.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148674				0	he	Changed attributes / Attributes				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040700.xhp	0	help	par_id3151042				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_LISTBOX_TP_REDLINE_OPT_LB_CHG_ATTR\"\>Defines how changes to text attributes are displayed in the document. These changes affect attributes such as bold, italic or underline.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040700.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153105				0	he	Color				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040700.xhp	0	help	par_id3145419				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_LISTBOX_TP_REDLINE_OPT_LB_CHG_COL\"\>You can also choose a color to display each type of recorded change. When you choose the condition "By author" in the list, the color is automatically determined by $[officename], then modified to match to the author of each change.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040700.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145607				0	he	Lines changed				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040700.xhp	0	help	par_id3149562				0	he	To indicate which lines of the text have been changed, you can define a mark that appears in the left or right page margin.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040700.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145785				0	he	Mark				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040700.xhp	0	help	par_id3154638				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:TP_REDLINE_OPT:LB_MARKPOS\"\>Defines if and where changed lines in the document are marked.\</ahelp\> You can set the markings so that they always appear on the left or right page margin, or on the outer or inner margin.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040700.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163713				0	he	Color				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01040700.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:TP_REDLINE_OPT:LB_LC_COL\"\>Specifies the color for highlighting the changed lines in the text.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010900.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Print Options				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010900.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147323				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>printing; colors in grayscale\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>grayscale printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>colors; printing in grayscale\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>printing; warnings\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>paper size warning\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010900.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148946				0	he	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010900.xhp\" name=\"Print Options\"\>Print Options\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010900.xhp	0	help	par_id3150359				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Specifies the print setting options.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010900.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148451				0	he	Reduce print data				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010900.xhp	0	help	par_id3154910				0	he	You can reduce the amount of data to be sent to the printer. Reducing the print data increases the print speed because the print files are smaller. This makes it easier for printers with a smaller memory to print. Reducing print data can result in slightly lower print quality.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010900.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147085				0	he	Settings for				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010900.xhp	0	help	par_id3158407				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"SFX2_RADIOBUTTON_TP_COMMONPRINTOPTIONS_RB_PRINTFILEOUTPUT\"\>Specifies whether the print settings apply to direct printing or to printing to a file.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010900.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145786				0	he	Reduce transparency				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010900.xhp	0	help	par_id3159154				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"SFX2_CHECKBOX_TP_COMMONPRINTOPTIONS_CB_REDUCETRANSPARENCY\"\>If you mark this field the transparent objects will be printed like normal, non-transparent objects, depending on your selection in the following two option buttons.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010900.xhp	0	help	par_id3156444				0	he	Transparency cannot be output directly to a printer. The areas of the document in which transparency is to be visible must therefore always be calculated as bitmaps and sent to the printer. Depending on the size of the bitmaps and the print resolution a large amount of data may result.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010900.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147441				0	he	Automatically				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010900.xhp	0	help	par_id3150488				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"SFX2_RADIOBUTTON_TP_COMMONPRINTOPTIONS_RB_REDUCETRANSPARENCY_AUTO\"\>Specifies that the transparency is only printed if the transparent area covers less than a quarter of the entire page.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010900.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149417				0	he	No transparency				20200411 15:09:53
