helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040300.xhp	0	help	par_id3152876				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_OFAPAGE_AUTOCORR_EXCEPT\"\>Specify the abbreviations or letter combinations that you do not want $[officename] to correct automatically.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040300.xhp	0	help	par_id3154926				0	he	The exceptions that you define depend on the current language setting. If you want, you can change the language setting by selecting a different language in the \<emph\>Replacements and exceptions for language\</emph\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149205				0	he	Replacements and exceptions for language:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040300.xhp	0	help	par_id3156027				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AUTOCORR_LANGUAGE\"\>Select the language for which you want to create or edit the replacement rules.\</ahelp\> $[officename] first searches for exceptions that are defined for the language at the current cursor position in the document, and then searches the remaining languages.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153681				0	he	Abbreviations (no subsequent capital)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040300.xhp	0	help	par_id3156410				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"OFFMGR:EDIT:RID_OFAPAGE_AUTOCORR_EXCEPT:ED_ABBREV\"\>Type an abbreviation followed by a period, and then click \<emph\>New\</emph\>. This prevents $[officename] from automatically capitalizing the first letter of the word that comes after the period at the end of the abbreviation.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040300.xhp	0	help	par_id3149751				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"OFFMGR:LISTBOX:RID_OFAPAGE_AUTOCORR_EXCEPT:LB_ABBREV\"\>Lists the abbreviations that are not automatically corrected.\</ahelp\> To remove an item from the list, select the item, and then click \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151110				0	he	Words with TWo INitial CApitals				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040300.xhp	0	help	par_id3154749				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"OFFMGR:EDIT:RID_OFAPAGE_AUTOCORR_EXCEPT:ED_DOUBLE_CAPS\"\>Type the word or abbreviation that starts with two capital letters that you do not want $[officename] to change to one initial capital. For example, enter PC to prevent $[officename] from changing PC to Pc.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040300.xhp	0	help	par_id3143271				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"OFFMGR:LISTBOX:RID_OFAPAGE_AUTOCORR_EXCEPT:LB_DOUBLE_CAPS\"\>Lists the words or abbreviations that start with two initial capitals that are not automatically corrected. All words which start with two capital letters are listed in the field.\</ahelp\> To remove an item from the list, select the item, and then click \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
