helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\xformsdatatab.xhp	0	help	par_id2107303				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Click the button to open a dialog where you can enter the name of a new user-defined data type. The new data type inherits all facets from the currently selected data type.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\xformsdatatab.xhp	0	help	par_id4071779				0	he	The following lists all facets that are valid for data types. Some facets are only available for some data types.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\xformsdatatab.xhp	0	help	hd_id4313791				0	he	Whitespaces				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\xformsdatatab.xhp	0	help	par_id4331797				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Specifies how whitespaces are to be handled when a string of the current data type is being processed. Possible values are Preserve, Replace, and Collapse. The sematics follow the definition at http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#rf-whiteSpace.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\xformsdatatab.xhp	0	help	hd_id4191717				0	he	Pattern				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\xformsdatatab.xhp	0	help	par_id2318796				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Specifies a regular expression pattern. Strings validated against the data type must conform to this pattern to be valid. The XSD data type syntax for regular expressions is different from the regular expression syntax used elseswhere in %PRODUCTNAME, for example in the Find & Replace dialog.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
