helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\01020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145367	40			0	he	            \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> recognizes templates that are located in any directory from the following list:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\01020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151292				0	he	the shared template directory				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\01020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3144442				0	he	the user template directory \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>in the home directory\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>in the Documents and Settings directory\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\01020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146905				0	he	all template folders as defined in \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010300.xhp\" name=\"%PRODUCTNAME - Paths\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Paths\</link\>\</emph\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\01020000.xhp	0	help	par_id7375713				0	he	When you use \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Template - Save\</item\> to save a template, the template will be stored in your user template directory. When you open a document that is based on such a template, the document will be checked for a changed template as described below. The template is associated with the document, it may be called a "sticky template".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\01020000.xhp	0	help	par_id6930143				0	he	When you use \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Save As\</item\> and select a template filter to save a template at any other directory that is not in the list, then the documents based on that template will not be checked.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\01020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150105				0	he	When you open a document that was created from a "sticky template" (as defined above), \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> checks to see if the template has been modified since the document was last opened. If the template was changed a dialog is shown where you can select which styles to apply to the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\01020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153096				0	he	To apply the new styles from the template to the document, click \<emph\>Yes\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\01020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147581				0	he	To retain the styles that are currently used in the document, click \<emph\>No\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\01020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154988				0	he	If a document was created using a template that cannot be found a dialog is shown that asks you how to proceed next time the document is opened.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\01020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151351				0	he	To break the link between the document and the missing template, click \<emph\>No\</emph\>, otherwise \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> will look for the template the next time you open the document.				20200411 15:09:53
