helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\03020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149495				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:FunctionBarVisible\"\>Shows or hides the \<emph\>Standard Bar\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Number Format Codes				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153514				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>numbers; format codes for time, date and currency\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>format codes; numbers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>conditions; in number formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>number formats; codes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>currency formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formats;of currencies/date/time\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>numbers; date, time and currency formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Euro; currency formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>date formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formats; date formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>time formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formats; time formats\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153514				0	he	\<variable id=\"zahlenformatcodes\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020301.xhp\" name=\"Number Format Codes\"\>Number Format Codes\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3150467				0	he	Number format codes can consist of up to three sections separated by a semicolon (;).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3150146				0	he	In a number format code with two sections, the first section applies to positive values and zero, and the second section applies to negative values.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3158442				0	he	In a number format code with three sections, the first section applies to positive values, the second section to negative values, and the third section to the value zero.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3155069				0	he	You can also assign conditions to the three sections, so that the format is only applied if a condition is met.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151262				0	he	Decimal Places and Significant Digits				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3153624	3			0	he	Use zero (0) or the number sign (#) as placeholders in your number format code to represent numbers. The (#) only displays significant digits, while the (0) displays zeroes if there are fewer digits in the number than in the number format.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3153323				0	he	Use question marks (?) to represent the number of digits to include in the numerator and the denominator of a fraction. Fractions that do not fit the pattern that you define are displayed as floating point numbers.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3148440				0	he	If a number contains more digits to the right of the decimal delimiter than there are placeholders in the format, the number is rounded accordingly. If a number contains more digits to the left of the decimal delimiter than there are placeholders in the format, the entire number is displayed. Use the following list as a guide for using placeholders when you create a number format code:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3150902				0	he	Placeholders				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3157896				0	he	Explanation				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3152801				0	he	#				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3145090				0	he	Does not display extra zeros.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088				0	he	0 (Zero)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3150774				0	he	Displays extra zeros if the number has less places than zeros in the format.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_idN1087E				0	he	Examples				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3149182				0	he	Number Format				20200411 15:09:53
