helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\packagemanager.xhp	0	help	par_idN10553				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"42772\"\>The Extension Manager adds, removes, disables, enables, and updates %PRODUCTNAME extensions.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\packagemanager.xhp	0	help	par_idN10615				0	he	The following are examples of %PRODUCTNAME extensions:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\packagemanager.xhp	0	help	par_idN1061B				0	he	UNO components (compiled software modules)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\packagemanager.xhp	0	help	par_idN1061F				0	he	Configuration data (for menu commands)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\packagemanager.xhp	0	help	par_idN10623				0	he	%PRODUCTNAME Basic libraries				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\packagemanager.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E8				0	he	%PRODUCTNAME dialog libraries				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\packagemanager.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F5				0	he	Extension files (*.oxt files containing one or more extensions of the above listed types)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\packagemanager.xhp	0	help	hd_id8570513				0	he	Extension Scope				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\packagemanager.xhp	0	help	par_idN1068A				0	he	The availability of an extension depends on the location where you add the extension.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\packagemanager.xhp	0	help	par_idN10626				0	he	A user with root or administrator privileges can install an extension as a shared extension that is available to all users. After selecting an extension, a dialog opens and asks whether to install for the current user or all users.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\packagemanager.xhp	0	help	par_idN1069C				0	he	Extensions that you add to "My Extensions" can only be used and managed by yourself.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\packagemanager.xhp	0	help	hd_id3895382				0	he	To install an extension				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\packagemanager.xhp	0	help	par_id9143955				0	he	An extension is available as a file with the file extension *.oxt. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\packagemanager.xhp	0	help	par_id7857905				0	he	You can find a collection of extensions on the Web. Click the "Get more extensions here" link in the Extension Manager to open your Web browser and see the \<link href=\"https://extensions.openoffice.org/\"\>https://extensions.openoffice.org/\</link\> page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\packagemanager.xhp	0	help	hd_id5016937				0	he	To install an extension for the current user				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\packagemanager.xhp	0	help	par_id1856440				0	he	Do any of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\packagemanager.xhp	0	help	par_id7654347				0	he	Double-click the *.oxt file in your system's file browser.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\packagemanager.xhp	0	help	par_id5269020				0	he	On a Web page, click a hyperlink to an *.oxt file (if your Web browser can be configured to start the Extension Manager for this file type).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\packagemanager.xhp	0	help	par_id8714255				0	he	Choose Tools - Extension Manager and click Add.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\packagemanager.xhp	0	help	hd_id3734550				0	he	To install a shared extension in text mode (for system administrators)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\packagemanager.xhp	0	help	par_id4139225				0	he	As a user with administrator rights, open a terminal or command shell.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\packagemanager.xhp	0	help	par_id671712				0	he	Change to the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WIN\"\>\\ \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>/\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>program folder in your installation.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\packagemanager.xhp	0	help	par_id4163945				0	he	Enter the following command, using the path and file name of your extension:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\packagemanager.xhp	0	help	par_id9581591				0	he	\<item type=\"literal\"\>unopkg add \</item\>\<item type=\"literal\"\>--shared \</item\>\<item type=\"literal\"\>path_filename.oxt\</item\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\packagemanager.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AD				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"42769\"\>Select the extension that you want to remove, enable, or disable. For some extensions, you can also open an Options dialog.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\packagemanager.xhp	0	help	par_idN10639				0	he	Add				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\packagemanager.xhp	0	help	par_idN106BA				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"2180256276\"\>Click Add to add an extension.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\packagemanager.xhp	0	help	par_idN106BD				0	he	A file dialog opens where you can select the extensions that you want to add. To copy and to register the selected extensions, click Open.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\packagemanager.xhp	0	help	par_id4856410				0	he	An extension can show a license dialog. \<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Read the license. Click the Scroll Down button to scroll down if necessary. Click Accept to continue the installation of the extension.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\packagemanager.xhp	0	help	par_idN10643				0	he	Remove				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\packagemanager.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D1				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"2180256277\"\>Select the extension that you want to remove, and then click Remove.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\packagemanager.xhp	0	help	par_id0523200810573866				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enable or disable the extension.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
