helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\main.xhp	0	help	par_idN10579				0	he	\<variable id=\"base\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/main.xhp\"\>שימוש במסדי-נתונים ב-‎%PRODUCTNAME Base‎\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\main.xhp	0	help	par_idN107BD				0	he	In %PRODUCTNAME Base, you can access data that is stored in a wide variety of database file formats. %PRODUCTNAME Base natively supports some flat file database formats, such as the dBase format. You can also use %PRODUCTNAME Base to connect to external relational databases, such as databases from MySQL or Oracle.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\main.xhp	0	help	par_id5864131				0	he	The following database types are read-only types in %PRODUCTNAME Base. From within %PRODUCTNAME Base it is not possible to change the database structure or to edit, insert, and delete database records for these database types:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\main.xhp	0	help	par_id8865016				0	he	Spreadsheet files				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\main.xhp	0	help	par_id3786736				0	he	Text files				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\main.xhp	0	help	par_id6747337				0	he	Address book data				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\main.xhp	0	help	par_idN107C0				0	he	Using a Database in %PRODUCTNAME				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\main.xhp	0	help	par_idN10838				0	he	To create a new database file, choose \<emph\>File - New - Database\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\main.xhp	0	help	par_idN1083B				0	he	The \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/dabawiz00.xhp\"\>Database Wizard\</link\> helps you to create a database file and to register a new database within %PRODUCTNAME.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\main.xhp	0	help	par_idN107E7				0	he	The database file contains queries, reports, and forms for the database as well as a link to the database where the records are stored. Formatting information is also stored in the database file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\main.xhp	0	help	par_idN1084A				0	he	To open a database file, choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\>. In the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> list box, select to view only \<item type=\"literal\"\>Database documents\</item\>. Select a database document and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
