helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\tablewizard00.xhp	0	help	par_idN1055C				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>The Table Wizard helps you to create a database table.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\tablewizard00.xhp	0	help	par_idN105AF				0	he	\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/tablewizard01.xhp\" name=\"Table Wizard - Select fields\"\>אשף הטבלאות - בחירת שדות\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Relations				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154015				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>join properties (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>link properties in relational databases (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inner joins (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>joins in databases (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>left joins (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>right joins (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>full joins (Base)\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154015				0	he	Relations				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	par_id3151205				0	he	If you double-click a connection between two linked fields in the query design, or if you choose \<emph\>Insert - New Relation\</emph\>, the \<emph\>Relations\</emph\> dialog appears. These properties will be used in all queries created in the future.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155066				0	he	Tables involved				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153924				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_QRY_RIGHT_TABLE\"\>Specifies two different tables that you want to join.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155766				0	he	Fields involved				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148994				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Specifies two data fields that will be joined by a relation.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159267				0	he	Options				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147340				0	he	Type				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	par_id3152482				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_QRY_JOINTYPE\"\>Specifies the link type of the selected link.\</ahelp\> Some databases support only a subset of the possible types.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155334				0	he	Inner Join				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155936				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_QRY_JOINTYPE\"\>With the internal join, the results table contains only the records for which the content of the linked fields is the same.\</ahelp\> In $[officename] SQL this type of link is created by a corresponding WHERE clause.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156372				0	he	Left Join				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	par_id3166450				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_QRY_JOINTYPE\"\>With the left join, the results table contains all fields of the left table and only those fields of the right table for which the content of the linked fields is the same.\</ahelp\> In $[officename] SQL this type of link corresponds to the LEFT OUTER JOIN command.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155607				0	he	Right Join				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150647				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_QRY_JOINTYPE\"\>With the right join, the results table contains all fields of the right table and only those fields of the left table for which the content of the linked fields is the same.\</ahelp\> In $[officename] SQL this type of link corresponds to the RIGHT OUTER JOIN command.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158215				0	he	Full Join				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	par_id3163665				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_QRY_JOINTYPE\"\>For a full join, the results table contains all fields of the left and right tables.\</ahelp\> In the SQL of $[officename] this type of link corresponds to the FULL OUTER JOIN command.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	hd_id0305200912031976				0	he	Natural				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	par_id0305200912031977				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Inserts the keyword NATURAL into the SQL statement that defines the relation. The relation joins all columns that have the same column name in both tables. The resulting joined table contains only one column for each pair of equally named columns.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\querywizard05.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Query Wizard - Grouping				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\querywizard05.xhp	0	help	par_idN10546				0	he	\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/querywizard05.xhp\"\>Query Wizard - Grouping\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\querywizard05.xhp	0	help	par_idN10556				0	he	Specifies whether to group the query. The data source must support the SQL statement "Order by clauses" to enable this page of the Wizard.				20200411 15:09:53
