helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id5091708				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>In the context menu of the Report Navigator, you see the same commands as in the Report Builder view, plus additional commands to create new functions or to delete them.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id9449446				0	he	Functions can be entered using a syntax as specified by the \<link href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OpenFormula\"\>OpenFormula\</link\> proposal.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id4095583				0	he	See \<link href=\"https://wiki.openoffice.org/wiki/Database\"\>Wiki page about Base\</link\> for some more help regarding the functions in a report.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	hd_id311593				0	he	To calculate a sum for each client				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id3948789				0	he	Open the Report Navigator.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id5391399				0	he	Open the Groups entry and the group where you want to calculate the cost. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id6989654				0	he	The group has a sub entry called functions. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id1803643				0	he	Open the context menu (right click) on the functions entry, choose to create a new function, and select it. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id868251				0	he	In the property browser you see the function. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id6247749				0	he	Change the name to e.g. CostCalc and the formula to [CostCalc] + [enter your cost column name].				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id1565904				0	he	In the initial value enter 0.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id1569261				0	he	Now you can insert a text field and bind it to your [CostCalc] (appears in the data field list box).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id9256874				0	he	Maybe you have to set the initial value to the value of the field like [field].				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id4601886				0	he	If there are blank fields in the cost column, use the following formula to replace the blank fields' content with zero:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id1754509				0	he	[SumCost] + IF(ISBLANK([field]);0;[field])				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id8122196				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the formula that defines the function. Use OpenFormula syntax.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id9909665				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the initial value for the evaluation of the formula. Often this is set to 0 or to 1.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id9141819				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>If Deep traversing is enabled, functions are evaluated considering all lower levels of hierarchy. This would be used for instance for line numbering. If Deep traversing is not enabled, only the first level of hierarchy is evaluated.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id6354869				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>If Pre evaluation is enabled, functions are evaluated only when the report is finished.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11080000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Execute SQL statement				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11080000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148983				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>SQL; executing SQL statements (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>databases; administration through SQL (Base)\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11080000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153345				0	he	\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/11080000.xhp\" name=\"Execute SQL statement\"\>Execute SQL statement\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154288				0	he	\<variable id=\"sqltext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Opens a dialog where you can enter an SQL command for administering a database.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147275				0	he	You can only enter administration commands in this dialog, such as Grant, Create Table, or Drop Table, and not filter commands. The commands that you can enter depend on the data source, for example, dBase can only run some of the SQL commands list here.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154860				0	he	To run an SQL query for filtering data in the database, use the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/02010100.xhp\" name=\"Query Design\"\>Query Design View\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11080000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149514				0	he	Command to execute				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147618				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"DBACCESS_MULTILINEEDIT_DLG_DIRECTSQL_ME_SQL\"\>Enter the SQL administration command that you want to run.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153087				0	he	For example, for a "Bibliography" data source, you can enter the following SQL command:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145673				0	he	SELECT "Address" FROM "biblio" "biblio"				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145611				0	he	For more information on SQL commands, please consult the documentation that came with the database.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11080000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156024				0	he	Previous commands				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149045				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"DBACCESS_LISTBOX_DLG_DIRECTSQL_LB_HISTORY\"\>Lists the previously executed SQL commands. To run a command again, click the command, and then click \<emph\>Run\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11080000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154348				0	he	Status				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151054				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"DBACCESS_MULTILINEEDIT_DLG_DIRECTSQL_ME_STATUS\"\>Displays the results, including errors, of the SQL command that you ran.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11080000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154071				0	he	Run				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151210	8			0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"DBACCESS_PUSHBUTTON_DLG_DIRECTSQL_PB_EXECUTE\"\>Runs the command that you entered in the \<emph\>Command to execute \</emph\>box.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Create New Adabas Database				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159176				0	he	\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/30100000.xhp\" name=\"Create New Adabas Database\"\>Create New Adabas Database\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154515				0	he	Creates a new \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/30000000.xhp\" name=\"Adabas database\"\>Adabas database\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156117				0	he	Database name				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3158432				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_ADABAS_DBNAME\"\>Type the name of the database.\</ahelp\> The name is added to the \<emph\>Data source URL\</emph\> field.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150256				0	he	User settings				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155628				0	he	Administrator				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145609				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_ADABAS_SYSUSR\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the name of the database administrator.\</ahelp\> The administrator name and password is assigned when you create an Adabas database. Apart from the administrator, two more users can access the Adabas database.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149045				0	he	Control User				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149294				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_ADABAS_CONUSR\"\>Enter the name of a user that you want to give limited control to modify some parameters of the database. Normally, the default settings for the name and the password of the control user are not changed.\</ahelp\> The control user does not affect the three-user limitation.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153379				0	he	Domain User				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153362				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_ADABAS_USR\"\>Enter the name of the domain user that is used by Adabas internally. Normally, the default settings for the name and password of the domain user are not changed.\</ahelp\> The domain user does not affect the three-user limit.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147084				0	he	Password				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148674				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_ADABAS_DOMAINPWD\"\>Enter a password.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144433				0	he	Database settings				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145607				0	he	Drives containing parts of the Serverdb are called DEVSPACEs. To improve performance, store each DEVSPACE on separate drives.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146985				0	he	The file path for a DEVSPACE, including its file name, cannot exceed 40 characters.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146148				0	he	SYSDEVSPACE				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149064				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_ADABAS_SYSDEVSPACE\"\>Enter the path for the system DEVSPACE.\</ahelp\> The SYSDEVSPACE manages the configuration data for the database. The size of the SYSDEVSPACE depends on the size of the database.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147319				0	he	TRANSACTIONLOG				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154190				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_ADABAS_TRANSACTIONLOG\"\>Enter the path for the transaction log file.\</ahelp\> This file records all modifications that are made to the database during a transaction, and overwrites them when the transaction is completed. The TRANSACTIONLOG is also used for the rollback of a transaction.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145748				0	he	DATADEVSPACE				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152597				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_ADABAS_DATADEVSPACE\"\>Enter the path for the data DEVSPACE.\</ahelp\> This file stores user data, such as tables and indexes, as well as the SQL catalog (schema info). The data contained in one user table is evenly distributed across all DATADEVSPACEs. The combined size of all DATADEVSPACEs corresponds to the size of the database.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150103				0	he	The maximum size for a DATADEVSPACE in the limited version Adabas database is 100MB.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147426				0	he	If the DATADEVSPACE reaches full capacity during a database operation, Adabas shuts down, increases the capacity of the DATADEVSPACE (up to 100 MB), and restarts the database. Saved data is not lost.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153189				0	he	...				20200411 15:09:53
