helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_id4572283				0	he	The availability of the following controls depends on the type of database:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN10590				0	he	Use SQL92 naming constraints				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN10594				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Only allows characters that conform to the SQL92 naming convention in a name in a data source. All other characters are rejected. Each name must begin with a lowercase letter, an uppercase letter, or an underscore ( _ ). The remaining characters can be ASCII letters, numbers, and underscores.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN105907				0	he	Use keyword AS before table alias names				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN105947				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Some databases use the keyword "AS" between a name and its alias, while other databases use a whitespace. Enable this option to insert AS before the alias.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	hd_id3534958				0	he	End text lines with CR + LF				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_id6151921				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Select to use the CR + LF code pair to end every text line (preferred for DOS and Windows operating systems).\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
