helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\brackets.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152596				0	he	\<variable id=\"brackets\"\>\<link href=\"text/smath/guide/brackets.xhp\" name=\"Merging Formula Parts in Brackets\"\>Merging Formula Parts in Brackets\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\brackets.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154511				0	he	Inserting fractions into formulas				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\brackets.xhp	0	help	par_id3146971				0	he	In the case of a fraction whose numerator and denominator consist of a product, a sum, and so on, the values that belong together must be bracketed together.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\brackets.xhp	0	help	par_id3149021				0	he	Use the following syntax:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\brackets.xhp	0	help	par_id3083280				0	he	{a + c} over 2 = m				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\brackets.xhp	0	help	par_id3154703				0	he	or				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\brackets.xhp	0	help	par_id3150297				0	he	m = {a + c} over 2				20200411 15:09:53
