helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154659				0	he	Import Formula from File				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150251				0	he	\<variable id=\"formelimportierentext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ImportFormula\" visibility=\"visible\"\>This command opens a dialog for importing a formula.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153916				0	he	The \<emph\>Insert\</emph\> dialog is set up like the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01020000.xhp\" name=\"Open\"\>Open\</link\> dialog under \<emph\>File\</emph\>. Use the \<emph\>Insert\</emph\> dialog to load, edit and display a formula saved as a file in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153917				0	he	You can import MathML files created by other applications as well. The MathML source must have a \<item type=\"code\"\>math\</item\> element with an \<item type=\"code\"\>xmlns\</item\> attribute with value "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML". The languages MathML and StarMath are not fully compatible, therefore you should revise the import result. For details about the language MathML see its \<link href=\"http://www.w3.org/TR/#tr_MathML\"\>specification\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06020000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154661				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>MathML; import via clipboard\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
