helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\smooth_line_properties.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Smooth Line Properties				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\smooth_line_properties.xhp	0	help	bm_id3803827				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>curves;properties in line charts/XY charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>properties;smooth lines in line charts/XY charts\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\smooth_line_properties.xhp	0	help	hd_id3050325				0	he	Smooth Line Properties				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\smooth_line_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id9421979				0	he	In a chart that displays lines (Line type or XY type), you can choose to show curves instead of straight lines. Some options control the properties of those curves.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\smooth_line_properties.xhp	0	help	hd_id1228370				0	he	To change line properties				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\smooth_line_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id1601611				0	he	Select Cubic Spline or B-Spline.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\smooth_line_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id879848				0	he	These are mathematical models that influence the display of the curves. The cubic spline line passes through all points, while the B-spline line connects the first and last point and passes by the intermediate points.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\smooth_line_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id3464461				0	he	Optionally set the resolution. A higher value leads to a smoother line.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\smooth_line_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id6998809				0	he	For B-spline lines optionally set the data points order.				20200411 15:09:53
