helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3149377				0	he	You can animate drawing objects, text objects, and graphic objects (images) on your slides to make your presentation more interesting. $[officename] Impress provides you with a simple animation editor where you can create animation images (frames) by assembling objects from your slide. The animation effect is achieved by rotating through the static frames that you create.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3154657				0	he	If you create a bitmap animation (animated GIF), you can assign a delay time to each frame, and specify the number of times the animation is played.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150250				0	he	To create an animated GIF:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3148703	59			0	he	Select an object or group of objects that you want to include in your animation and choose\<emph\> Insert - Animated Image\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3149601				0	he	Do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3145086	97			0	he	Click the \<emph\>Apply Object \</emph\>button \<image id=\"img_id3148489\" src=\"sd/res/get1obj.png\" width=\"0.423cm\" height=\"0.423cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3148489\"\>Note Icon\</alt\>\</image\> to add a single object or a group of objects to the current animation frame.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3150860	98			0	he	Click the \<emph\>Apply Objects Individually \</emph\>button \<image id=\"img_id3149355\" src=\"sd/res/getallob.png\" width=\"0.423cm\" height=\"0.423cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149355\"\>Tip Icon\</alt\>\</image\> to create a separate animation frame for each of the selected objects.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3148391	61			0	he	In the \<emph\>Animation Group \</emph\>area, select \<emph\>Bitmap object\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3154871				0	he	Use the animation timeline to specify the duration for displaying a frame and the number of times an animation sequence is presented (looping).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3154644				0	he	Enter a frame number in the \<emph\>Image Number\</emph\> box (left box).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3150756	63			0	he	Enter the number of seconds you want the frame to display in the \<emph\>Duration \</emph\>box (middle box).				20200411 15:09:53
