helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150441				0	he	\<variable id=\"line_edit\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/line_edit.xhp\" name=\"Editing Curves\"\>Editing Curves\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3150342				0	he	A curved line segment consists of two data points (endpoints) and two control points (handles). A control line connects a control point to a data point. You can change the shape of a curve by converting a data point to a different type, or by dragging the control points to a different location.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3145252				0	he	You can also modify the properties of the line by selecting the line and choosing \<emph\>Format - Line\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3153711				0	he	\<image id=\"img_id3149018\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_toggleobjectbeziermode.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149018\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3155959				0	he	To view the data points and control points of a curved line, select the line, and then click the \<emph\>Points\</emph\> icon on the Drawing bar. The data points are represented by squares and the control points by circles. A control point might overlay a data point.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145587				0	he	To adjust a curved line segment:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3151241	51			0	he	Select a curved line, and then click the \<emph\>Points \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> Bar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3150213				0	he	Do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3153810				0	he	Drag a data point to resize the line. If a control point overlies the data point, drag the control point until you can see the data point, and then drag the data point.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3149872				0	he	Drag a control point. The curve pulls in the direction that you drag the control point.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150431				0	he	To split a curved line:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3150395				0	he	You can only split a curved line that has three or more data points.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3151392	59			0	he	Select a curved line, and then click the \<emph\>Points \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> Bar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3149941	60			0	he	Select a data point, and then click the \<emph\>Split Curve \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\> Bar.				20200411 15:09:53
