helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Converting Text Characters into Drawing Objects				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150717				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>text; converting to curves\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>characters; converting to curves\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sign conversion to curves\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>converting; text to curves\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>draw objects;converting text to\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>curves;converting text to\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150717				0	he	\<variable id=\"text2curve\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/text2curve.xhp\" name=\"Converting Text Characters into Drawing Objects\"\>Converting Text Characters into Drawing Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	par_id3155960				0	he	You can convert text characters into curves that you can edit and resize as you would any drawing object. Once you convert text into a drawing object, you can no longer edit the content of the text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153965				0	he	To convert text into a drawing object:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	par_id3146963				0	he	Select the text that you want to convert, and do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	par_id3149053				0	he	In $[officename] Draw, choose \<emph\>Modify - Convert - To Curve\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	par_id3150395				0	he	In $[officename] Impress, right-click the border of the text object, and then choose \<emph\>Convert - To Curve\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	par_id3150746				0	he	If your text contains more than one character, the converted text becomes a grouped object. Double-click the group to edit individual objects. Press Esc when finished.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	par_id3150336				0	he	Now, click the \<emph\>Points\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> bar. Click the object. You can see all the Bézier points of the object. On the \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\> bar, you can find various icons for editing, inserting and deleting points.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Using Shortcut Keys in $[officename] Impress 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154702				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>accessibility; $[officename] Impress\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154702				0	he	\<variable id=\"keyboard\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/keyboard.xhp\" name=\"Using Shortcut Keys in $[officename] Impress\"\>Using Shortcut Keys in $[officename] Impress\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148610				0	he	You can use the keyboard to access $[officename] Impress commands as well as to navigate through the workspace. $[officename] Impress uses the same shortcut keys as $[officename] Draw to create \<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/keyboard.xhp\" name=\"drawing objects\"\>drawing objects\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149602				0	he	Selecting placeholders				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150212				0	he	$[officename] Impress \<emph\>AutoLayouts\</emph\> use placeholders for slide titles, text, and objects. To select a placeholder, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+Enter\</item\>. To move to the next placeholder, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+Enter\</item\> again.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3166467				0	he	If you press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+Enter\</item\> after you reach the last placeholder in a slide, a new slide is inserted after the current slide. The new slide uses the same layout as the current slide.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157871				0	he	During a Slide Show				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150650				0	he	To start a slide show, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+F2\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
