helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\01\13050700.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146119				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>converting; to contours\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>contours; converting to\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\01\13050700.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146119				0	he	\<link href=\"text/simpress/01/13050700.xhp\" name=\"To Contour\"\>To Contour\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\01\13050700.xhp	0	help	par_id3146974				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:convert_to_contour\"\>Converts the selected object to a polygon, or a group of polygons.\</ahelp\> If the conversion creates a group of polygons (for example, when you convert a text object), then press F3 to enter the group before you can select an individual polygon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\01\13050700.xhp	0	help	par_id3155601	3			0	he	Once you convert a line or a text object to a contour, you can no longer edit it as you normally would. Instead, you can edit the contour as you would any polygon, including using the \<emph\>Edit – Points \</emph\>command to adjust its shape.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\01\03090000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Outline				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\01\03090000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149664				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>outline view\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing;slide titles\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\01\03090000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149664				0	he	\<link href=\"text/simpress/01/03090000.xhp\" name=\"Outline\"\>Outline\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\01\03090000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152597				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SD_BTN_OUTLINE\"\>Switches to outline view where you can reorder slides and edit slide titles and headings.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\01\03090000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150715				0	he	The \<emph\>Text Formatting\</emph\> bar contains the following icons for slide titles:\<link href=\"text/shared/02/06060000.xhp\" name=\"Promote\"\>Promote\</link\>, \<link href=\"text/shared/02/06050000.xhp\" name=\"Demote\"\>Demote\</link\>, \<link href=\"text/shared/02/06100000.xhp\" name=\"Move Up\"\>Move Up\</link\> and \<link href=\"text/shared/02/06110000.xhp\" name=\"Move Down\"\>Move Down\</link\>. If you want to reorder slide titles with the keyboard, ensure that the cursor is at the beginning of a title and press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Tab\</item\> to move the title one level lower in the hierarchy. To move the title up one level, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Shift+Tab\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\01\03090000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156382				0	he	The upper outline level corresponds to slide titles, and the lower levels correspond to the headings on a slides.				20200411 15:09:53
