helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\04\01020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154766				0	he	Moves the cursor to the left edge of the current data range. If the column to the left of the cell that contains the cursor is empty, the cursor moves to the next column to the left that contains data.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\04\01020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153554				0	he	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Right Arrow				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\04\01020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155593				0	he	Moves the cursor to the right edge of the current data range. If the column to the right of the cell that contains the cursor is empty, the cursor moves to the next column to the right that contains data.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\04\01020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149317				0	he	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Up Arrow				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\04\01020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153076				0	he	Moves the cursor to the top edge of the current data range. If the row above the cell that contains the cursor is empty, the cursor moves up to the next row that contains data.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\04\01020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147250				0	he	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Down Arrow				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\04\01020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149054				0	he	Moves the cursor to the bottom edge of the current data range. If the row below the cell that contains the cursor is empty, the cursor moves down to the next row that contains data.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\04\01020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148744				0	he	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+Arrow				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\04\01020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3159258				0	he	Selects all cells containing data from the current cell to the end of the continuous range of data cells, in the direction of the arrow pressed. If used to select rows and columns together, a rectangular cell range is selected.				20200411 15:09:53
