helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3146113				0	he	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05070000.xhp\" name=\"Format - Page - (Header / Footer)\"\>Format - Page - (Header / Footer)\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Protecting Cells from Changes				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146119				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>protecting;cells and sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; protecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cell protection; enabling\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheets; protecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>documents; protecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; hiding for printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>modifying; sheet protection\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing; document protection\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hiding;formulas\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formulas;hiding\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146119				0	he	\<variable id=\"cell_protect\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cell_protect.xhp\" name=\"Protecting Cells from Changes\"\>Protecting Cells from Changes\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3153368				0	he	In \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc you can protect sheets and the document as a whole. You can choose whether the cells are protected against accidental changes, whether the formulas can be viewed from within Calc, whether the cells are visible or whether the cells can be printed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3145261				0	he	Protection can be provided by means of a password, but it does not have to be. If you have assigned a password, protection can only be removed once the correct password has been entered.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3148576				0	he	Note that the cell protection for cells with the \<emph\>Protected\</emph\> attribute is only effective when you protect the whole sheet. In the default condition, every cell has the \<emph\>Protected\</emph\> attribute. Therefore you must remove the attribute selectively for those cells where the user may make changes. You then protect the whole sheet and save the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id5974303				0	he	These protection features are just switches to prevent accidential action. The features are not intended to provide any secure protection. For example, by exporting a sheet to another file format, a user may be able to surpass the protection features. There is only one secure protection: the password that you can apply when saving an OpenDocument file. A file that has been saved with a password can be opened only with the same password.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066B				0	he	Select the cells that you want to specify the cell protection options for.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3149019				0	he	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Cells\</item\> and click the \<emph\>Cell Protection\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3152985				0	he	Select the protection options that you want. All options will be applied only after you protect the sheet from the Tools menu - see below.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id31529866655				0	he	Uncheck \<emph\>Protected\</emph\> to allow the user to change the currently selected cells.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3152898	10			0	he	Select \<emph\>Protected\</emph\> to prevent changes to the contents and the format of a cell. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_idN1069A				0	he	Select \<emph\>Hide formula\</emph\> to hide and to protect formulas from changes.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A1				0	he	Select \<emph\>Hide when printing\</emph\> to hide protected cells in the printed document. The cells are not hidden onscreen.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3152872				0	he	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3145362				0	he	Apply the protection options.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_idN106C0				0	he	To protect the cells from being changed / viewed / printed according to your settings in the \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\> dialog, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Protect Document - Sheet\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_idN106C7				0	he	To protect the structure of the document, for example the count, \<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/rename_table.xhp\"\>names\</link\>, and order of the sheets, from being changed, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Protect Document - Document\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_idN106CF				0	he	(Optional) Enter a password.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D2				0	he	If you forget your password, you cannot deactivate the protection. If you only want to protect cells from accidental changes, set the sheet protection, but do not enter a password.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3153810	13			0	he	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B8C				0	he	            \<embedvar href=\"text/shared/guide/digital_signatures.xhp#digital_signatures\"/\>         				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Freezing Rows or Columns as Headers				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154684				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>tables; freezing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>title rows; freezing during table split\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rows; freezing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>columns; freezing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>freezing rows or columns\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>headers; freezing during table split\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>scrolling prevention in tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>windows; splitting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; splitting windows\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154684				0	he	\<variable id=\"line_fix\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/line_fix.xhp\" name=\"Freezing Rows or Columns as Headers\"\>Freezing Rows or Columns as Headers\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3148576				0	he	If you have long rows or columns of data that extend beyond the viewable area of the sheet, you can freeze some rows or columns, which allows you to see the frozen columns or rows as you scroll through the rest of the data.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3156441				0	he	Select the row below, or the column to the right of the row or column that you want to be in the frozen region. All rows above, or all columns to the left of the selection are frozen.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3153158				0	he	To freeze both horizontally and vertically, select the \<emph\>cell\</emph\> that is below the row and to the right of the column that you want to freeze.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3156286				0	he	Choose \<emph\>Window - Freeze\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3151073	5			0	he	To deactivate, choose \<emph\>Window - Freeze \</emph\>again.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3155335				0	he	If the area defined is to be scrollable, apply the \<emph\>Window - Split\</emph\> command.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3147345				0	he	If you want to print a certain row on all pages of a document, choose \<emph\>Format - Print ranges - Edit\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3147004				0	he	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/07090000.xhp\" name=\"Window - Freeze\"\>Window - Freeze\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3150088				0	he	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/07080000.xhp\" name=\"Window - Split\"\>Window - Split\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3150304				0	he	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05080300.xhp\" name=\"Format - Print ranges - Edit\"\>Format - Print ranges - Edit\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\year2000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	19xx/20xx Years				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\year2000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150439				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>years; 2-digits\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>dates; 19xx/20xx\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\year2000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150439				0	he	\<variable id=\"year2000\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/year2000.xhp\" name=\"19xx/20xx Years\"\>19xx/20xx Years\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\year2000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151116				0	he	The year in a date entry is often entered as two digits. Internally, the year is managed by $[officename] as four digits, so that in the calculation of the difference from 1/1/99 to 1/1/01, the result will correctly be two years.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\year2000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154011				0	he	Under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - $[officename] - General\</emph\> you can define the century that is used when you enter a year with only two digits. The default is 1930 to 2029.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\year2000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150010				0	he	This means that if you enter a date of 1/1/30 or higher, it will be treated internally as 1/1/1930 or higher. All lower two-digit years apply to the 20xx century. So, for example, 1/1/20 is converted into 1/1/2020.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Deactivating Automatic Changes				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149456				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>deactivating; automatic changes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; deactivating automatic changes in\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>AutoInput function on/off\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text in cells;AutoInput function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; AutoInput function of text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>input support in spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing; input in cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>AutoCorrect function;cell contents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cell input;AutoInput function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>lowercase letters;AutoInput function (in cells)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>capital letters;AutoInput function (in cells)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>date formats;avoiding conversion to\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>number completion on/off\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text completion on/off\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149456				0	he	\<variable id=\"auto_off\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/auto_off.xhp\" name=\"Deactivating Automatic Changes\"\>Deactivating Automatic Changes\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3156442				0	he	By default, $[officename] automatically corrects many common typing errors and applies formatting while you type. You can immediately undo any automatic changes with \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Z.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3145273				0	he	The following shows you how to deactivate and reactivate the automatic changes in $[officename] Calc:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145748				0	he	Automatic text or number completion				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3154730				0	he	When making an entry in a cell, $[officename] Calc automatically suggests matching input found in the same column. This function is known as \<emph\>AutoInput\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3153878				0	he	To turn the AutoInput on and off, set or remove the check mark in front of \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06130000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Cell Contents - AutoInput\"\>\<emph\>Tools - Cell Contents - AutoInput\</emph\>\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146972				0	he	Automatic conversion to date format				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3153707				0	he	$[officename] Calc automatically converts certain entries to dates. For example, the entry \<emph\>1.1\</emph\> may be interpreted as January 1 of the current year, according to the locale settings of your operating system, and then displayed according to the date format applied to the cell.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3159267				0	he	To ensure that an entry is interpreted as text, add an apostrophe at the beginning of the entry. The apostrophe is not displayed in the cell.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150043				0	he	Quotation marks replaced by custom quotes				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3155333				0	he	Choose \<emph\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options\</emph\>. Go to the \<emph\>Localized Options\</emph\> tab and unmark \<emph\>Replace\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149565				0	he	Cell content always begins with uppercase				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3147001				0	he	Choose \<emph\>Tools - AutoCorrect\</emph\>. Go to the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab. Unmark \<emph\>Capitalize first letter of every sentence\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150345				0	he	Replace word with another word				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3166425				0	he	Choose \<emph\>Tools - AutoCorrect\</emph\>. Go to the \<emph\>Replace\</emph\> tab. Select the word pair and click \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3152992				0	he	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06130000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Cell Contents - AutoInput\"\>Tools - Cell Contents - AutoInput\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3154368				0	he	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - AutoCorrect\"\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Using Rounded Off Numbers				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153361				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>numbers; rounded off\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rounded off numbers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exact numbers in $[officename] Calc\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>decimal places; showing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;number of decimal places\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>values;rounded in calculations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>calculating;rounded off values\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>numbers; decimal places\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>precision as shown\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rounding precision\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables in spreadsheets; values as shown\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156422				0	he	\<variable id=\"rounding_numbers\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/rounding_numbers.xhp\" name=\"Using Rounded Off Numbers\"\>Using Rounded Off Numbers\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3153726				0	he	In $[officename] Calc, all decimal numbers are displayed rounded off to two decimal places.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152596				0	he	To change this for selected cells				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3154321				0	he	Mark all the cells you want to modify.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3147428				0	he	Choose \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\> and go to the \<emph\>Numbers\</emph\> tab page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3153876				0	he	In the \<emph\>Category\</emph\> field, select \<emph\>Number\</emph\>. Under \<emph\>Options\</emph\>, change the number of \<emph\>Decimal places\</emph\> and exit the dialog with OK.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155415				0	he	To change this everywhere				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3150715				0	he	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3153707				0	he	Go to the \<emph\>Calculate\</emph\> page. Modify the number of \<emph\>Decimal places\</emph\> and exit the dialog with OK.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154755				0	he	To calculate with the rounded off numbers instead of the internal exact values				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3150045				0	he	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3146920				0	he	Go to the \<emph\>Calculate\</emph\> page. Mark the \<emph\>Precision as shown\</emph\> field and exit the dialog with OK.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3145790				0	he	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020300.xhp\" name=\"Numbers\"\>Numbers\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3147005				0	he	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060500.xhp\" name=\"Calculate\"\>Calculate\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_tipps.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Selecting Pivot Table Output Ranges				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_tipps.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148663				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>pivot table function; preventing data overwriting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>output ranges of pivot tables\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_tipps.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148663				0	he	\<variable id=\"datapilot_tipps\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/datapilot_tipps.xhp\" name=\"Selecting Pivot Table Output Ranges\"\>Selecting Pivot Table Output Ranges\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_tipps.xhp	0	help	par_id3154123				0	he	Click the button \<emph\>More\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Pivot Table\</emph\> dialog. The dialog will be extended.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_tipps.xhp	0	help	par_id3153771				0	he	You can select a named range in which the pivot table is to be created, from the \<emph\>Results to\</emph\> box. If the results range does not have a name, enter the coordinates of the upper left cell of the range into the field to the right of the \<emph\>Results to\</emph\> box. You can also click on the appropriate cell to have the coordinates entered accordingly.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_tipps.xhp	0	help	par_id3146974				0	he	If you mark the \<emph\>Ignore empty rows\</emph\> check box, they will not be taken into account when the pivot table is created.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_tipps.xhp	0	help	par_id3145273				0	he	If the \<emph\>Identify categories\</emph\> check box is marked, the categories will be identified by their headings and assigned accordingly when the pivot table is created.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	References to Other Sheets and Referencing URLs				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150441				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>HTML; in sheet cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>references; URL in cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; Internet references\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>URL; in Calc\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150441				0	he	\<variable id=\"cellreferences_url\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cellreferences_url.xhp\" name=\"Referencing URLs\"\>Referencing URLs\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id1955626				0	he	For example, if you found an Internet page containing current stock exchange information in spreadsheet cells, you can load this page in $[officename] Calc by using the following procedure:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3152993				0	he	In a $[officename] Calc document, position the cursor in the cell into which you want to insert the external data.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3145384				0	he	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Link to External Data\</item\>. The \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04090000.xhp\" name=\"External Data\"\>\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>External Data\</item\>\</link\> dialog appears.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3152892				0	he	Enter the URL of the document or Web page in the dialog. The URL must be in the format: http://www.my-bank.com/table.html. The URL for local or local area network files is the path seen in the \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3153068				0	he	$[officename] loads the Web page or file in the "background", that is, without displaying it. In the large list box of the \<emph\>External Data\</emph\> dialog, you can see the name of all the sheets or named ranges you can choose from.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3153914				0	he	Select one or more sheets or named ranges. You can also activate the automatic update function every "n" minutes and click OK.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3157979				0	he	The contents will be inserted as a link in the $[officename] Calc document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3144768				0	he	Save your spreadsheet. When you open it again later, $[officename] Calc will update the linked cells following an inquiry.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3159204				0	he	Under \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040900.xhp\" name=\"Spreadsheet - General\"\>\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Calc - General\</item\>\</link\> you can choose to have the update, when opened, automatically carried out either always, upon request or never. The update can be started manually in the dialog under \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit - Links\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Grouping Pivot Tables				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	bm_id4195684				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>grouping; pivot tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pivot table function;grouping table entries\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>ungrouping entries in pivot tables\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	par_idN10643				0	he	\<variable id=\"datapilot_grouping\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/datapilot_grouping.xhp\"\>Grouping Pivot Tables\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	par_idN10661				0	he	The resulting pivot table can contain many different entries. By grouping the entries, you can improve the visible result.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	par_idN10667				0	he	Select a cell or range of cells in the pivot table.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066B				0	he	Choose \<emph\>Data - Outline - Group\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066E				0	he	Depending on the format of the selected cells, either a new group field is added to the pivot table, or you see one of the two \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12090400.xhp\"\>Grouping\</link\> dialogs, either for numeric values, or for date values.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	par_id3328653				0	he	The pivot table must be organized in a way that grouping can be applied.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	par_idN10682				0	he	To remove a grouping, click inside the group, then choose \<emph\>Data - Outline - Ungroup\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Inserting and Editing Notes				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153968				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>comments; on cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells;comments\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>remarks on cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting;comments on cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>viewing;comments on cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>displaying; comments\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153968				0	he	\<variable id=\"note_insert\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/note_insert.xhp\" name=\"Inserting and Editing Comments\"\>Inserting and Editing Comments\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150440				0	he	You can assign a comment to each cell by choosing \<link href=\"text/shared/01/04050000.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Comment\"\>\<emph\>Insert - Comment\</emph\>\</link\>. The comment is indicated by a small red square, the comment indicator, in the cell.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3145750				0	he	The note is visible whenever the mouse pointer is over the cell, provided you have activated \<emph\>Help - Tips\</emph\> or - \<emph\>Extended Tips\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3148575				0	he	When you select the cell, you can choose \<emph\>Show Note\</emph\> from the context menu of the cell. Doing so keeps the note visible until you deactivate the \<emph\>Show Note\</emph\> command from the same context menu.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149958				0	he	To edit a permanently visible note, just click in it. If you delete the entire text of the note, the note itself is deleted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_idN10699				0	he	Move or resize each note as you like.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_idN1069D				0	he	Format each note by specifying background color, transparency, border style, and text alignment. Choose the commands from the context menu of the note.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3144764				0	he	To show or hide the comment indicator, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</emph\> and mark or unmark the \<emph\>Comment indicator\</emph\> check box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150715				0	he	To display a help tip for a selected cell, use \<emph\>Data - Validity - Input Help\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153707				0	he	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/04050000.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Comment\"\>Insert - Comment\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Formatting Spreadsheets				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154125				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>text in cells; formatting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets;formatting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>backgrounds;cells and pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>borders;cells and pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting;spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>numbers; formatting options for selected cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; number formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>currencies;formats\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154125				0	he	\<variable id=\"format_table\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/format_table.xhp\" name=\"Designing Spreadsheets\"\>Formatting Spreadsheets\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153912	13			0	he	Formatting Text in a Spreadsheet 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3144772				0	he	Select the text you want to format.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3155268	15			0	he	Choose the desired text attributes from the \<emph\>Formatting \</emph\>Bar. You can also choose \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\> dialog will appear in which you can choose various text attributes on the \<emph\>Font\</emph\> tab page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149899				0	he	Formatting Numbers in a Spreadsheet				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3159226				0	he	Select the cells containing the numbers you want to format.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3150046	18			0	he	To format numbers in the default currency format or as percentages, use the icons on the \<emph\>Formatting \</emph\>Bar. For other formats, choose \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\>. You can choose from the preset formats or define your own on the \<emph\>Numbers\</emph\> tab page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153483				0	he	Formatting Borders and Backgrounds for Cells and Pages				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3154733				0	he	You can assign a format to any group of cells by first selecting the cells (for multiple selection, hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>key when clicking), and then activating the \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\> dialog in \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Cell\</item\>. In this dialog, you can select attributes such as shadows and backgrounds.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3145116				0	he	To apply formatting attributes to an entire sheet, choose \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\>. You can define headers and footers, for example, to appear on each printed page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3145389				0	he	An image that you have loaded with \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Page - Background\</item\> is only visible in print or in the page preview. To display a background image on screen as well, insert the graphic image by choosing \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Picture - From File\</item\> and arrange the image behind the cells by choosing \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Arrange - To Background\</item\>. Use the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/02110000.xhp\" name=\"Navigator\"\>Navigator\</link\> to select the background image.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id2837916				0	he	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020300.xhp\"\>Number Formatting Options\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id2614215				0	he	\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/background.xhp\"\>Backgrounds for Cells\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Applying Multiple Sheets				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154759				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>sheets; inserting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheets; selecting multiple\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheets; simultaneous multiple filling\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>appending sheets\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154759				0	he	\<variable id=\"multitables\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/multitables.xhp\" name=\"Applying Multiple Sheets\"\>Applying Multiple Sheets\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148576				0	he	Inserting a Sheet				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3154731				0	he	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Sheet\</item\> to insert a new sheet or an existing sheet from another file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id05092009140203598				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Opens a dialog box where you can assign macros to sheet events.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id05092009140203523				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Opens a window where you can assign a color to the sheet tab.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id050920091402035				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click to select all sheets in the document.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id0509200914020391				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click to deselect all sheets in the document, except the current sheet.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154491				0	he	Selecting Multiple Sheets				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3145251				0	he	The sheet tab of the current sheet is always visible in white in front of the other sheet tabs. The other sheet tabs are gray when they are not selected. By clicking other sheet tabs while pressing \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>you can select multiple sheets.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B7				0	he	You can use Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Page Up or Page Down to select multiple sheets using the keyboard.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155600				0	he	Undoing a Selection				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3146969				0	he	To undo the selection of a sheet, click its sheet tab again while pressing the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>key. The sheet that is currently visible cannot be removed from the selection.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156382				0	he	Calculating Across Multiple Sheets				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3155333				0	he	You can refer to a range of sheets in a formula by specifying the first and last sheet of the range, for example, \<item type=\"literal\"\>=SUM(Sheet1.A1:Sheet3.A1) \</item\>sums up all A1 cells on Sheet1 through Sheet3.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Changing Row Height or Column Width				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145748				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>heights of cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cell heights\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cell widths\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; heights and widths\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>widths of cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>column widths\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rows; heights\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>columns; widths\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;row heights/column widths\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145748				0	he	\<variable id=\"row_height\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/row_height.xhp\" name=\"Changing Row Height or Column Width\"\>Changing Row Height or Column Width\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3154017				0	he	You can change the height of the rows with the mouse or through the dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3154702				0	he	What is described here for rows and row height applies accordingly for columns and column width.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153963				0	he	Using the mouse to change the row height or column width				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3154020				0	he	Click the area of the headers on the separator below the current row, keep the mouse button pressed and drag up or down in order to change the row height.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3159237				0	he	Select the optimal row height by double-clicking the separator below the row.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154659				0	he	Using the dialog to change the row height or column width				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3150367				0	he	Click the row so that you achieve the focus.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3166432				0	he	Start the context menu on the header at the left-hand side.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3150519				0	he	You will see the commands \<emph\>Row Height\</emph\> and \<emph\>Optimal row height\</emph\>. Choosing either opens a dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3154487				0	he	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05340100.xhp\" name=\"Row height\"\>Row height\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3149408				0	he	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05030200.xhp\" name=\"Optimal row height\"\>Optimal row height\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3153305				0	he	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05340200.xhp\" name=\"Column width\"\>Column width\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3153815				0	he	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05040200.xhp\" name=\"Optimal column width\"\>Optimal column width\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Defining Database Ranges				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154758				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>tables; database ranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>database ranges; defining\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>ranges; defining database ranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defining;database ranges\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154758				0	he	\<variable id=\"database_define\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/database_define.xhp\" name=\"Defining Database Ranges\"\>Defining a Database Range\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3153768				0	he	You can define a range of cells in a spreadsheet to use as a database. Each row in this database range corresponds to a database record and each cell in a row corresponds to a database field. You can sort, group, search, and perform calculations on the range as you would in a database.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3145801	82			0	he	You can only edit and access a database range in the spreadsheet that contains the range. You cannot access the database range in the %PRODUCTNAME Data Sources view. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	par_idN10648				0	he	To Define a Database Range				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3155064				0	he	Select the range of cells that you want to define as a database range.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	par_idN10654				0	he	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Define Range\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3153715				0	he	In the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> box, enter a name for the database range.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066A				0	he	Click \<emph\>More\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3154253				0	he	Specify the options for the database range.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	par_idN10675				0	he	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Merging and Splitting Cells				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147240				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>cells; merging/unmerging\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; merging cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cell merges; defining/canceling\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>unmerging cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>merging;cells\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	hd_id8005005				0	he	\<variable id=\"table_cellmerge\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/table_cellmerge.xhp\" name=\"Merging and Unmerging Cells\"\>Merging and Unmerging Cells\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id8049867				0	he	You can select adjacent cells, then merge them into a single cell. Conversely, you can take a large cell that has been created by merging single cells, and divide it back into individual cells.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id0509200913480176				0	he	When you copy cells into a target range containing merged cells, the target range gets unmerged first, then the copied cells are pasted in. If the copied cells are merged cells, they retain their merge state.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	hd_id235602				0	he	Merging Cells				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id1272927				0	he	Select the adjacent cells.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id6424146				0	he	Choose \<emph\>Format - Merge Cells\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	hd_id451368				0	he	Canceling the merging of cells				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id7116611				0	he	Place the cursor in the cell to be split.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id9493087				0	he	Choose \<emph\>Format - Merge Cells\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Selecting Multiple Cells				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153361				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>cells; selecting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>marking cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>selecting;cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>multiple cells selection\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>selection modes in spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables; selecting ranges\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153361				0	he	\<variable id=\"mark_cells\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/mark_cells.xhp\" name=\"Selecting Multiple Cells\"\>Selecting Multiple Cells\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145272				0	he	Select a rectangular range				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3149261				0	he	With the mouse button pressed, drag from one corner to the diagonally opposed corner of the range.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151119				0	he	Mark a single cell				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975				0	he	Do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3163710				0	he	Click, then Shift-click the cell.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3149959				0	he	Pressing the mouse button, drag a range across two cells, do not release the mouse button, and then drag back to the first cell. Release the mouse button. You can now move the individual cell by drag and drop.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154942				0	he	Select various dispersed cells				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id1001200901072060				0	he	Do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3156284				0	he	Mark at least one cell. Then while pressing \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>, click each of the additional cells.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id1001200901072023				0	he	Click the STD / EXT / ADD area in the status bar until it shows ADD. Now click all cells that you want to select.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146971				0	he	Switch marking mode				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3155064				0	he	On the status bar, click the box with the legend STD / EXT / ADD to switch the marking mode:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3159264				0	he	Field contents				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3155337				0	he	Effect of clicking the mouse				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3149568				0	he	STD				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3148486				0	he	A mouse click selects the cell you have clicked on. Unmarks all marked cells.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3150090				0	he	EXT				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3150305				0	he	A mouse click marks a rectangular range from the current cell to the cell you clicked. Alternatively, Shift-click a cell.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3145587				0	he	ADD				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3154368				0	he	A mouse click in a cell adds it to the already marked cells. A mouse click in a marked cell unmarks it. Alternatively, \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>-click the cells.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3154487				0	he	\<link href=\"text/scalc/main0208.xhp\" name=\"Status bar\"\>Status bar\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\sorted_list.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Applying Sort Lists				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\sorted_list.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150870				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>filling;customized lists\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sort lists;applying\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>applying;sort lists\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defining;sort lists\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>geometric lists\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>arithmetic lists\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>series;sort lists\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>lists; user-defined\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>customized lists\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\sorted_list.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150870	3			0	he	\<variable id=\"sorted_list\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/sorted_list.xhp\" name=\"Applying Sort Lists\"\>Applying Sort Lists\</link\> \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\sorted_list.xhp	0	help	par_id3159154				0	he	Sort lists allow you to type one piece of information in a cell, then drag it to fill in a consecutive list of items.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\sorted_list.xhp	0	help	par_id3148645				0	he	For example, enter the text "Jan" or "January" in an empty cell. Select the cell and click the mouse on the lower right corner of the cell border. Then drag the selected cell a few cells to the right or downwards. When you release the mouse button, the highlighted cells will be filled with the names of the months.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\sorted_list.xhp	0	help	par_id2367931				0	he	Hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>if you do not want to fill the cells with different values.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\sorted_list.xhp	0	help	par_id3152577				0	he	The predefined series can be found under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - Sort Lists\</emph\>. You can also create your own lists of text strings tailored to your needs, such as a list of your company's branch offices. When you use the information in these lists later (for example, as headings), just enter the first name in the list and expand the entry by dragging it with your mouse.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\sorted_list.xhp	0	help	par_id3147434				0	he	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060400.xhp\" name=\"Sort lists\"\>Sort lists\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Converting Text to Numbers				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145068				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>formats; text as numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>time format conversion\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>date formats;conversion\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>converting;text, into numbers\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id0908200901265171				0	he	\<variable id=\"numbers_text\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/numbers_text.xhp\" name=\"Converting Text to Numbers\"\>Converting Text to Numbers\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265127				0	he	Calc converts text inside cells to the respective numeric values if an unambiguous conversion is possible. If no conversion is possible, Calc returns a #VALUE! error.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265196				0	he	Only integer numbers including exponent are converted, and ISO 8601 dates and times in their extended formats with separators. Anything else, like fractional numbers with decimal separators or dates other than ISO 8601, is not converted, as the text string would be locale dependent. Leading and trailing blanks are ignored.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265220				0	he	The following ISO 8601 formats are converted:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265288				0	he	CCYY-MM-DD				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265267				0	he	CCYY-MM-DDThh:mm				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265248				0	he	CCYY-MM-DDThh:mm:ss				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265374				0	he	CCYY-MM-DDThh:mm:ss,s				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265327				0	he	CCYY-MM-DDThh:mm:ss.s				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265399				0	he	hh:mm				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265347				0	he	hh:mm:ss				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265349				0	he	hh:mm:ss,s				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265342				0	he	hh:mm:ss.s				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265491				0	he	The century code CC may not be omitted. Instead of the T date and time separator, exactly one space character may be used.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265467				0	he	If a date is given, it must be a valid Gregorian calendar date. In this case the optional time must be in the range 00:00 to 23:59:59.99999...				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265420				0	he	If only a time string is given, it may have an hours value of more than 24, while minutes and seconds can have a maximum value of 59.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265448				0	he	The conversion is done for single arguments only, as in =A1+A2, or ="1E2"+1. Cell range arguments are not affected, so SUM(A1:A2) differs from A1+A2 if at least one of the two cells contain a convertible string.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id090820090126540				0	he	Strings inside formulas are also converted, such as in ="1999-11-22"+42, which returns the date 42 days after November 22nd, 1999. Calculations involving localized dates as strings inside the formula return an error. For example, the localized date string "11/22/1999" or "22.11.1999" cannot be used for the automatic conversion.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id1005200903485368				0	he	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id1005200903485359				0	he	In A1 enter the text \<item type=\"literal\"\>'1e2\</item\> (which is converted to the number 100 internally).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id1005200903485341				0	he	In A2 enter \<item type=\"literal\"\>=A1+1\</item\> (which correctly results in 101).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265544				0	he	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020300.xhp\" name=\"Format - Cells - Numbers\"\>Format - Cells - Numbers\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Highlighting Negative Numbers				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147434				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>negative numbers; highlighting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>numbers; highlighting negative numbers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>highlighting;negative numbers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>colors;number formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>number formats;colors\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147434				0	he	\<variable id=\"cellstyle_minusvalue\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp\" name=\"Highlighting Negative Numbers\"\>Highlighting Negative Numbers\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3153878				0	he	You can format cells with a number format that highlights negative numbers in red. Alternatively, you can define your own number format in which negative numbers are highlighted in other colors.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3155600				0	he	Select the cells and choose \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3146969				0	he	On the \<emph\>Numbers\</emph\> tab, select a number format and mark \<emph\>Negative numbers red\</emph\> check box. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3145640				0	he	The cell number format is defined in two parts. The format for positive numbers and zero is defined in front of the semicolon; after the semicolon the formula for negative numbers is defined. You can change the code (RED) under \<emph\>Format code\</emph\>. For example, instead of "RED," enter "YELLOW". If the new code appears in the list after clicking the \<emph\>Add\</emph\> icon, this is a valid entry.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Referencing a Cell in Another Document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147436				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>sheet references\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>references; to cells in another document\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; operating in another document\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147436				0	he	\<variable id=\"cellreferences\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cellreferences.xhp\" name=\"Referencing Other Sheets\"\>Referencing Other Sheets\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id9663075				0	he	In a sheet cell you can show a reference to a cell in another sheet.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id1879329				0	he	In the same way, a reference can also be made to a cell from another document provided that this document has already been saved as a file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	hd_id7122409				0	he	To Reference a Cell in the Same Document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id2078005				0	he	Open a new, empty spreadsheet.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id4943693				0	he	By way of example, enter the following formula in cell A1 of Sheet1:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id9064302				0	he	=Sheet2.A1				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id7609790				0	he	Click the \<emph\>Sheet 2\</emph\> tab at the bottom of the spreadsheet. Set the cursor in cell A1 there and enter text or a number.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id809961				0	he	If you switch back to Sheet1, you will see the same content in cell A1 there. If the contents of Sheet2.A1 change, then the contents of Sheet1.A1 also change.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	hd_id9209570				0	he	To Reference a Cell in Another Document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id5949278				0	he	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\>, to load an existing spreadsheet document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id8001953				0	he	Choose \<emph\>File - New\</emph\>, to open a new spreadsheet document. Set the cursor in the cell where you want to insert the external data and enter an equals sign to indicate that you want to begin a formula.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id8571123				0	he	Now switch to the document you have just loaded. Click the cell with the data that you want to insert in the new document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id8261665				0	he	Switch back to the new spreadsheet. In the input line you will now see how $[officename] Calc has added the reference to the formula for you. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id5888241				0	he	The reference to a cell of another document contains the name of the other document in single inverted commas, then a hash #, then the name of the sheet of the other document, followed by a point and the name of the cell.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id7697683				0	he	Confirm the formula by clicking the green check mark.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id7099826				0	he	If you drag the box in the lower right corner of the active cell to select a range of cells, $[officename] automatically inserts the corresponding references in the adjacent cells. As a result, the sheet name is preceded with a "$" sign to designate it as an absolute reference.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id674459				0	he	If you examine the name of the other document in this formula, you will notice that it is written as a \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#url\" name=\"URL\"\>URL\</link\>. This means that you can also enter a URL from the Internet.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Applying Multiple Operations				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147559				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>multiple operations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>what if operations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; multiple operations in\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data tables; multiple operations in\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cross-classified tables\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147559				0	he	\<variable id=\"multioperation\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/multioperation.xhp\" name=\"Applying Multiple Operations\"\>Applying Multiple Operations\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145171				0	he	Multiple Operations in Columns or Rows				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id4123966				0	he	The \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Multiple Operations\</item\> command provides a planning tool for "what if" questions. In your spreadsheet, you enter a formula to calculate a result from values that are stored in other cells. Then, you set up a cell range where you enter some fixed values, and the Multiple Operations command will calculate the results depending on the formula.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3156424				0	he	In the \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\> field, enter the cell reference to the formula that applies to the data range. In the \<emph\>Column input cell/Row input cell\</emph\> field, enter the cell reference to the corresponding cell that is part of the formula. This can be explained best by examples:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159153				0	he	Examples				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3153189				0	he	You produce toys which you sell for $10 each. Each toy costs $2 to make, in addition to which you have fixed costs of $10,000 per year. How much profit will you make in a year if you sell a particular number of toys?				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id6478774				0	he	\<image id=\"img_id1621753\" src=\"res/helpimg/what-if.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id1621753\"\>what-if sheet area\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145239				0	he	Calculating With One Formula and One Variable				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3146888				0	he	To calculate the profit, first enter any number as the quantity (items sold) - in this example 2000. The profit is found from the formula Profit=Quantity * (Selling price - Direct costs) - Fixed costs. Enter this formula in B5.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3157875				0	he	In column D enter certain annual sales, one under the other; for example, in steps of 500 from 500 to 5000.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3159115				0	he	Mark the range D2:E11, and thus the values in column D and the empty cells alongside in column E.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149723				0	he	Choose \<emph\>Data - Multiple operations\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149149	46			0	he	With the cursor in the \<emph\>Formulas \</emph\>field, click cell B5.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149355				0	he	Set the cursor in the \<emph\>Column\</emph\> field and click cell B4. This means that: B4, the quantity, is the variable in the formula, which is replaced by the marked column values.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149009				0	he	Close the dialog with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. You will see the profit in column E.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148725				0	he	Calculating with Several Formulas Simultaneously				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3146880				0	he	Delete column E.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3154675				0	he	Enter the following formula in C5: = B5 / B4. You are now calculating the annual profit per item sold.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3148885				0	he	Select the range D2;F11, thus three columns.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3147474				0	he	Choose \<emph\>Data - Multiple Operations\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3154846				0	he	With the cursor in the \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\> field, select cells B5 through C5.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3153931				0	he	Set the cursor in the \<emph\>Columns\</emph\> field and click cell B4.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3150862				0	he	Close the dialog with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. You will now see the profits in column E and the annual profit per item in column F.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146139				0	he	Multiple Operations Across Rows and Columns				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3148584				0	he	\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> allows you to carry out joint multiple operations for columns and rows in so-called cross-tables. The formula cell has to refer to both the data range arranged in rows and the one arranged in columns. Select the range defined by both data ranges and call the multiple operation dialog. Enter the reference to the formula in the \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\> field. The \<emph\>Row input cell\</emph\> and the \<emph\>Column input cell\</emph\> fields are used to enter the reference to the corresponding cells of the formula.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149949				0	he	Calculating with Two Variables				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3154808				0	he	Consider columns A and B of the sample table above. You now want to vary not just the quantity produced annually, but also the selling price, and you are interested in the profit in each case.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149731				0	he	Expand the table shown above. D2 through D11 contain the numbers 500, 1000 and so on, up to 5000. In E1 through H1 enter the numbers 8, 10, 15 and 20.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3152810				0	he	Select the range D1:H11.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3153620				0	he	Choose \<emph\>Data - Multiple Operations\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149981				0	he	With the cursor in the \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\> field, click cell B5.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3156113				0	he	Set the cursor in the \<emph\>Rows\</emph\> field and click cell B1. This means that B1, the selling price, is the horizontally entered variable (with the values 8, 10, 15 and 20).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3154049				0	he	Set the cursor in the \<emph\>Column\</emph\> field and click in B4. This means that B4, the quantity, is the vertically entered variable.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149141				0	he	Close the dialog with OK. You will see the profits in the range E2:H11. In some cases you must first press F9 to update the table.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3155104				0	he	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12060000.xhp\" name=\"Multiple operations\"\>Multiple operations\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	 Importing and Exporting CSV Files 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	bm_id892361				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>number series import\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data series import\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>importing; text databases\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>delimited values and files\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>comma separated files and values\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text file import and export\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>csv files;importing and exporting\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10862				0	he	\<variable id=\"csv_files\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/csv_files.xhp\"\>Opening and Saving Text CSV Files\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10880				0	he	Comma Separated Values (CSV) is text file format that you can use to exchange data from a database or a spreadsheet between applications. Each line in a Text CSV file represents a record in the database, or a row in a spreadsheet. Each field in a database record or cell in a spreadsheet row is usually separated by a comma. However, you can use other characters to delimit a field, such as a tabulator character.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10886				0	he	If the content of a field or cell contains a comma, the contents of the field or cell \<emph\>must\</emph\> be enclosed by single quotes (') or double quotes (").				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10890				0	he	To Open a Text CSV file in Calc				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10897				0	he	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1089F				0	he	Locate the CSV file that you want to open.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN108A2				0	he	If the file has a *.csv extension, select the file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN108A5				0	he	If the CSV file has another extension, select the file, and then select "Text CSV" in the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> box				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1082D				0	he	Click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10834				0	he	The \<emph\>Text Import\</emph\> dialog opens.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN108B1				0	he	Specify the options to divide the text in the file into columns.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN108BB				0	he	You can preview the layout of the imported data at the bottom of the \<emph\>Text Import\</emph\> dialog. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_id8444166				0	he	Right-click a column in the preview to set the format or to hide the column.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN108E2				0	he	If the CSV file uses a text delimiter character that is not listed in the \<emph\>Text delimiter\</emph\> box, click in the box, and type the character.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN108C5				0	he	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN108FA				0	he	To Save a Sheet as a Text CSV File				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN106FC				0	he	When you export a spreadsheet to CSV format, only the data on the current sheet is saved. All other information, including formulas and formatting, is lost.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10901				0	he	Open the Calc sheet that you want to save as a Text CSV file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107AF				0	he	Only the current sheet can be exported.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10905				0	he	Choose \<emph\>File - Save as\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10915				0	he	In the \<emph\>File name\</emph\> box, enter a name for the file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1090D				0	he	In the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> box, select "Text CSV".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107DD				0	he	(Optional) Set the field options for the Text CSV file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1091C				0	he	Select \<emph\>Edit filter settings\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107ED				0	he	In the \<emph\>Export of text files\</emph\> dialog, select the options that you want.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F4				0	he	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107FC				0	he	Click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
