helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id9115573				0	he	If an error occurs, other than #NA, the function returns the error value.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145774				0	he	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3153883				0	he	N(value)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3151101				0	he	\<emph\>Value\</emph\> is the parameter to be converted into a number. N() returns the numeric value if it can. It returns the logical values TRUE and FALSE as 1 and 0 respectively. It returns text and errors as 0.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147097				0	he	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3154117				0	he	N(123) returns 123				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id2337717				0	he	N(TRUE) returns 1				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3153781				0	he	N(FALSE) returns 0				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3154670				0	he	N("abc") returns 0				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3519089				0	he	=N(1/0) returns #DIV/0!				20200411 15:09:53
