helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060115.xhp	0	help	par_id3148753				0	he	BIN2HEX(Number;Places)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060115.xhp	0	help	par_id3155255				0	he	Number: the binary number. The number can have a maximum of 10 places (bits). The most significant bit is the sign bit. Negative numbers are entered as two's complement.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060115.xhp	0	help	par_id3150860				0	he	Places: the number of places to be output.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060115.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155829				0	he	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060115.xhp	0	help	par_id3149686				0	he	=BIN2HEX(1100100;6) returns 000064.				20200411 15:09:53
