helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060115.xhp	0	help	par_id3149293				0	he	HEX2DEC(Number)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060115.xhp	0	help	par_id3159176				0	he	Number: the hexadecimal number. The number can have a maximum of 10 places. The most significant bit is the sign bit, the following bits return the value. Negative numbers are entered as two's complement.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060115.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154304				0	he	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060115.xhp	0	help	par_id3146093				0	he	=HEX2DEC(64) returns 100.				20200411 15:09:53
