helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_id3145389				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:NUMERICFIELD:RID_SCPAGE_TABLE:ED_PAGENO\"\>Enter the number of the first page.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146978				0	he	Scale				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_id3149408				0	he	Defines a page scale for the printed spreadsheet.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_idN1096D				0	he	Scaling mode				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_idN10971				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"sc:ListBox:RID_SCPAGE_TABLE:LB_SCALEMODE\"\>Select a scaling mode from the list box. Appropriate controls will be shown at the side of the list box.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155089				0	he	Reduce/enlarge printout				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_id3159171				0	he	Specifies a scaling factor to scale all printed pages.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_idN1099A				0	he	Scaling factor				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_id3152899				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"SC_METRICFIELD_RID_SCPAGE_TABLE_ED_SCALEALL\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter a scaling factor. Factors less than 100 reduce the pages, higher factors enlarge the pages.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_idN109B2				0	he	Fit print range(s) to width/height				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_idN109B5				0	he	Specifies the maximum number of pages horizontally (width) and vertically (height) on which every sheet with the current Page Style is to be printed. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_idN109BB				0	he	The print ranges are always scaled proportionally, so the resulting number of pages may be less than specified.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_idN109BF				0	he	You may clear one of the boxes, then the unspecified dimension will use as many pages as necessary.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_idN109C3				0	he	If you clear both boxes, this will result in a scaling factor of 100%.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_idN109CE				0	he	Width in pages				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_idN109D1				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"sc:NumericField:RID_SCPAGE_TABLE:ED_SCALEPAGEWIDTH\"\>Enter the maximum number of pages to be printed horizontally across.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_idN109E8				0	he	Height in pages				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_idN109EB				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"sc:NumericField:RID_SCPAGE_TABLE:ED_SCALEPAGEHEIGHT\"\>Enter the maximum number of pages to be printed vertically stacked.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148868				0	he	Fit print range(s) on number of pages				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_id3145074				0	he	Specifies the maximum number of pages on which every sheet with the current Page Style is to be printed. The scale will be reduced as necessary to fit the defined number of pages.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A26				0	he	Number of pages				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_id3144507				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:NUMERICFIELD:RID_SCPAGE_TABLE:ED_SCALEPAGENUM\"\>Enter the maximum number of pages to be printed.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	WEEKDAY 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154925				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>WEEKDAY function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154925				0	he	\<variable id=\"weekday\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/func_weekday.xhp\"\>WEEKDAY\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	par_id3154228				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_WOCHENTAG\"\>Returns the day of the week for the given date value.\</ahelp\> The day is returned as an integer between 1 (Sunday) and 7 (Saturday) if no type or type=1 is specified. If type=2, numbering begins at Monday=1; and if type=3 numbering begins at Monday=0.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147217				0	he	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	par_id3149033				0	he	WEEKDAY(Number; Type)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	par_id3149046				0	he	\<emph\>Number\</emph\>, as a date value, is a decimal for which the weekday is to be returned.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	par_id3154394				0	he	\<emph\>Type\</emph\> determines the type of calculation. For Type =1, the weekdays are counted starting from Sunday (this is the default even when the Type parameter is missing). For Type =2, the weekdays are counted starting from Monday =1. For Type = 3, the weekdays are counted starting from Monday = 0.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	par_id3156188				0	he	These values apply only to the standard date format that you select under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - Calculate\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153836				0	he	Examples				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	par_id3150317				0	he	WEEKDAY("6/14/2000") returns 4 (the Type parameter is missing, therefore the standard count is used. The standard count starts with Sunday as day number 1. June 14, 2000 was a Wednesday and therefore day number 4).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	par_id3153174				0	he	WEEKDAY("7/24/1996";2) returns 3 (the Type parameter is 2, therefore Monday is day number 1. July 24, 1996 was a Wednesday and therefore day number 3).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	par_id3153525				0	he	WEEKDAY("7/24/1996";1) returns 4 (the Type parameter is 1, therefore Sunday is day number 1. July 24, 1996 was a Wednesday and therefore day number 4).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	par_id3150575				0	he	WEEKDAY(NOW()) returns the number of the current day.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	par_id3150588	171			0	he	To obtain a function indicating whether a day in A1 is a business day, use the IF and WEEKDAY functions as follows: IF(WEEKDAY(A1;2)<6;"Business day";"Weekend")				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090105.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Data field				20200411 15:09:53
