helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3163230				0	he	See LINEST. However, no square sum will be returned.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	bm_id3163286				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>SUMPRODUCT function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>scalar products\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>dot products\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inner products\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163286				0	he	SUMPRODUCT				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3163314				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_SUMMENPRODUKT\"\>Multiplies corresponding elements in the given arrays, and returns the sum of those products.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163334				0	he	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3163347				0	he	SUMPRODUCT(Array 1; Array 2...Array 30)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3163362				0	he	\<emph\>Array 1, Array 2...Array 30\</emph\> represent arrays whose corresponding elements are to be multiplied.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_idN11B19				0	he	At least one array must be part of the argument list. If only one array is given, all array elements are summed.				20200411 15:09:53
