helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154511				0	he	MAX				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3153709				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_MAX\"\>Returns the maximum value in a list of arguments.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id9282509				0	he	Returns 0 if no numeric value and no error was encountered in the cell range(s) passed as cell reference(s). Text cells are ignored by MIN() and MAX(). The functions MINA() and MAXA() return 0 if no value (numeric or text) and no error was encountered. Passing a literal string argument to MIN() or MAX(), e.g. MIN("string"), still results in an error.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154256				0	he	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3147340				0	he	MAX(Number 1; Number 2; ...Number 30)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3149568	6			0	he	\<emph\>Number 1; Number 2;...Number 30\</emph\> are numerical values or ranges. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153963				0	he	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3147343				0	he	=MAX(A1;A2;A3;50;100;200) returns the largest value from the list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3148485				0	he	=MAX(A1:B100) returns the largest value from the list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3166426				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>MAXA function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166426				0	he	MAXA				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3150363				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_MAXA\"\>Returns the maximum value in a list of arguments. In opposite to MAX, here you can enter text. The value of the text is 0.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id7689443				0	he	The functions MINA() and MAXA() return 0 if no value (numeric or text) and no error was encountered.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150516				0	he	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3166431				0	he	MAXA(Value 1; Value 2; ... Value 30)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3150202				0	he	\<emph\>Value 1; Value 2;...Value 30\</emph\> are values or ranges. Text has the value of 0.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156290				0	he	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3156446				0	he	=MAXA(A1;A2;A3;50;100;200;"Text") returns the largest value from the list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3149404				0	he	=MAXA(A1:B100) returns the largest value from the list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153820				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>MEDIAN function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153820				0	he	MEDIAN				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3151241				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_MEDIAN\"\>Returns the median of a set of numbers. In a set containing an uneven number of values, the median will be the number in the middle of the set and in a set containing an even number of values, it will be the mean of the two values in the middle of the set.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148871				0	he	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3155264				0	he	MEDIAN(Number 1; Number 2; ...Number 30)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3150109				0	he	\<emph\>Number 1; Number 2;...Number 30\</emph\> are values or ranges, which represent a sample. Each number can also be replaced by a reference.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144506				0	he	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3145078				0	he	for an odd number: =MEDIAN(1; 5; 9; 20; 21) returns 9 as the median value.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3149126				0	he	for an even number: =MEDIAN(1; 5; 9; 20) returns the average of the two middle values 5 and 9, thus 7.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154541				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>MIN function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154541				0	he	MIN				20200411 15:09:53
