helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id2301400				0	he	Returns 0 if no numeric value and no error was encountered in the cell range(s) passed as cell reference(s). Text cells are ignored by MIN() and MAX(). The functions MINA() and MAXA() return 0 if no value (numeric or text) and no error was encountered. Passing a literal string argument to MIN() or MAX(), e.g. MIN("string"), still results in an error.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154651				0	he	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3146964				0	he	MIN(Number 1; Number 2; ...Number 30)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3153486				0	he	\<emph\>Number 1; Number 2;...Number 30\</emph\> are numerical values or ranges.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155523				0	he	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3154734				0	he	=MIN(A1:B100) returns the smallest value in the list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147504				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>MINA function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
