helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090102.xhp	0	help	par_id3155922				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:DataPilotExec\"\>Specify the layout of the table that is generated by the pivot table.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090102.xhp	0	help	par_id3148798				0	he	The pivot table displays data fields as buttons which you can drag and drop to define the pivot table.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090102.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154908				0	he	Layout				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090102.xhp	0	help	par_id3150768	19			0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SC_DPLAY_SELECT\"\>To define the layout of a pivot table, drag and drop data field buttons onto the \<emph\>Page Fields, Row Fields, Column Fields, \</emph\>and\<emph\> Data Fields \</emph\>areas.\</ahelp\> You can also use drag and drop to rearrange the data fields on a pivot table.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090102.xhp	0	help	par_id3147229	20			0	he	$[officename] automatically adds a caption to buttons that are dragged into the \<emph\>Data Fields \</emph\>area. The caption contains the name of the data field as well as the formula that created the data.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090102.xhp	0	help	par_id3145749				0	he	To change the function that is used by a data field, double-click a button in the \<emph\>Data Fields\</emph\> area to open the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12090105.xhp\" name=\"Data Field\"\>Data Field\</link\> dialog. You can also double-click buttons in the \<emph\>Row Fields\</emph\> or \<emph\>Column Fields\</emph\> areas.				20200411 15:09:53
