helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3145241	51			0	he	\<emph\>Mean\</emph\> is the arithmetic mean of the distribution.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3148874	52			0	he	\<emph\>STDEV\</emph\> is the standard deviation of the distribution.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145351				0	he	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3156067	54			0	he	=STANDARDIZE(11; 10; 1) returns 1. The value 11 in a normal distribution with a mean of 10 and a standard deviation of 1 is as much above the mean of 10, as the value 1 is above the mean of the standard normal distribution.				20200411 15:09:53
