helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3156203	216			0	he	=VARPA(A1:A50)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154599				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>PERMUT function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>number of permutations\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154599				0	he	PERMUT				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3154334				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_VARIATIONEN\"\>Returns the number of permutations for a given number of objects.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149422				0	he	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3148466				0	he	PERMUT(Count_1; Count_2)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3148656	148			0	he	\<emph\>Count_1\</emph\> is the total number of objects.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3150826	149			0	he	\<emph\>Count_2\</emph\> is the number of objects in each permutation.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153351				0	he	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3150424	151			0	he	=PERMUT(6; 3) returns 120. There are 120 different possibilities, to pick a sequence of 3 playing cards out of 6 playing cards.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	bm_id3143276				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>PERMUTATIONA function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143276				0	he	PERMUTATIONA				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3144759				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_VARIATIONEN2\"\>Returns the number of permutations for a given number of objects (repetition allowed).\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145598				0	he	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3149298				0	he	PERMUTATIONA(Count_1; Count_2)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3156139	157			0	he	\<emph\>Count_1\</emph\> is the total number of objects.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3149519	158			0	he	\<emph\>Count_2\</emph\> is the number of objects in each permutation.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151382				0	he	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3153949				0	he	How often can 2 objects be selected from a total of 11 objects?				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3149233	161			0	he	PERMUTATIONA(11;2) returns 121.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3150622	162			0	he	PERMUTATIONA(6; 3) returns 216. There are 216 different possibilities to put a sequence of 3 playing cards together out of six playing cards if every card is returned before the next one is drawn.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152952				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>PROB function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152952				0	he	PROB				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3154110				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_WAHRSCHBEREICH\"\>Returns the probability that values in a range are between two limits.\</ahelp\> If there is no \<item type=\"literal\"\>End\</item\> value, this function calculates the probability based on the principle that the Data values are equal to the value of \<item type=\"literal\"\>Start\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146810				0	he	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3147330				0	he	PROB(Data; Probability; Start; End)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3154573	168			0	he	\<emph\>Data\</emph\> is the array or range of data in the sample.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3156334	169			0	he	\<emph\>Probability\</emph\> is the array or range of the corresponding probabilities.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3151107	170			0	he	\<emph\>Start\</emph\> is the start value of the interval whose probabilities are to be summed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3153694	171			0	he	\<emph\>End\</emph\> (optional) is the end value of the interval whose probabilities are to be summed. If this parameter is missing, the probability for the \<emph\>Start \</emph\>value is calculated.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147574				0	he	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3153666	173			0	he	=PROB(A1:A50; B1:B50; 50; 60) returns the probability with which a value within the range of A1:A50 is also within the limits between 50 and 60. Every value within the range of A1:A50 has a probability within the range of B1:B50.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150941				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>WEIBULL function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150941				0	he	WEIBULL				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3154916				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_WEIBULL\"\>Returns the values of the Weibull distribution.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id0305200911372767				0	he	The Weibull distribution is a continuous probability distribution, with parameters Alpha > 0 (shape) and Beta > 0 (scale). 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id0305200911372777				0	he	If C is 0, WEIBULL calculates the probability density function.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id0305200911372743				0	he	If C is 1, WEIBULL calculates the cumulative distribution function.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159393				0	he	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3154478				0	he	WEIBULL(Number; Alpha; Beta; C)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3151317	179			0	he	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the value at which to calculate the Weibull distribution.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3158436	180			0	he	\<emph\>Alpha \</emph\>is the Alpha parameter of the Weibull distribution.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3154668	181			0	he	\<emph\>Beta\</emph\> is the Beta parameter of the Weibull distribution.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3154825	182			0	he	            \<emph\>C\</emph\> indicates the type of function.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153794				0	he	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3146077	184			0	he	=WEIBULL(2; 1; 1; 1) returns 0.86.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id0305200911372899				0	he	See also the \<link href=\"https://wiki.openoffice.org/wiki/Documentation/How_Tos/Calc:_WEIBULL_function\"\>Wiki page\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
