helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3156060				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ODER\"\>Returns TRUE if at least one argument is TRUE.\</ahelp\> This function returns the value FALSE, if all the arguments have the logical value FALSE.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3148771				0	he	The arguments are either logical expressions themselves (TRUE, 1<5, 2+3=7, B8<10) that return logical values, or arrays (A1:C3) containing logical values.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3153546				0	he	When a function expects a single value, but you entered a cell range, then the value from the cell range is taken that is in the same column or row as the formula.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3149027				0	he	If the entered range is outside of the current column or row of the formula, the function returns the error value #VALUE!				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155517				0	he	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3150468				0	he	OR(Logical value 1; Logical value 2 ...Logical value 30)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3155819	24			0	he	\<emph\>Logical value 1; Logical value 2 ...Logical value 30\</emph\> are conditions to be checked. All conditions can be either TRUE or FALSE. If a range is entered as a parameter, the function uses the value from the range that is in the current column or row.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153228				0	he	Examples:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3154870				0	he	The logical values of entries 12<11; 13>22, and 45=45 are to be checked.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3155371	27			0	he	OR(12<11; 13>22; 45=45) returns TRUE.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3158412	59			0	he	OR(FALSE;TRUE) returns TRUE.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148394K				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>XOR function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148394K				0	he	XOR				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3156060K				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ODER\"\>Returns the exclusive "or" of arguments.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3148771K				0	he	The arguments are either numbers, logical expressions themselves (TRUE, 1<5, 2+3=7, B8<10) that return logical values, or arrays (A1:C3).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3149027K				0	he	If the entered range is outside of the current column or row of the formula, the function returns the error value #VALUE!				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155517K				0	he	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3150468K				0	he	XOR(Value1; Value2 ...Value30)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3155819K				0	he	\<emph\>Value1; Value2 ...Value30\</emph\> are added modulo 2. TRUE is returned if the result of this addition is 1;FALSE is returned if the result of this addition is 0.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153228K				0	he	Examples:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3155371K				0	he	\<item type=\"input\"\>=XOR(12<11;13>22;10)\</item\> returns TRUE since this converts to (1+0+10) mod 2 = 0				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3158412K				0	he	\<item type=\"input\"\>=XOR(FALSE;TRUE)\</item\> returns TRUE.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Mathematical Functions				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147124				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>mathematical functions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Function Wizard; mathematical\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>functions; mathematical functions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>trigonometric functions\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147124				0	he	Mathematical Functions				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3154943				0	he	\<variable id=\"mathematiktext\"\>This category contains the \<emph\>Mathematical\</emph\> functions for Calc.\</variable\> To open the \<emph\>Function Wizard\</emph\>, choose \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060000.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Function\"\>\<emph\>Insert - Function\</emph\>\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146944				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>ABS function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>absolute values\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>values;absolute\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146944				0	he	ABS				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3154546				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ABS\"\>Returns the absolute value of a number.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154843				0	he	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3147475				0	he	ABS(Number)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3148438				0	he	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the value whose absolute value is to be calculated.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155823				0	he	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152787				0	he	Entering the value -56 will return an absolute value of 56.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3148752				0	he	Entering the value 56 will return an absolute value of 56.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id320139				0	he	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ABS(0)\</item\> returns 0.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150896				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>COUNTBLANK function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>counting;empty cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>empty cells;counting\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150896				0	he	COUNTBLANK				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155260				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ANZAHLLEEREZELLEN\"\>Returns the number of empty cells.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145144				0	he	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3153931				0	he	COUNTBLANK(range)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3149512				0	he	\<emph\>range\</emph\> is the cell range in which the empty cells are counted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146139				0	he	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3148586				0	he	Entering = COUNTBLANK (A1:C3) in an empty cell range results in 9.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153114				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>ACOS function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153114				0	he	ACOS				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145163				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ARCCOS\"\>Returns the inverse trigonometric cosine of a number.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
