helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3150020				0	he	ACOS(Number)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3159134				0	he	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the value, whose inverse trigonometric cosine value is to be calculated.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id679647				0	he	To return the angle in degrees, use the DEGREES function.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149882				0	he	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3150128				0	he	The inverse trigonometric cosine of -1 returns the value 3.14.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id8792382				0	he	\<item type=\"input\"\>=DEGREES(ACOS(0.5))\</item\> returns 60. The cosine of 60 degrees is 0.5.				20200411 15:09:53
