helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060199.xhp	0	help	par_id3154949				0	he	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060199.xhp	0	help	par_id3156257				0	he	: (Colon)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060199.xhp	0	help	par_id3153924				0	he	Range				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060199.xhp	0	help	par_id3148432				0	he	A1:C108				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060199.xhp	0	help	par_id3152592				0	he	! (Exclamation point)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060199.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150606				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>intersection operator\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060199.xhp	0	help	par_id3150606				0	he	Intersection				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060199.xhp	0	help	par_id3083445				0	he	SUM(A1:B6!B5:C12)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060199.xhp	0	help	par_id3150385				0	he	Calculates the sum of all cells in the intersection; in this example, the result yields the sum of cells B5 and B6.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060199.xhp	0	help	par_id4003723				0	he	~ (Tilde)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060199.xhp	0	help	par_id838953				0	he	Concatenation or union				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060199.xhp	0	help	par_id2511978				0	he	Takes two references and returns a reference list, which is a concatenation of the left reference followed by the right reference. Double entries are referenced twice. See note below this table.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060199.xhp	0	help	par_id181890				0	he	Reference concatenation using a tilde character was implemented lately. When a formula with the tilde operator exists in a document that is opened in old versions of the software, an error is returned. A reference list is not allowed inside an array expression.				20200411 15:09:53
