helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3145560				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_TBILLYIELD\"\>Calculates the yield of a treasury bill.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145578				0	he	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3156077				0	he	TBILLYIELD(Settlement;Maturity;Price)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3156091				0	he	\<emph\>Settlement\</emph\> is the date of purchase of the security.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3157856				0	he	\<emph\>Maturity\</emph\> is the date on which the security matures (expires).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3149627				0	he	Price: the price (purchase price) of the treasury bill per 100 currency units of par value.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149642				0	he	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3145178				0	he	Settlement date: March 31 1999, maturity date: June 1 1999, price: 98.45 currency units.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3145193				0	he	The yield of the treasury bill is worked out as follows:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3148528				0	he	=TBILLYIELD("3/31/99";"6/1/99"; 98.45) returns 0.091417 or 9.1417 per cent.				20200411 15:09:53
