helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_id3146969				0	he	Time				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155066				0	he	All numbers corresponding to the condition. The entered values are formatted accordingly the next time the dialog is called up.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A0				0	he	Cell range				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A5				0	he	Allow only values that are given in a cell range. The cell range can be specified explicitly, or as a named database range, or as a named range. The range may consist of one column or one row of cells. If you specify a range of columns and rows, only the first column is used.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AB				0	he	List				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B0				0	he	Allow only values or strings specified in a list. Strings and values can be mixed. Numbers evaluate to their value, so if you enter the number 1 in the list, the entry 100% is also valid.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154756				0	he	Text length				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147339				0	he	Entries whose length corresponds to the condition.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154704				0	he	Allow empty cells				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153967				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:TRISTATEBOX:TP_VALIDATION_VALUES:TSB_ALLOW_BLANKS\"\>In conjunction with \<emph\>Tools - Detective - Mark invalid Data\</emph\>, this defines that empty cells are shown as invalid data (disabled) or not (enabled).\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_idN10709				0	he	Show selection list				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_idN1070D				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"sc:CheckBox:TP_VALIDATION_VALUES:CB_SHOWLIST\"\>Shows a list of all valid strings or values to select from. The list can also be opened by selecting the cell and pressing Ctrl+D (Mac: Command+D).\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_idN10724				0	he	Sort entries ascending				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_idN10728				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"sc:CheckBox:TP_VALIDATION_VALUES:CB_SORTLIST\"\>Sorts the selection list in ascending order and filters duplicates from the list. If not checked, the order from the data source is taken.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
