helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Edit Print Ranges				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153088				0	he	Edit Print Ranges				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	par_id3159488				0	he	\<variable id=\"druckbereichetext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:EditPrintArea\"\>Opens a dialog where you can specify the print range.\</ahelp\>\</variable\> You can also set the rows or columns which are to be repeated in every page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	par_idN105AE				0	he	\<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/guide/printranges.xhp#printranges\"/\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156281				0	he	Print range				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	par_id3147228				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:EDIT:RID_SCDLG_AREAS:ED_PRINTAREA\"\>Allows you to modify a defined print range.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	par_id3145174				0	he	Select \<emph\>-none-\</emph\> to remove a print range definition for the current spreadsheet. Select \<emph\>-entire sheet-\</emph\> to set the current sheet as a print range. Select \<emph\>-selection-\</emph\> to define the selected area of a spreadsheet as the print range. By selecting \<emph\>-user-defined-\</emph\>, you can define a print range that you have already defined using the \<emph\>Format - Print Ranges - Define\</emph\> command. If you have given a name to a range using the \<emph\>Insert - Names - Define\</emph\> command, this name will be displayed and can be selected from the list box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	par_id3145272				0	he	In the right-hand text box, you can enter a print range by reference or by name. If the cursor is in the \<emph\>Print range\</emph\> text box, you can also select the print range in the spreadsheet with your mouse.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149260				0	he	Rows to repeat				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	par_id3147426				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:EDIT:RID_SCDLG_AREAS:ED_REPEATROW\"\>Choose one or more rows to print on every page. In the right text box enter the row reference, for example, "1" or "$1" or "$2:$3".\</ahelp\> The list box displays \<emph\>-user defined-\</emph\>. You can also select \<emph\>-none-\</emph\> to remove a defined repeating row.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	par_id3155418				0	he	You can also define repeating rows by dragging the mouse in the spreadsheet, if the cursor is in the \<emph\>Rows to repeat\</emph\> text field in the dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149581				0	he	Columns to repeat				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	par_id3155602				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:EDIT:RID_SCDLG_AREAS:ED_REPEATCOL\"\>Choose one or more columns to print on every page. In the right text box enter the column reference, for example, "A" or "AB" or "$C:$E".\</ahelp\> The list box then displays \<emph\>-user defined-\</emph\>. You can also select \<emph\>-none-\</emph\> to remove a defined repeating column.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	par_id3150749				0	he	You can also define repeating columns by dragging the mouse in the spreadsheet, if the cursor is in the \<emph\>Columns to repeat\</emph\> text field in the dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_second.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	SECOND 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_second.xhp	0	help	bm_id3159390				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>SECOND function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_second.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159390				0	he	\<variable id=\"second\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/func_second.xhp\"\>SECOND\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_second.xhp	0	help	par_id3148974				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_SEKUNDE\"\>Returns the second for the given time value.\</ahelp\> The second is given as an integer between 0 and 59.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_second.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154362				0	he	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_second.xhp	0	help	par_id3148407				0	he	SECOND(Number)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_second.xhp	0	help	par_id3155904				0	he	\<emph\>Number\</emph\>, as a time value, is a decimal, for which the second is to be returned.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_second.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149992				0	he	Examples				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_second.xhp	0	help	par_id3153350				0	he	SECOND(NOW()) returns the current second				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_second.xhp	0	help	par_id3150831				0	he	SECOND(C4) returns 17 if contents of C4 = 12:20:17.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060200.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Protecting document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150541				0	he	Protecting document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145172				0	he	\<variable id=\"dokumenttext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ToolProtectionDocument\"\>Protects the sheet structure of your document from modifications. It is impossible to insert, delete, rename, move or copy sheets.\</ahelp\>\</variable\> Open the \<emph\>Protect document\</emph\> dialog with \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document - Document\</emph\>. Optionally enter a password and click OK.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153188				0	he	The structure of protected spreadsheet documents can be changed only if the \<emph\>Protect\</emph\> option is disabled. On the context menus for the spreadsheet tabs at the lower graphic border, only the menu item \<emph\>Select All Sheets\</emph\> can be activated. All other menu items are deactivated. To remove the protection, call up the command \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document - Document\</emph\> again. If no password is assigned, protection is immediately removed. If you were assigned a password, the \<emph\>Remove Spreadsheet Protection\</emph\> dialog appears, in which you must enter the password. Only then can you remove the check mark specifying that protection is active.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145750	7			0	he	A protected document, once saved, can only be saved again with the \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\> menu command. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152596				0	he	Password (optional)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155412				0	he	You can create a password to protect your document against unauthorized or accidental modifications.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150717	9			0	he	You can completely protect your work by combining both options from \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document\</emph\>, including password entry. If you want to prevent the document from being opened by other users, select \<emph\>Save With Password \</emph\>and click the \<emph\>Save\</emph\> button. The \<emph\>Enter Password\</emph\> dialog appears. Consider carefully when choosing a password; if you forget it after you close a document you will be unable to access the document.				20200411 15:09:53
