helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3155266	49			0	he	Click the \<emph\>Text\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3156450\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_text.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3156450\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> and move the mouse pointer to where you want to enter the text box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3149052				0	he	Drag a text frame to the size you want in your document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3151194				0	he	Type or paste your text in the text frame.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145118				0	he	Double-click the text to edit it or to format text properties, such as font size or font color. Click the border of the text object to edit the object properties, such as border color or arranging in front or behind other objects.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150437				0	he	Fitting Text to Frames				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3146877				0	he	Create a text frame as described in the steps above. The size of the frame determines the size of the text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN108A3				0	he	With the text object selected, choose \<emph\>Format - Text\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Text\</emph\> dialog opens.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN108AF				0	he	On the \<emph\>Text\</emph\> tab page, clear the \<emph\>Fit height to text\</emph\> checkbox, then select the \<emph\>Fit to frame\</emph\> checkbox. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id0610200902133994				0	he	Now you can resize the text box to change the size and shape of the text characters.				20200411 15:09:53
