helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155628				0	he	\<variable id=\"keyboard\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/keyboard.xhp\" name=\"Shortcut Keys for Drawing Objects\"\>Shortcut Keys for Drawing Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148663				0	he	You can create and edit drawing objects using the keyboard.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3125863				0	he	To Create and Edit a Drawing Object				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153188				0	he	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>F6\</item\> to navigate to the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> bar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3146971				0	he	Press the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Right\</item\> arrow key until you reach the toolbar icon of a drawing tool.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_idN106CD				0	he	If there is an arrow next to the icon, the drawing tool opens a sub toolbar. Press the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Up\</item\> or \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Down\</item\> arrow key to open the sub toolbar, then press the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Right\</item\> or \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Left\</item\> key to select an icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3147338				0	he	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154705				0	he	The object is created at the center of the current document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155962				0	he	To return to the document, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+F6\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155062				0	he	You can use the arrow keys to position the object where you want. To choose a command from the context menu for the object, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Shift+F10\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150306				0	he	To Select an Object				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3152990				0	he	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+F6\</item\> to enter the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145587				0	he	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Tab\</item\> until you reach the object you want to select.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Creating Gradient Fills				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150792				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>gradients; applying and defining\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing;gradients\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defining;gradients\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>applying;gradients\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>custom gradients\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>transparency;adjusting\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150792	3			0	he	\<variable id=\"gradient\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/gradient.xhp\" name=\"Creating Gradient Fills\"\>Creating Gradient Fills\</link\> \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3154012				0	he	A gradient fill is an incremental blend of two different colors, or shades of the same color, that you can apply to a drawing object.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147436				0	he	To apply a gradient:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3146974				0	he	Select a drawing object.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3154491				0	he	Choose \<emph\>Format - Area\</emph\> and select \<emph\>Gradient\</emph\> as the \<emph\>Fill\</emph\> type.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3153415				0	he	Select a gradient style from the list and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154702				0	he	Creating Custom Gradients				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3145791				0	he	You can define your own gradients and modify existing gradients, as well as save and load a list of gradient files.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145384				0	he	To create a custom gradient:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3151242				0	he	Choose \<emph\>Format - Area\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Gradients\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3150046				0	he	Select a gradient from the list to use as the basis for your new gradient and click \<emph\>Add\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3145116				0	he	Type a name for the gradient in the text box and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id6535843				0	he	The name appears at the end of the gradient list and is selected for editing.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3150391				0	he	Set the gradient properties and click \<emph\>Modify\</emph\> to save the gradient.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3156396	16			0	he	Click \<emph\>OK.\</emph\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149947				0	he	Using Gradients and Transparency				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3157905				0	he	You can adjust the properties of a gradient as well as the transparency of a drawing object with your mouse.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150653				0	he	To adjust the gradient of a drawing object:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3154844				0	he	Select a drawing object with the gradient that you want to modify.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3145592				0	he	Choose \<emph\>Format - Area\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Gradients\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_idN107BE				0	he	Adjust the values for the gradient to suit your needs and click \<emph\>Ok\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3150659				0	he	To adjust the transparency of an object, select the object, choose \<emph\>Format - Area\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Transparency\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Drawing Sectors and Segments				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146974				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>sectors of circles/ellipses\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>segments of circles/ellipses\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>circle segments\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>ellipses; segments\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>drawing; sectors and segments\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146974				0	he	\<variable id=\"draw_sector\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/draw_sector.xhp\" name=\"Drawing Sectors and Segments\"\>Drawing Sectors and Segments\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3147396				0	he	The \<emph\>Ellipse\</emph\> toolbar contains tools for drawing ellipses and circles. You can also draw segments and sectors of circles and ellipses.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151075				0	he	To draw a sector of a circle or an ellipse:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3155335	33			0	he	Open the \<emph\>Ellipses\</emph\> toolbar and click one of the \<emph\>Circle Pie\</emph\> or \<emph\>Ellipse Pie\</emph\> icons \<image id=\"img_id3155768\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_circlepie_unfilled.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3155768\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>. The mouse pointer changes to a cross hair with a small icon of a sector.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3150199				0	he	Position the pointer at the edge of the circle you want to draw and drag to create the circle.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3148868				0	he	To create a circle by dragging from the center, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> while dragging.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3145361				0	he	Release the mouse button when the circle has reached the size you want. A line corresponding to the circle radius appears in the circle.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3149872				0	he	Position the pointer where you want to place the first boundary of the sector and click.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3157871				0	he	As the radius line that follows the pointer is constrained to the circle boundaries, you can click anywhere in the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3146874				0	he	Position the pointer where you want to place the second boundary of the sector and click. The completed sector is displayed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3148581				0	he	To draw a segment of a circle or ellipse, follow the steps for creating a sector based on a circle.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3153084				0	he	To draw an arc based on an ellipse, choose one of the arc icons and follow the same steps for creating a sector based on a circle.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Arranging, Aligning and Distributing Objects				20200411 15:09:53
