helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id8611102				0	he	כדי להוסיף מספר עמוד למקום הסמן בטקסט יש לבחור \<emph\>הוספה - שדות - מספר עמוד\</emph\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id6604510				0	he	אם מופיע "Page number" במקום מספר העמוד, יש לבחור \<emph\>תצוגה - שמות שדות\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id2678914				0	he	למרות זאת, שדות אלו ישנו מיקום עם הוספת או מחיקת טקסט. לכן, מומלץ להוסיף את שדה מספר העמוד לכותרת העליונה או התחתונה. אלו אינם משנים את המיקום שלהם ונראים אותו דבר לאורך כל המסמך.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id614642				0	he	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Header - (name of page style)\</emph\> or \<emph\>Insert - Footer - (name of page style)\</emph\> to add a header or footer to all pages with the current Page Style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id2551652				0	he	Starting with a defined page number				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id6111941				0	he	Now you want some more control on page numbers. You are writing a text document that should start with page number 12.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id5757621				0	he	Click into the first paragraph of your document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id2632831				0	he	Choose \<emph\>Format - Paragraph - Text flow\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id4395275				0	he	In the Breaks area, enable \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>. Enable \<emph\>With Page Style\</emph\> just to be able to set the new \<emph\>Page number\</emph\>. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id1654408				0	he	The new page number is an attribute of the first paragraph of the page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id7519150				0	he	Formatting the page number style				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id9029206				0	he	You want roman page numbers running i, ii, iii, iv, and so on.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3032319				0	he	Double-click directly before the page number field. You see the \<emph\>Edit Fields\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id9139378				0	he	Select a number format and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id5051728				0	he	Using different page number styles				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id1558885				0	he	You need some pages with the roman numbering style, followed by the remaining pages in another style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id1541184				0	he	In Writer, you will need different Page Styles. The first Page Style has a footer with a page number field formatted for roman numbers. The following Page Style has a footer with a page number field formatted in another look.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id18616				0	he	Both Page Styles must be separated by a page break. In Writer, you can have automatic page breaks and manually inserted page breaks.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id6138492				0	he	An \<emph\>automatic page break\</emph\> appears at the end of a page when the Page Style has a different "next style".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id4569231				0	he	For example, the "First Page" page style has "Default" as the next style. To see this, you may press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command+T\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>F11\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> to open the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Styles and Formatting\</item\> window, click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Page Styles\</item\> icon, right-click the First Page entry. Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Modify\</item\> from the context menu. On the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Organizer\</item\> tab, you can see the "next style".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id291451				0	he	A \<emph\>manually inserted page break\</emph\> can be applied without or with a change of page styles.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3341776				0	he	If you just press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+Enter\</item\>, you apply a page break without a change of styles.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id5947141				0	he	If you choose \<emph\>Insert - Manual break\</emph\>, you can insert a page break without or with a change of style or with a change of page number.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id1911679				0	he	It depends on your document what is best: to use a manually inserted page break between Page Styles, or to use an automatic change. If you just need one title page with a different style than the other pages, you can use the automatic method:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id9364909				0	he	To apply a different page style to the first page				20200411 15:09:53
