helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3155858				0	he	Use the AutoFormat feature to remove line breaks that occur within sentences. Unwanted line breaks can occur when you copy text from another source and paste it into a text document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3153413	3			0	he	This AutoFormat feature only works on text that is formatted with the "Default" paragraph style. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3153138	5			0	he	יש לבחור \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>כלים - אפשרויות תיקון אוטומטי\</item\>.            				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3149645				0	he	On the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab, ensure that \<emph\>Combine single line paragraphs if length greater than 50%\</emph\> is selected. To change the minimum percentage for the line length, double-click the option in the list, and then enter a new percentage.				20200411 15:09:53
