helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\reset_format.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Resetting Font Attributes				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\reset_format.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149963				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>formats; resetting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>font attributes; resetting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>fonts; resetting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>resetting; fonts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>direct formatting;exiting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting;exiting direct formatting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exiting direct formatting\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\reset_format.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149963				0	he	\<variable id=\"reset_format\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/reset_format.xhp\" name=\"Resetting Font Attributes\"\>Resetting Font Attributes\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\reset_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3154091				0	he	You can quickly exit manual formatting by pressing the right-arrow key. For example, if you are pressed Ctrl+B to apply the bold typeface to the text that you type, press the right arrow to return to the default character format of the paragraph.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\reset_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3155854				0	he	To reset all direct formatting of existing text, select that text, then choose the menu command \<emph\>Format - Default Formatting\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Changing the Case of Text				20200411 15:09:53
