helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id090220080439090				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Lists the available field types. To add a field to your document, click a field type, click a field in the \<emph\>Select \</emph\>list, and then click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3154196				0	he	Field type				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3149484				0	he	Meaning				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3149096				0	he	Any Record				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3151257				0	he	Inserts the contents of the database field that you specify in the \<emph\>Record Number\</emph\> box as a mail merge field if the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090200.xhp\" name=\"Condition\"\>\<emph\>Condition\</emph\>\</link\> that you enter is met. Only records selected by a multiple selection in the data source view are considered.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3147100				0	he	You can use this field to insert several records into a document. Simply insert the \<emph\>Any Record\</emph\> field in front of the form letter fields that use a certain record.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3153632				0	he	Database Name				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3152776	9			0	he	Inserts the name of the database table selected in the \<emph\>Database selection \</emph\>box. The "Database Name" field is a global field, that is, if you insert a different database name in your document, the contents of all previously inserted "Database Name" fields are updated.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3149167				0	he	Mail merge field				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3145779				0	he	Inserts the name of a database field as a placeholder, so that you can create a mail merge document. The field content is automatically inserted when you print the form letter.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3151372				0	he	Next record				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3150114				0	he	Inserts the contents of the next mail merge field in your document, if the condition that you define is met. The records that you want to include must be selected in the data source view.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3155861				0	he	You can use the "Next record" field to insert the contents of consecutive records between the mail merge fields in a document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3147412				0	he	Record number				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3147495				0	he	Inserts the number of the selected database record.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149565				0	he	Database Selection				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3145268				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DB_SELECTION_TLB\"\>Select the database table or the database query that you want the field to refer to.\</ahelp\> You can include fields from more than one database or query in a document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id0902200804391084				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>For fields linked to a condition, enter the criteria here.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3147739				0	he	If you want, you can assign a condition that must be met before the contents of the "Any Record" and "Next Record" fields are inserted. The default condition is "True", that is, the condition is always true if you do not change the condition text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146336				0	he	Record number				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3149836				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:EDIT:TP_FLD_DB:ED_DBSETNUMBER\"\>Enter the number of the record that you want to insert when the condition that you specify is met.\</ahelp\> The record number corresponds to the current selection in the data source view. For example, if you select the last 5 records in a database containing 10 records, the number of the first record will be 1, and not 6.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3153305				0	he	If you refer to fields in a different database (or in a different table or query within the same database), $[officename] determines the record number relative to the current selection.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156109				0	he	Format				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3156122				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Select the format of the field that you want to insert. This option is available for numerical, boolean, date and time fields.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150904				0	he	From database				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3150922				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:RADIOBUTTON:TP_FLD_DB:RB_DBOWNFORMAT\"\>Uses the format defined in the selected database.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_idN1076E				0	he	Browse				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_idN10772				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"878711313\"\>Opens a file open dialog where you can select a database file (*.odb). The selected file is added to the Databases Selection list.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155084				0	he	User defined				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3154333				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:RADIOBUTTON:TP_FLD_DB:RB_DBFORMAT\"\>Applies the format that you select in the \<emph\>List of user-defined formats\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146948				0	he	List of user-defined formats				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3150093				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:TP_FLD_DB:LB_DBFORMAT\"\>Lists the available user-defined formats.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_idN107FF				0	he	Printing a form letter				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_idN10803				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>When you print a document that contains database fields, a dialog asks you if you want to print a form letter. If you answer Yes, the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/01150000.xhp\"\>Mail Merge\</link\> dialog opens where you can select the database records to print.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_idN10812				0	he	Do not show warning again				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_idN10816				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Suppresses this dialog from now on. There is no easy way to get it back!\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05040000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Page Style				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05040000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150016				0	he	Page Style				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148774				0	he	\<variable id=\"seitetext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:PageDialog\"\>Specify the formatting styles and the layout for the current page style, including page margins, headers and footers, and the page background.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\03090000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Fields				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\03090000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154505				0	he	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/03090000.xhp\" name=\"Fields\"\>Field Names\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\03090000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147171				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Fieldnames\"\>Switches the field display between field names and field contents.\</ahelp\> A check mark indicates that the field names are displayed, and no check mark indicates that field contents are displayed. Some field contents cannot be displayed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\03090000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149287	4			0	he	To change the default field display to field names instead of the field contents, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - View\</emph\>, and then select the\<emph\> Field codes \</emph\>checkbox in the \<emph\>Display\</emph\> area.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\03090000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154098				0	he	When you print a document with \<emph\>View - Field Names\</emph\> enabled, you are prompted to include the field names in the print out.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\03090000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145579				0	he	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090000.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Fields\"\>Insert - Fields\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Apply				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	bm_id5028839				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>automatic heading formatting\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	bm_id				0	he	\<bookmark_value\>AutoCorrect function;headings\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>headings;automatic\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>separator lines;AutoCorrect function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155962				0	he	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05150200.xhp\" name=\"Apply\"\>Apply\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149871	2			0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:AutoFormatApply\"\>Automatically formats the file according to the options that you set under \<emph\>Tools - AutoCorrect\</emph\>            \<emph\>Options\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147404				0	he	When you apply automatic formats, the following rules apply:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155625				0	he	AutoFormat for Headings				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154505				0	he	A paragraph is formatted as a heading when the following conditions are met:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145241				0	he	paragraph begins with a capital letter				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148386				0	he	paragraph does not end with a punctuation mark				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150564				0	he	empty paragraph above and below the paragraph				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149030				0	he	AutoFormat for Bullets / Numbering				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156316				0	he	To create a bulleted list, type a hyphen (-), star (*), or plus sign (+), followed by a space or tab at the beginning of a paragraph.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150763	18			0	he	To create a numbered list, type a number followed by a period (.), followed by a space or tab at the beginning of a paragraph. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147507				0	he	Automatic numbering is only applied to paragraphs formatted with the \<emph\>Standard\</emph\>, \<emph\>Text body\</emph\> or \<emph\>Text body indent\</emph\> paragraph styles.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152941				0	he	AutoFormat for Separator Lines				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154105				0	he	If you type three or more hyphens (---), underscores (___) or equal signs (===) on line and then press Enter, the paragraph is replaced by a horizontal line as wide as the page. The line is actually the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05030500.xhp\" name=\"lower border\"\>lower border\</link\> of the preceding paragraph. The following rules apply:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153530				0	he	Three hyphens (-) yield a single line (0.05 pt thick, gap 0.75 mm).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154477				0	he	Three underscore (_) yield a single line (1 pt thick, gap 0.75 mm).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150982				0	he	Three equal signs (=) yield a double line (1.10 pt thick, gap 0.75 mm).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120211.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Index				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120211.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150018				0	he	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04120211.xhp\" name=\"Index\"\>Index\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120211.xhp	0	help	par_id3150570	2			0	he	\<variable id=\"verzeichnis\"\>The following options are available when you select \<emph\>Table of Contents \</emph\>as the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04120210.xhp\" name=\"index\"\>index\</link\> type. \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120211.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150763				0	he	Type and Title				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120211.xhp	0	help	par_id3149286				0	he	Specify the type and title of the index.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120211.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151171				0	he	Type				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120211.xhp	0	help	par_id3145418				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:TP_TOX_SELECT:LB_TYPE\"\>Select the type of index that you want to insert.\</ahelp\> The options available on this tab depend on the index type that you select. If the cursor is in an index when you choose the \<emph\>Insert - Indexes and Tables - Indexes and Tables\</emph\>, you can then edit that index.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120211.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149801				0	he	Title				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120211.xhp	0	help	par_id3153532				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:EDIT:TP_TOX_SELECT:ED_TITLE\"\>Enter a title for the selected index.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120211.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151317				0	he	Protected against manual changes				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120211.xhp	0	help	par_id3153665	10			0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:CHECKBOX:TP_TOX_SELECT:CB_READONLY\"\>Prevents the contents of the index from being changed.\</ahelp\> Manual changes that you make to an index are lost when the index is refreshed. If you want the cursor to scroll through a protected area, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Formatting Aids\</emph\>, and then select the \<emph\>Cursor in protected areas - Enabled \</emph\>check box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120211.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155893				0	he	Create index for				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120211.xhp	0	help	par_id3149688				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:TP_TOX_SELECT:LB_AREA\"\>Select whether to create the index for the document or for the current chapter.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120211.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154199				0	he	Evaluation level				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120211.xhp	0	help	par_id3143270				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:NUMERICFIELD:TP_TOX_SELECT:NF_LEVEL\"\>Enter the number of heading levels to include in the index.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120211.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149484				0	he	Create from				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120211.xhp	0	help	par_id3149096				0	he	Use this area to specify which information to include in an index.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120211.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149815				0	he	Outline				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120211.xhp	0	help	par_id3151253				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:CHECKBOX:TP_TOX_SELECT:CB_FROMHEADINGS\"\>Creates the index using outline levels, that is, paragraphs formatted with one of the predefined heading styles (Heading 1-10) are added to the index.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120211.xhp	0	help	par_id1209200804373840				0	he	You can also assign the outline levels in the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05030800.xhp\"\>Outline & Numbering\</link\> tab page of the Format - Paragraph dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120211.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153633				0	he	Additional Styles				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120211.xhp	0	help	par_id3152772				0	he	\<variable id=\"vorlg\"\>\<ahelp hid=\"SW:CHECKBOX:TP_TOX_SELECT:CB_ADDSTYLES\"\>Includes the paragraph styles that you specify in the \<emph\>Assign Styles\</emph\> dialog as index entries. To select the paragraph styles that you want to include in the index, click the \<emph\>Assign Styles (...\</emph\>) button to the right of this box.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120211.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149168				0	he	...				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120211.xhp	0	help	par_id3145776				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:PUSHBUTTON:TP_TOX_SELECT:PB_ADDSTYLES\"\>Opens the \<emph\>Assign Styles\</emph\> dialog, where you can select the paragraph styles to include in the index.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120211.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151374				0	he	Index marks				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120211.xhp	0	help	par_id3155861				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:CHECKBOX:TP_TOX_SELECT:CB_TOXMARKS\"\>Includes the index entries that you inserted by choosing \<emph\>Insert - Indexes and Tables - Entry\</emph\> in the index.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05040501.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Options				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05040501.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149871				0	he	Options				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05040501.xhp	0	help	par_id3148569				0	he	Specifies the number of columns and the column layout for the section.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05040501.xhp	0	help	par_id3151390				0	he	Sections follow the text flow behavior of the page they are inserted into.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05040501.xhp	0	help	par_id3083448				0	he	For example, if you insert a section that uses a two-column layout into a page style that uses a four-column layout, the two-column layout is nested inside one of the four columns.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05040501.xhp	0	help	par_id3155625				0	he	You can also nest sections, that is, you can insert a section into another section.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05100400.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Unprotect				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05100400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149052				0	he	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05100400.xhp\" name=\"Unprotect\"\>Unprotect\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05100400.xhp	0	help	par_id3083450				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:UnsetCellsReadOnly\"\>Removes the cell protection for all selected cells in the current table.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05100400.xhp	0	help	par_id3154558	3			0	he	To remove the protection from several tables at once, select the tables, and then press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+T. To remove the protection from all of the tables in a document, click anywhere in the document, and then press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+T.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05100400.xhp	0	help	par_id3150765				0	he	You can also remove cell protection from a table in the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/02110000.xhp\" name=\"Navigator\"\>Navigator\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120212.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	Index				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120212.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147338				0	he	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04120212.xhp\" name=\"Index\"\>Index\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120212.xhp	0	help	par_id3155962	2			0	he	\<variable id=\"verzeichnis\"\>The following options are available when you select \<emph\>Alphabetical Index \</emph\>as the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04120210.xhp\" name=\"index\"\>index\</link\> type. \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120212.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153247				0	he	Options				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120212.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154651				0	he	Combine identical entries				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120212.xhp	0	help	par_id3153810				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_CHECKBOX_TP_TOX_SELECT_CB_COLLECTSAME\"\>Replaces identical index entries with a single entry that lists the page numbers where the entry occurs in the document. For example, the entries "View 10, View 43" are combined as "View 10, 43".\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120212.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147403				0	he	Combine identical entries with p or pp				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120212.xhp	0	help	par_id3083451				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_CHECKBOX_TP_TOX_SELECT_CB_USEFF\"\>Replaces identical index entries, which occur also on the directly following page or pages, with a single entry that lists the first page number and a "p" or "pp". For example, the entries "View 10, View 11, View 12" are combined as "View 10pp", and "View 10, View 11" as "View 10p".\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120212.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157870				0	he	Combine with -				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120212.xhp	0	help	par_id3145825				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_CHECKBOX_TP_TOX_SELECT_CB_USE_DASH\"\>Replaces identical index entries that occur on consecutive pages with a single entry and the page range where the entry occurs. For example, the entries "View 10, View 11, View 12" are combined as "View 10-12".\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120212.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154502				0	he	Case sensitive				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120212.xhp	0	help	par_id3149880				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_CHECKBOX_TP_TOX_SELECT_CB_CASESENSITIVE\"\>Distinguishes between uppercase and lowercase letters in identical index entries. For Asian languages special handling applies.\</ahelp\> If you want the first occurrence of the entry in the document to determine the case of the entry, select \<emph\>Combine identical entries\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120212.xhp	0	help	par_idN10671				0	he	To use multi-level collation to Asian languages, select \<emph\>Case sensitive\</emph\>. In the multi-level collation, the cases and diacritics of the entries are ignored and only the primitive forms of the entries are compared. If the forms are identical, the diacritics of the forms are compared. If the forms are still identical, the cases of the forms as well as the widths of the characters, and the differences in the Japanese Kana are compared.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120212.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150569				0	he	AutoCapitalize entries				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120212.xhp	0	help	par_id3148772				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_CHECKBOX_TP_TOX_SELECT_CB_INITIALCAPS\"\>Automatically capitalizes the first letter of an index entry.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120212.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155986				0	he	Keys as separate entries				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120212.xhp	0	help	par_id3147170				0	he	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_CHECKBOX_TP_TOX_SELECT_CB_KEYASENTRY\"\>Inserts index keys as separate index entries.\</ahelp\> A key is inserted as a top level index entry and the entries that are assigned to the key as indented subentries.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120212.xhp	0	help	par_id3151184				0	he	To define an index key, choose \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04120100.xhp\" name=\"Insert Index Entry\"\>\<emph\>Insert Index Entry\</emph\>\</link\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
