helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150114				0	he	Displays formatting styles for text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150700				0	he	Chapter Styles				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147412				0	he	Displays formatting styles for headings.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147500				0	he	List Styles				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149568				0	he	Displays formatting styles for numbered or bulleted lists.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145263				0	he	Index Styles				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155975				0	he	Displays formatting styles for indexes.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149213				0	he	Special Region Styles				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147736				0	he	Displays formatting styles for headers, footers, footnotes, endnotes, tables, and captions.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146339				0	he	HTML Styles				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149845				0	he	Displays a list of styles for HTML documents.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155560				0	he	Conditional Styles				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154774				0	he	Displays the user-defined conditional styles.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151090				0	he	Hierarchical				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148448				0	he	Displays the styles in the selected category in a hierarchical list. To view the styles in a sublevel, click on the plus sign (+) next to the sublevel name.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155580				0	he	Template Management				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145622				0	he	Use the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01110100.xhp\" name=\"Template Management\"\>\<emph\>Template Management\</emph\>\</link\> dialog to copy styles from one document to another.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	he	While  Typing				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147436	1			0	he	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05150100.xhp\" name=\"While  Typing\"\>While Typing\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154017	2			0	he	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:OnlineAutoFormat\"\>Automatically formats the document while you type. To set the formatting options, choose \<emph\>Tools - AutoCorrect\</emph\>\<emph\> Options\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Options \</emph\>tab.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148488				0	he	You can use AutoCorrect to format text documents and plain ASCII text files, but not characters that you have manually formatted. Automatic \<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040100.xhp\" name=\"word completion\"\>word completion\</link\> only occurs after you type a word for the second time in a document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147407				0	he	To reverse the last AutoCorrect action, choose \<emph\>Edit - \</emph\>\<link href=\"text/shared/01/02010000.xhp\" name=\"Undo\"\>\<emph\>Undo\</emph\>\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150536				0	he	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05150200.xhp\" name=\"Other AutoFormat rules\"\>Other AutoCorrect rules\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
