helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145246				0	he	\<variable id=\"kapnum\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ChapterNumberingDialog\"\>Specifies the number format and the hierarchy for chapter numbering in the current document.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150934				0	he	Outline numbering is linked to paragraph styles. By default, the "Heading" paragraph styles (1-10) are assigned to the corresponding outline number levels (1-10). If you want, you can assign different paragraph styles to the outline number level.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	par_id8237250				0	he	If you want numbered headings, use the \<emph\>Tools - Outline Numbering\</emph\> menu command to assign numbering to a paragraph style. Do not use the Numbering icon on the Formatting toolbar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147567	55			0	he	To highlight the screen display of outline numbers, choose \<emph\>View -\</emph\>\<emph\>Field Shadings\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
